The braid diagram records a positive crossing of strand 1 past the two-strand block $(2,3)$: the lower labels are the strand labels, height increases upward, and each bold right-bottom branch is the overstrand. The crossings occur in the order $(1,2)$ then $(1,3)$; the proof justifies the corresponding path homotopy independently of the drawing.

