        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-finite-measure-uniqueness-on-a-pi-system",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal P$ be a pi-system on $X$ and let $\\mathcal A=\\sigma_X(\\mathcal P)$. If finite measures $\\mu$ and $\\nu$ on $(X,\\mathcal A)$ agree on $\\mathcal P$ and satisfy $\\mu(X)=\\nu(X)$, then $\\mu=\\nu$ on $\\mathcal A$.\n\nThe total-mass equality is separate because this library's pi-system convention does not require $X\\in\\mathcal P$.",
