        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ip-q2-ellipsoid-extremal-profile-is-minimizer",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the minimax detection-risk definition, $q=2$, and positive nondecreasing sequences $a_j$ and $\\sigma_j$ with $a_j\\to\\infty$. Let $A,z_0>0$ and suppose $S=\\{j:Aa_j^2<1\\}$ is finite and nonempty. Define $\\widetilde\\eta_j^2=z_0^2\\sigma_j^2(1-Aa_j^2)_+$ and assume\n$$\\sum_{j\\ge1}\\sigma_j^2\\widetilde\\eta_j^2=r^2,\\qquad \\sum_{j\\ge1}a_j^2\\sigma_j^2\\widetilde\\eta_j^2=1.$$\nThen $\\widetilde\\eta\\in\\Theta_2(r)$ and minimizes $\\sum_{j\\ge1}\\eta_j^4$ over $\\Theta_2(r)$; the nonnegative minimizer is unique.",
          "uses": [
