        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-ip-gaussian-product-mixture-testing-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. In the Gaussian sequence detection experiment, let $v\\in\\Theta_q(r)$ have finite support $J$ and put\n$$u(v)^2=\\frac{1}{2\\varepsilon^4}\\sum_{j\\in J}v_j^4.$$\nLet $\\pi_v$ be the uniform probability law on the finite family of mean sequences whose $j$th coordinate is independently $+v_j$ or $-v_j$ for $j\\in J$ and is zero off $J$, and let $P_{\\pi_v}$ be the corresponding mixture sampling law. Then its likelihood ratio with respect to the null law is\n$$L_v=\\frac{dP_{\\pi_v}}{dP_{\\varepsilon,0}}=\\prod_{j\\in J}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{v_j^2}{2\\varepsilon^2}\\right)\\cosh\\!\\left(\\frac{v_jY_j}{\\varepsilon^2}\\right),$$\nit satisfies\n$$\\mathbb E_{\\varepsilon,0}L_v^2=\\prod_{j\\in J}\\cosh\\!\\left(\\frac{v_j^2}{\\varepsilon^2}\\right),\\qquad \\mathbb E_{\\varepsilon,0}(L_v-1)^2\\le \\exp(u(v)^2)-1,$$\nand the minimax risks obey\n$$\\gamma_\\varepsilon(\\Theta_q(r))\\ge1-\\frac12\\sqrt{\\exp(u(v)^2)-1},\\qquad \\beta_\\varepsilon(\\Theta_q(r),\\alpha)\\ge1-\\alpha-\\frac12\\sqrt{\\exp(u(v)^2)-1}$$\nfor every $\\alpha\\in(0,1)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
