        {
          "id": "derive-2.1",
          "claim": "For any $\\eta\\in\\Theta_2(r_\\varepsilon)$, put $x_j=\\eta_j^2$ and $\\widetilde x_j=\\widetilde\\eta_j^2$. Since $1-Aa_j^2\\le0$ off the profile support, $$\\sum_j\\widetilde x_jx_j=z_0^2\\sum_{j\\in S}\\sigma_j^2(1-Aa_j^2)x_j\\ge z_0^2(r_\\varepsilon^2-A)=\\sum_j\\widetilde x_j^2,$$ where the inequality follows from $\\sum_j\\sigma_j^2x_j\\ge r_\\varepsilon^2$ and $\\sum_ja_j^2\\sigma_j^2x_j\\le1$. Thus $$m_\\eta\\ge\\frac{\\sum_j\\widetilde\\eta_j^4}{\\varepsilon^2\\sqrt{2\\sum_j\\widetilde\\eta_j^4}}=u_\\varepsilon.$$",
          "step": "2.1",
