          "claim": "In the degenerate branch, with the notation of step 2.4, for the matching degenerate lower bound first take $D_\\varepsilon\\to d\\in\\mathbb R$. Put $M=\\lfloor n/(\\log n)^2\\rfloor$, $I=\\{\\lfloor n\\rfloor-M+1,\\ldots,\\lfloor n\\rfloor\\}$, and mix uniformly over indices $i\\in I$ and signs with $\\eta_i=\\pm r i^{-\\beta}$, all other coordinates zero. Every point has energy $r^2$ and budget $(ri^\\alpha)^q\\le1$. Write $T=\\sqrt{2\\log M}$ and $\\mu_i=r/(\\varepsilon i^\\beta)$; uniformly on $I$, $\\mu_i=T+d+o(1)$ since $M/n=O((\\log n)^{-2})$ and $T-\\sqrt{2\\log n}\\to0$. The null likelihood from step 1.1 is $L=M^{-1}\\sum_{i\\in I}e^{-\\mu_i^2/2}\\cosh(\\mu_iG_i)$. Truncate each summand to $|G_i|\\le T$, obtaining $\\widetilde L$. Completing the square gives its summand mean $\\Phi(T-\\mu_i)-\\Phi(-T-\\mu_i)\\to c=\\Phi(-d)$ and its second moment at most $\\tfrac12e^{\\mu_i^2}\\Phi(T-2\\mu_i)+\\tfrac12e^{-\\mu_i^2}$. The upper Mills bound and $$\\mu_i^2-\\tfrac12(2\\mu_i-T)^2-\\log M=-(\\mu_i-T)^2$$ bound this second moment divided by $M$ by $O(1/T)$. Independence gives $\\operatorname{Var}\\widetilde L=O(1/T)\\to0$, and $\\mathbb P_0(L\\ne\\widetilde L)\\le2M\\overline\\Phi(T)=O(1/T)\\to0$. Thus $\\mathbb E_0|\\widetilde L-c|\\to0$ and $L\\to c$ in null probability. Since $L\\ge\\widetilde L$, every size-$\\ell$ test has mixture type-II error at least $c(1-\\ell)-\\mathbb E|\\widetilde L-c|$; every total error is at least $\\mathbb E\\min(1,L)\\to c$. Bounded convergence in probability here follows directly by splitting at any fixed positive deviation; no likelihood uniform integrability is asserted. This proves both lower bounds for finite $d$.",
