          "claim": "In the ordered basis of [F1], direct subtraction gives $e:=A(c_{V,V}-AI)=\\begin{pmatrix}0&0&0&0\\\\0&-A^2&1&0\\\\0&1&-A^{-2}&0\\\\0&0&0&0\\end{pmatrix}$. Writing $U(1)=-A^2v_+\\otimes v_-+v_-\\otimes v_+$ and $B(v_+\\otimes v_-)=1$, $B(v_-\\otimes v_+)=-A^{-2}$ shows entrywise that $e=UB$. Hence $B(U(1))=-A^2-A^{-2}=\\delta$ and $e^2=\\delta e$. The explicit snake equalities in [F2] give the adjacent tensor relations: $e_{12}e_{23}e_{12}=UB\\otimes1$ because the middle composites $(1\\otimes B)(U\\otimes1)$ and then $(B\\otimes1)(1\\otimes U)$ are identities; the reversed calculation gives $e_{23}e_{12}e_{23}=e_{23}$. Distant placements commute because they act on disjoint tensor factors.",
