          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $k$ be a field and let $\\mathcal C$ be a $k$-linear ribbon category with $k$-bilinear tensor product and $\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathcal C}(\\mathbf1)=k$. Let $X$ be absolutely simple, so its twist is $\\theta_X=\\lambda\\operatorname{id}_X$ for a unique $\\lambda\\in k^\\times$. For $n\\ge1$ and $\\beta\\in B_n$, let $t_n(\\beta)$ be the value of the blackboard-framed $X$-colored closure and let $w(\\beta)$ be the exponent sum, with positive Artin generator and positive stabilization conventions fixed as in the supplied ribbon-trace formulas. Then\n$$J_X(\\widehat\\beta):=\\lambda^{-w(\\beta)}t_n(\\beta)$$\ndepends only on the oriented unframed link type of $\\widehat\\beta$ when every component has color $X$. This statement makes no normalization by the categorical dimension.",
