      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1.1",
          "claim": "The portion of $\\partial X$ added by deleting $\\nu(D)$ is the normal-circle bundle $D^2\\times S^1$, and it meets $E_K$ in $S^1\\times S^1$. By excision [F2], the relative pair $(B^4,X)$ has the homology of $(D^2\\times D^2,D^2\\times S^1)$. The latter solid-torus subspace has $H_1\\cong\\mathbb Z$ generated by a normal circle and $H_2=0$, while $D^2\\times D^2$ is contractible by [F3]. Its pair sequence [F2] therefore identifies $H_2(B^4,X;\\mathbb Z)$ with $\\mathbb Z$, generated by a normal disk whose boundary is that normal circle.",
