          "source": "lem-lee-cobordism-filtration-genus-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $S\\subset S^3\\times[0,1]$ be a connected compact oriented smoothly properly embedded surface of genus $g$, with product collars and oriented boundary $(-K_0\\times\\{0\\})\\sqcup(K_1\\times\\{1\\})$ for oriented knots $K_0,K_1$ in the standard three-sphere. A **finite movie** for $S$ is a finite ordered sequence of regular-level link diagrams whose changes are planar isotopies, oriented Reidemeister moves, births, saddles or deaths. Such a movie defines a map on rational Lee homology that preserves the induced decreasing filtration with degree $\\chi(S)=-2g$. The map is an isomorphism; consequently\n$$\n|s(K_1)-s(K_0)|\\le 2g.\n$$",
