        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-tait-graph-of-a-link-diagram",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a link projection on $S^2$, a **checkerboard coloring** assigns one of two colors to each complementary region so that regions sharing an edge have different colors. Given such a coloring, the **black Tait graph** has one vertex for each black region and one edge for each crossing joining the two opposite black sectors at that crossing. The **white Tait graph** is defined by interchanging black and white. Loops and parallel edges are allowed.",
