        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-euler-formula-for-connected-plane-graphs",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "If a connected plane graph has vertex, edge and face sets $V,E,F$ ([[def-plane-graph-face-and-boundary]]), then\n\n$$|V|-|E|+|F|=2.$$\n\nDeletion is as in [[def-graph-deletion-contraction-minor-and-subdivision]], the tree boundary case uses [[prop-plane-forest-has-one-face]], and the finite induction is [[thm-induction-principle]].",
