      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $\\mu$ be the number of components represented by $D$. By [F8],\n$$(-A^3)^{-\\operatorname{wr}(D)}\\langle D\\rangle\\big|_{A=1}=(-2)^{\\mu-1}\\ne0.$$\nThe writhe-normalizing factor is a Laurent monomial and hence a unit, so $\\langle D\\rangle$ is nonzero and its span is defined. Now let $s_A$ and $s_B$ be the numbers of circles in the all-$A$ and all-$B$ states. If a state has $j$ $B$-smoothings, then its weight factor is $A^{c-2j}$. A single smoothing change is a band surgery and changes the circle count by exactly $1$ or $-1$, so a state with $k$ circles has $k\\le s_A+j$. Since the highest degree of $\\delta^{k-1}$ is $2(k-1)$, every state term has degree at most $c-2j+2(k-1)\\le c+2(s_A-1)$. Reversing $A$ and $B$ gives minimum degree at least $-c-2(s_B-1)$. Hence $\\operatorname{span}_A\\langle D\\rangle\\le2c+2(s_A+s_B-2)$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
