          "claim": "For the closure of $\\sigma_1^3$, the endpoint permutation is the transposition of the two strands, hence one cycle by [F4]. The three positive crossings form a connected projection. Starting on the left bottom strand, the successive crossing visits are under, over, under; after closure the right bottom strand visits over, under, over. Thus the diagram is alternating. Its black Tait graph has two vertices and three parallel edges, while the white dual graph is a triangle. Both graphs have no loops, so no crossing repeats a region on its boundary; the diagram is reduced by [F6].",
