          "claim": "For the four-level braid with levels $\\sigma_2^{-1},\\sigma_1,\\sigma_2^{-1},\\sigma_1$, the successive endpoint orders are $[1,3,2]$, $[3,1,2]$, $[3,2,1]$, and $[2,3,1]$. The resulting endpoint permutation is the cycle $1\\mapsto3\\mapsto2\\mapsto1$, so the closure is one knot component by [F4]. Traversing it from the first bottom strand gives crossing visits under, over; from the third bottom strand gives under, over, under; and from the second gives over, under, over. The full cyclic sequence alternates. The black Tait graph is the theta graph with two parallel edges between $u,v$ and a two-edge path $u-w-v$; it has no loops or bridges. Its dual has no loops because the primal has no bridges. Thus both color pairs at every crossing are distinct and the diagram is reduced by [F6].",
