          "claim": "For any second lift $P_1$, define $L(P_0,P_1)_x$ to be the set of Spin$^c$-equivariant maps from $(P_0)_x$ to $(P_1)_x$ covering the identity map of the common oriented frame fiber. Since both are lifts of that same frame fiber, two such maps differ by a unique element of the central kernel $U(1)$ from [F1]. In local lift trivializations, the transition functions of $P_0$ and $P_1$ project to the same $\\mathrm{SO}(n)$ functions, so their pointwise quotient lies in central $U(1)$; the cocycle identity for each lift makes these quotients a $U(1)$-valued cocycle. Thus the difference fibers form a principal $U(1)$-bundle $L(P_0,P_1)$ over $X$.",
