          "quote": "For every closed connected oriented rational homology three-sphere $Y$ and Spin$^c$ structure $\\mathfrak t$, the absolutely graded infinity group $HF^\\infty(Y,\\mathfrak t;\\mathbb F_2)$ is a single free Laurent tower. If $W:Y_0\\to Y_1$ is a smooth connected rational homology cobordism between rational homology spheres, then for each fixed Spin$^c$ structure $\\mathfrak s$ on $W$ the infinity map is a degree-zero isomorphism. The corresponding plus map commutes with the infinity-to-plus maps. This conclusion concerns each individual extending Spin$^c$ structure, including nonprimitive handle attachments and torsion labels.",
