          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The minus chain complex is finite free over $\\mathbb F_2[U]$, with generators $[\\mathbf x,-1]$ for the finitely many intersection points in $\\mathfrak t$. Its homology is finitely generated and its localization is the infinity homology, since localization is exact and the localized differentials are identical. Thus the graded image $L$ of $HF^-\\to R\\rho$ is nonzero. Its degrees are bounded above by the largest degree of a minus-chain generator. The set of integers $j$ with $U^j\\rho\\in L$ is consequently nonempty, bounded below, and closed under addition of nonnegative integers. If $a$ is its minimum, that set is exactly $\\{a,a+1,\\ldots\\}$. Every homogeneous element of the Laurent tower is a monomial multiple of $\\rho$, and the image is graded; hence $L=U^a\\mathbb F_2[U]\\rho$.",
