          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For the negative-trace map from $S^3$ to $-L(p,1)$, the fixed triangle has index and basepoint multiplicity zero and count one. It sends the sphere generator at exponent zero to $[x_i,0]$. The four-dimensional data are $c_1^2=-k^2/p$, $\\chi=1$ and $\\sigma=-1$. Hence its degree is $D_i=(1-k^2/p)/4$, and $d(-L(p,1),i)=D_i$. This computes the negative orientation directly.",
