          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $B$ be a compact connected oriented smooth four-manifold with $H_*(B;\\mathbb Q)\\cong H_*(\\mathrm{point};\\mathbb Q)$ and connected rational homology sphere boundary $Y$. Choose a smoothly embedded closed four-ball $D$ in its interior and put $W=B\\setminus\\operatorname{int}D$. With the induced orientation,\n$$\\partial W=-S^3\\sqcup Y.$$\nThe manifold $W$ is connected, $H_j(W;\\mathbb Q)$ is $\\mathbb Q$ for $j=0,3$ and zero otherwise, and both inclusions $S^3\\to W$, $Y\\to W$ induce isomorphisms on rational homology in every degree. Its rational homological Euler characteristic is zero and its rational intersection module $H_2(W;\\mathbb Q)$ is zero. Consequently its signature is zero, and the square of every covector with respect to that zero intersection module is zero. These assertions hold also for the reversed cobordism $-W$ from $Y$ to $S^3$, and use no choice principle.\n\nThe last square assertion refers to the intersection-form covector convention; the lemma supplies no Floer cobordism map, absolute grading formula, or Spin-c existence theorem.",
