          "claim": "Twist the actual module of step1.1 by $G$, with the product connection. On its local multiplicity factor the curvature is $F^{V_0/S}\\otimes I+I\\otimes F_G$, and the two factors commute. The finite exponential and tensor-trace identities therefore give $\\operatorname{ch}((V_0\\otimes G)/S)=\\Theta\\operatorname{ch}(G)$. The identities are invariant under the local multiplicity transitions in [F1], so they are global form identities, requiring no Spin structure. Applying the actual analytic index theorem to the twisted and untwisted modules yields $\\operatorname{ind}_{\\mathbb C}\\widetilde D_A=3\\operatorname{ind}_{\\mathbb C}\\widetilde D_0-4\\int_X\\widehat A_0\\Theta_0c_2(E)$. Here $\\widetilde D_A=d_A^*\\oplus\\sqrt2d_A^-$, $\\widehat A_0=1$, and $\\Theta_0=2$ by step2.1. Using [F3] to evaluate the Chern form gives $\\operatorname{ind}_{\\mathbb C}\\widetilde D_A=3(b_1-1-b_-)-8\\langle c_2(P),[X]\\rangle$. No assertion that $d_A^2=0$ was used: the Clifford operator and its index calculation apply to every smooth connection.",
