        {
          "id": "step-2-2",
          "claim": "**The charge of the constructed bundle.** The bundle $P'$ and its transition map in step 1.1 are fixed as $\\lambda$ varies. Its Chern–Weil integral is consequently an integer independent of $\\lambda$. On the fixed inner ball, the explicit Euclidean self-dual BPST integral tends to $-1$ in the convention $c_2=(8\\pi^2)^{-1}\\operatorname{tr}(F\\wedge F)$. On the cutoff annulus its curvature is $O_\\rho(\\lambda^2)$, so its Chern integral tends to zero. The integral is metric independent. Hence $c_2(P')[X]=-1$ exactly. This computes the charge of the actual fixed bundle used by the contraction, not merely that of an abstract model.",
