          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $X$ be a closed oriented Riemannian four-manifold, let $P$ be a fixed principal $SU(2)$-bundle with charge $k=-\\langle c_2(P),[X]\\rangle$, and let $(A_j)$ be smooth connections satisfying $F_{A_j}^-=0$ and $\\sup_j\\int_X|F_{A_j}|^2\\,d\\mathrm{vol}<\\infty$. Then a subsequence, bundle isomorphisms, and a finite set $S\\subset X$ exist such that the transported connections converge in local Sobolev gauge on compact subsets of $X\\setminus S$ to a self-dual connection on a possibly lower-charge bundle of charge $k_\\infty$. For each $p\\in S$ there is a positive integer bubble charge $m_p$, and $k=k_\\infty+\\sum_{p\\in S}m_p$. The limiting connection extends smoothly across every puncture after gauge transformation, and the compactified moduli space is obtained by adjoining the lower-charge limits together with the finite bubble points and their integer charge labels.",
