          "source": "thm-taubes-small-instanton-gluing-and-compactified-end",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $X$ be a closed connected simply connected oriented smooth Riemannian four-manifold with positive-definite intersection form, and fix a smooth $SU(2)$ bundle $P$ with $c_2(P)[X]=-1$. The unperturbed self-dual moduli space has a neighborhood of its ideal stratum consisting precisely of the flat connection and one charge-one point, and this neighborhood, including the ideal stratum, is diffeomorphic in its interior and homeomorphic up to that stratum to $X\\times[0,\\lambda_0)$. Its interior consists of irreducible regular solutions. The parameter on the second factor is a smooth positive concentration scale tending to zero at the ideal stratum. Every sufficiently concentrating solution occurs, and occurs once. In particular this is a complete end theorem, not merely existence of a five-parameter family. It does not assert that arbitrary perturbations preserve this end.",
