          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "**Prepare precisely the actual reducibles.** Apply [F2] to their finite set and choose disjoint bounded invariant slice neighborhoods. Its constructed smoothing section $\\sigma_r$ is supported in their union and vanishes at the central reducible points. On smaller neighborhoods its zeros are equivariant smooth graphs over $\\mathbb C^3$; the punctured quotients are smooth oriented five-manifolds, and cutting their graph-radius gives projective links. There are no additional reducible solutions inside these slice neighborhoods: the stabilizer of a nearby orbit is a subgroup of the center's circle by the local slice construction; a reducible orbit must therefore be fixed by that circle. On its fixed diagonal subspace the equivariant off-diagonal perturbation is zero. The diagonal equation is the abelian self-dual equation, whose only local slice solution is the center because its $H^1$ is zero. Outside these neighborhoods the equation remains unperturbed, so [F2] lists all remaining reducibles. The construction is bounded and smooth into $H^3$ in these finitely many slices.",
