        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-seifert-van-kampen",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X=U\\cup V$, where $U$ and $V$ are open path-connected subsets of $X$, let $U\\cap V$ be path-connected, and fix $x_0\\in U\\cap V$. For the inclusion-induced maps in the diagram\n\n$$\\pi_1(U,x_0)\\longleftarrow\\pi_1(U\\cap V,x_0)\\longrightarrow\\pi_1(V,x_0),$$\n\nthe group $\\pi_1(X,x_0)$, together with the two inclusion-induced homomorphisms, is a pushout ([[def-pushout-of-group-homomorphisms]]). Equivalently, the canonical homomorphism from any pushout $P$ of the displayed diagram to $\\pi_1(X,x_0)$ is an isomorphism. No injectivity of either map from the overlap group is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-mayer-vietoris-sequence-in-singular-homology",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For an open cover $X=U\\cup V$, the sequence\n$$\\cdots\\to H_n(U\\cap V;G)\\to H_n(U;G)\\oplus H_n(V;G)\\to H_n(X;G)\\xrightarrow{\\delta}H_{n-1}(U\\cap V;G)\\to\\cdots$$\nis exact, with middle map $(u,v)\\mapsto u+v$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-collar-neighborhood-theorem",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Every smooth manifold with boundary has a smooth collar.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "lem-rationalization-is-exact-and-commutes-with-singular-homology",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. For every abelian group A, A⊗_Z Q is its positive-integer localization: every element is a/s and a/s=0 iff a is killed by some positive integer. Thus A⊗Q=0 iff A is torsion. Rationalization is exact and commutes with direct sums. Naturally for every space Y, H_j(Y;Z)⊗Q≅H_j(Y;Q); for every rational vector space V, H_j(Y;V)≅H_j(Y;Q)⊗_Q V.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "By [F3], $D$ is a smooth proper slice disk; [F1] and [F2] then give a compact rational homology four-ball $B_D$ with boundary $M=\\Sigma_2(K)$. The boundary identification in the statement permits the smooth oriented gluing $X=W\\cup_M(-B_D)$; collars [F7] give a smooth closed oriented four-manifold.",
