        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-grid-alexander-grading-integral",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $G$ be a toroidal grid of grid number $n$ representing one oriented knot, and let $M_{\\mathbb O}$, $M_{\\mathbb X}$, and $A_G$ be the functions defined from its finite point sets and the pair-counting function $J$. Then $M_{\\mathbb O}$ and $M_{\\mathbb X}$ are integer-valued, and every rectangle $r$ from a grid state $\\mathbf x$ to a grid state $\\mathbf y$ satisfies $M_{\\mathbb O}(\\mathbf x)-M_{\\mathbb O}(\\mathbf y)=1-2n_{\\mathbb O}(r)+2\\#(\\mathbf x\\cap\\operatorname{Int}r)$ and $M_{\\mathbb X}(\\mathbf x)-M_{\\mathbb X}(\\mathbf y)=1-2n_{\\mathbb X}(r)+2\\#(\\mathbf x\\cap\\operatorname{Int}r)$. Consequently $A_G$ is integer-valued and $A_G(\\mathbf x)-A_G(\\mathbf y)=n_{\\mathbb X}(r)-n_{\\mathbb O}(r)$.",
