          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The sum defining $H_\\ell$ is finite because there are finitely many states and at most two torus rectangles for each ordered state pair. It is $\\mathbb F_2[U_1,\\ldots,U_n]$-linear by its coefficient formula. For each counted rectangle $r$, [F4] gives $M(\\mathbf x)-M(\\mathbf y)=1-2n_{\\mathbb O}(r)$; the coefficient has Maslov degree $-2n_{\\mathbb O}(r)$ by [F2]. Therefore each term of $H_\\ell(\\mathbf x)$ has Maslov degree $M(\\mathbf x)-1$. Also [F4] gives $A(\\mathbf y)-n_{\\mathbb O}(r)=A(\\mathbf x)-n_{\\mathbb X}(r)$, and $X_\\ell\\in\\operatorname{Int}(r)$ implies $n_{\\mathbb X}(r)\\ge1$. Thus $H_\\ell$ does not raise the Alexander filtration.",
