          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "By [F2] choose a finite sequence of planar isotopies and oriented Reidemeister moves from $D_0$ to $D_1$. Compose successive planar isotopies, and regard each remaining Reidemeister move as an edge between its two decorated planar-isotopy classes. The sequence now traverses finitely many such classes, with the first and last represented by $D_0,D_1$. If there is no Reidemeister edge, these two diagrams are planar isotopic. Otherwise each intermediate class is incident to a Reidemeister edge and has a bridge representative by [F4]. Choose one bridge representative for each occurrence of a class in this finite sequence, keeping $D_0,D_1$ at its ends, and choose a bridge rectification there. The choices are finite; no stronger choice principle is invoked.",
