          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-grid-destabilization-filtered-equivalence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For a southwest $X$ stabilization, the incoming-domain map from the full filtered grid complex to the cone of $U_1+U_2$ on the polynomial extension of the smaller grid complex is a filtered chain homotopy equivalence over the full polynomial ring. Its inverse and both inverse homotopies can be computed by finite polynomial matrix formulas from empty rectangles and incoming domains. Composing with the explicit cone retraction gives filtered equivalence with the smaller complex over any retained old variable action, without imposing relations on its other variables. After simultaneous ordinary collapse of the marking variables, stabilization contributes the zero-differential factor $V$ of bidegrees $(0,0)$ and $(-1,-1)$. The same $V$ factor occurs on tilde homology.",
