          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $C$ be the full filtered complex of a knot grid with independent marking variables. The same underlying complex, regarded as a module over $\\mathbb F_2[U]$ with $U$ acting as $U_i$, has filtered chain homotopy type independent of $i$. This assertion concerns restriction of scalars; no marking variables are identified or set to zero. For consecutive markings the equivalence and its inverse homotopies are explicit polynomial divided-difference formulas and finite weighted rectangle counts.",
