          "quote": "Let $K\\subset S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot and let $C(K)=\\mathrm{CFK}^{\\infty}(K)$ be its normalized bifiltered complex over $\\mathbb F_2[U,U^{-1}]$. The complex of the reverse mirror $-K$ is filtered-chain-homotopy equivalent to the dual complex $C(K)^*=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb F_2[U,U^{-1}]}(C(K),\\mathbb F_2[U,U^{-1}])$, with dual differential $d\\phi(x)=\\phi(\\partial x)$ and dual basis elements at negated bifiltration coordinates. There is also a Maslov-graded filtered-chain-homotopy equivalence from $C(K)$ to the complex obtained by exchanging the algebraic and Alexander filtrations. These are distinct symmetries: duality negates both filtration coordinates, while conjugation exchanges them.",
