          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Give a complete oriented Heegaard splitting $Y=U_\\alpha\\cup_\\Sigma U_\\beta$ of a closed connected smooth three-manifold, with actual disjoint compression disks cutting each handlebody into a ball. Then $TY$ has a Spin structure, constructed by finite handle and boundary-lift operations. Its induced Spin-c structure has trivial determinant line and hence first Chern class zero. In particular its Chern class evaluates to zero on every capped periodic domain, whether or not that sector has a generator in the given diagram.\n\nConsequently the following two full-diagram conditions are equivalent: every nonzero normalized integral periodic domain has both signs; and for EVERY Spin-c structure $\\mathfrak s$ on Y, including those with no diagram generators, every such domain with $\\langle c_1(\\mathfrak s),H(P)\\rangle=0$ has both signs. This equivalence does not identify either condition with a test only at existing generators. For ONE specified sector, ordinary weak admissibility remains a separate condition.",
