          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Suppose two complete globally weak pointed Heegaard diagrams for any closed connected oriented smooth three-manifold differ by a supplied attaching-circle isotopy avoiding the basepoint and the other circles of its own family. Their actual chosen hat complexes, with the auxiliary choices described below, have actual finite chain maps and inverse chain homotopies. The construction uses diagram transport on regular intervals and genuine triangle maps at finitely many births and deaths. The local inverse at a birth is an explicit unit-pair cancellation map composed with a finite action-triangular inverse. It does not assume that birth cancellation preserves counts or that arbitrary intermediate diagrams are admissible.\n\nOne fixed finite winding preparation makes the whole central isotopy globally weak. The preparation and its removal are themselves globally weak isotopies. All finite analytic comparisons are performed using the stated continuation suppliers and consistently retained actual generator charts. This proves the attaching-circle isotopy operation between globally weak hat diagrams for general Y, including both attaching families. It does not prove the sector-only input comparison, positive-basepoint minus invariance, absolute grading or naturality.",
