          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\mathcal H=(\\Sigma,\\alpha,\\beta,z)$ be a complete globally weakly admissible pointed Heegaard diagram for ANY closed connected oriented smooth three-manifold. Choose actual zero-basepoint regular data defining a finite chosen hat complex, with a fixed surface complex structure and area form and with $J_t=\\operatorname{Sym}^g(j)$ on a neighborhood of the diagonal and each chosen region-point divisor. The path has genuine physical-time collars. Such data exist by the globally weak chosen-complex theorem.\n\nThere is an ordinary genus-one Heegaard stabilization in a disk in the $z$-region, disjoint from $z$ and all curves, together with actual allowed time-collar data on the stabilized diagram, for which every zero-basepoint holomorphic strip is EXACTLY an old strip times the unique new intersection point $c$. The stabilized diagram is globally weakly admissible. The actual linearization splits as the old linearization plus a bounded invertible real strip operator. Thus this bijection preserves actual indices, regularity, finite rigid counts and translation quotients.\n\nThe generator maps\n$$I(x)=x\\times c,\\qquad P(x\\times c)=x$$\nare actual inverse chain isomorphisms of the hat complexes. In particular $PI=\\mathrm{Id}$ and $IP=\\mathrm{Id}$; their inverse chain homotopies can be taken to be zero. Destabilization uses P. This is a geometric stabilization move map for these actual chosen diagrams, not merely an auxiliary almost-complex comparison.\n\nThe target disk is chosen inside a neighborhood on whose ENTIRE point-divisor family the old structure is standard; the proof supplies a smooth global stabilized structure with holomorphic normal coordinates for every divisor over a separating circle. It does not assume that an arbitrary extension has that property or invoke an unproved target-degeneration compactness theorem. This is the general closed-manifold hat operation; positive-basepoint minus/infinity stabilization, arbitrary attaching-circle isotopy or handleslide maps and absolute gradings are not asserted here. Genus zero is included.",
