          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Fix a complete globally weak pointed Heegaard diagram, its surface complex structure j and positive area form, and its smooth symmetric-product target. Let $J^-_t,J^+_t$ be two allowed generic hat paths for that fixed background, tame for this same form off their protected symmetric neighborhoods, with actual time-constant endpoint collars. Their nonconstant zero-basepoint strips are regular at all actual indices. Their product-integrable generator normal forms, if supplied, need not agree; no such normal form is required at either endpoint. Full tensor values on the two boundary tori may also differ.\n\nThere are actual finite zero-basepoint anchored continuation chain maps between their hat complexes and actual finite inverse chain homotopies. The coefficient profile is compactly source-dependent and stationary at its two source ends. Generic relative one-parameter profiles give the actual chain homotopies, and separated-transition gluing gives actual composition. No quotient by translation is taken on an anchored central solution. The constant-profile continuation counts the identity.\n\nThis removes the shared-generator prescription from the fixed-background comparison, including optional generator charts and arbitrary transverse complex angles. It is not an independence assertion outside the stated common-background and generic endpoint hypotheses. Rank zero has the direct point-target comparison.",
