          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Fix actual nearly symmetric polygon data with common exact transverse generator charts and smooth source/target coefficient bounds. In each matching chart the boundary planes are $\\mathbb R^m$ and $\\prod_j e^{i\\theta_j}\\mathbb R$, with $0<\\theta_j<\\pi$; set $g$ to the positive finite minimum of $\\theta_j$ and $\\pi-\\theta_j$ over the matching ends. Decay exponents and any weights are chosen below $g$, not below an assumed right angle. Consider either two regular polygon components joined at a transverse matching corner, or one regular polygon component and one regular nonconstant strip joined at an external corner. Include the components' actual conformal parameters in their derivatives, and quotient the strip component by its actual translation. Suppose the component count dimensions are zero. Fix representatives, using a smooth compact-source phase for the strip.\n\nSuppose the actual coefficient data on the sewn sources agree asymptotically with the component data in their finite-tree neck charts as follows: on each fixed component core their difference and all required derivatives are $O(e^{-cT})$; they have uniform smooth bounds on the neck; and they are EXACTLY the common product structure wherever a map value is in the matching generator chart. The same estimates hold after differentiating in $T$. For polygon–polygon sewing $T$ is its actual new conformal neck parameter. For strip–polygon sewing it is the strip core's longitudinal position relative to the polygon core; the polygon has no translation quotient.\n\nFor all large $T$ there is a regular corrected polygon, and modulo the stated component phases these polygons form an injective half-open collar. Their index and count dimension are the actual sums: the glued count dimension is one. Every sequence converging to this unbubbled two-component breaking, with the actual strong compact convergence and no-neck convergence, is eventually in this collar. Kernel matching and bounded right inverses are proved below; they are not extra hypotheses. The collar is smooth for finite $T$ in the solution charts, and is a topological half-interval after adding its broken endpoint. No differentiability in a prescribed compactifying parameter at the endpoint is asserted.\n\nMore generally, for any fixed finite unbubbled tree of regular polygon and nonconstant strip components, the construction gives actual local product charts with the component solution coordinates and one positive gluing coordinate for each node. Their dimension is the sum of the component count dimensions plus the number of nodes. These charts exhaust every sequence with that component limit and strong compact and no-neck convergence. The constants may depend on that fixed component tree and small component charts. The assertion supplies neither a uniform inverse across unrelated components nor regularity of an arbitrary limiting component.",
