          "claim": "By [F1], the smoothing gives finitely many disjoint embedded circles in the projection sphere. Choose a point $q$ outside them. By [F3], each circle is nullhomotopic; [F2] and [A1] supply both complementary disk regions, so for each circle choose the region not containing $q$ and orient it to induce the Seifert-circle orientation. Disjoint Jordan circles have disk regions that are nested or disjoint, so their finite strict-inclusion order admits a linear extension. Place nested disks at distinct nearby heights in that order; their interiors are then pairwise disjoint as subsets of $S^3$.",
