          "source": "thm-oriented-knot-framing-classes-form-z-torsor",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented three-sphere, and let $F$ be a connected compact oriented smooth embedded surface with oriented boundary $K$. Fix the standard round metric on $S^3$. A normal field along $K$ assigns to every point $p\\in K$ a nonzero vector in the plane orthogonal to $T_pK$; two such fields represent the same framing class when they are homotopic through nonzero normal fields. The inward unit vector tangent to $F$ along $K$, together with the positive quarter-turn in each oriented normal plane, gives a reference frame. In this frame the relative normal field is a map $K\\cong S^1\\to S^1$, and its degree gives a bijection from framing classes to $\\mathbb Z$. Adding $n$ positive full twists changes this integer by $n$.",
