          "claim": "Let $U$ be the standard round unknot and $D$ a smooth embedded spanning disk. Remove the interiors of two disjoint small disks from $\\operatorname{Int}D$ to obtain a pair of pants $P$. Join the two new boundary circles by a simple arc in a small ball on one side of $D$ and disjoint from $U$; the lateral boundary of a sufficiently thin tubular neighborhood of that arc is an embedded annulus $A$ meeting $P$ only in its two attaching circles. Glue with matching orientations. Then $F=P\\cup A$ is connected, compact, smooth, embedded, oriented, and has only boundary $U$. Choose finite cell structures with both attaching circles subcomplexes. Cell-count inclusion-exclusion gives $\\chi(P)=\\chi(D)-2\\chi(D^2)+2\\chi(S^1)=1-2+0=-1$; then $\\chi(F)=\\chi(P)+\\chi(A)-2\\chi(S^1)=-1+0-0=-1$.",
