          "source": "lem-bifiltered-two-hook-maps-cannot-both-vanish",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $C$ be a free based chain complex over $\\mathbb F_2[U,U^{-1}]$ with integer bifiltration $(i,j)$, multiplication by $U$ lowering both coordinates by one, and differential not increasing either coordinate. Chains have finite support. The filtration of a sum is the maximum of the coordinates of its supported basis monomials. Write $V=C\\{i=0\\}$ and, for an integer $s$, write $E_s=C\\{\\min(i,j-s)=0\\}$ and $A_s=C\\{\\max(i,j-s)=0\\}$. These are the subquotients supported on the vertical line, the northeast hook, and the southwest hook respectively. More precisely, $V=C\\{i\\le0\\}/C\\{i<0\\}$; $E_s$ is the subcomplex supported on $i=0$ or $j=s$ in the quotient $C/C\\{i<0\\text{ or }j<s\\}$; and $A_s=C\\{i\\le0,j\\le s\\}/C\\{i<0,j<s\\}$. Define $F_s:H(V)\\to H(E_s)$ by quotienting the vertical line below $s$ and including the resulting upper ray into $E_s$. Define $G_s:H(A_s)\\to H(V)$ by killing the strictly left ray and including the resulting lower vertical ray.\n\nIf a class $\\xi\\in H(V)$ has a cycle representative supported at $j\\le s$ and satisfies $F_s(\\xi)=0$, then $\\xi$ belongs to the image of $G_s$. Consequently, if $H(V)$ is one-dimensional and $s$ is the least level representing its nonzero class, the two maps $F_s,G_s$ cannot both be zero.",
