          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal R$ be the nonnegative real-exponent series ring over $\\mathbb F_2$, with $\\operatorname{gr}(v^\\alpha)=-\\alpha$. Let $C$ be a finite free $\\mathcal R$-module with a fixed finite real-graded basis and an $\\mathcal R$-linear differential of degree $-1$. Then graded changes of basis decompose $C$ into finitely many zero-differential rank-one summands and finitely many two-term summands\n$$\\mathcal R x\\xrightarrow{\\partial}\\mathcal R y,\\qquad\\partial x=v^\\alpha y,\\quad\\partial y=0,\\quad\\alpha\\ge0.$$\nConsequently homology is a finite direct sum of graded copies of $\\mathcal R$ and of cyclic torsion modules $\\mathcal R/(v^\\alpha)$; a summand with $\\alpha=0$ contributes zero homology. If there is a non-torsion homology class, the maximal grading of a homogeneous non-torsion class exists and equals the greatest grading of the finitely many free homology generators.",
