          "quote": "Let $K\\subset S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot and $C=\\mathrm{CFK}^{\\infty}(K)$ a finitely generated free $\\mathbb F_2[U,U^{-1}]$ complex. Choose a finite homogeneous basis $\\{x_r\\}$, with $M(x_r)$ and Alexander filtration $A(x_r)$. The translate $U^k x_r$ has Maslov grading $M(x_r)-2k$ and filtration coordinates $(i,j)=(-k,A(x_r)-k)$. The total homology is $\\mathbb F_2[U,U^{-1}]$; use the standard normalization in which its Maslov-zero tower generator first appears at algebraic filtration level $i=0$, and denote it by $\\xi_K$.\n\nFor $t\\in[0,2]$ and a nonzero finite chain $z$, define\n$$ F_t(U^k x_r)=(1-t/2)(-k)+(t/2)(A(x_r)-k),\\qquad F_t(z)=\\max\\{F_t(U^k x_r):U^k x_r\\text{ has nonzero coefficient in }z\\}. $$\nLet $\\mathcal Z_0(C)$ be the set of Maslov-zero cycles representing $\\xi_K$. Set\n$$ \\nu_t(C)=\\min_{z\\in\\mathcal Z_0(C)}F_t(z),\\qquad \\Upsilon_K(t)=-2\\nu_t(C). $$\nThe minimum is over cycles representing the normalized homology generator, not over individual basis terms. For comparison, let $C^-(K)$ be the $\\mathbb F_2[U]$-span of the chosen basis and form its $t$-modified complex over the ring $\\mathcal R$ of formal sums $\\sum_{\\alpha\\in S}c_\\alpha v^\\alpha$ whose support $S\\subset[0,\\infty)$ is well-ordered (every nonempty subset of $S$ has a least element). The coefficient extension uses $U=v^2$. In the extended Laurent complex, $v$ lowers both filtration coordinates by $1/2$ and Maslov grading by one, so a diagonal $U$-translation lowers the extended $t$-grading by two. On arbitrary homogeneous Laurent terms this grading is $M-t(j-i)$; the formula $M-tA$ below is specified on the chosen generators at $i=0$. A homogeneous generator $x$ has $t$-grading $M(x)-tA(x)$, extended by $\\operatorname{gr}_t(v^\\alpha x)=\\operatorname{gr}_t(x)-\\alpha$. If a term $U^k y$ occurs in $\\partial x$, its $t$-modified differential coefficient is $v^{\\operatorname{gr}_t(y)-\\operatorname{gr}_t(x)+1}$; thus for $\\partial 