          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $G$ be a toroidal grid representing one oriented knot, and let $\\partial^-$ be the full filtered minus differential over $\\mathbb F_2[U_1,\\ldots,U_n]$. Call $O_i$ and $O_j$ consecutive when the $X$-marking in the row of $O_i$ lies in the column of $O_j$. Let $X_\\ell$ be that marking and define the module map\n$$H_\\ell(\\mathbf x)=\\sum_{\\mathbf y}\\sum_{\\substack{r\\in\\operatorname{Rect}^{\\circ}(\\mathbf x,\\mathbf y)\\\\X_\\ell\\in\\operatorname{Int}(r)}}\\left(\\prod_{a=1}^{n}U_a^{O_a(r)}\\right)\\mathbf y.$$\nThen $\\partial^-H_\\ell+H_\\ell\\partial^-=(U_i+U_j)\\operatorname{id}$. The map $H_\\ell$ has Maslov degree $-1$ and does not raise the Alexander filtration. Consequently multiplication by any two variables $U_i,U_j$ is filtered chain homotopic, since the consecutive relation follows the single cycle of the knot grid.",
