          "quote": "Let $C,C'$ be free $\\mathbb F_2[U]$ chain complexes on homogeneous Alexander-filtered bases. Suppose $U$ lowers Maslov grading by two and Alexander filtration by one, and the differentials lower Maslov grading by one and do not increase Alexander filtration. Bases may be infinite provided each matrix column has finite support. Put $g_t(x)=M(x)-tA(x)$ for each basis vector and $0\\le t\\le2$. Replace a homogeneous degree-$d$ filtered polynomial matrix term $cU^ky$ in $f(x)$ by $cv^{g_t(y)-g_t(x)-d}y$ over the nonnegative real-exponent ring $\\mathcal R$. This defines a degree-$d$ matrix $f_t$ over $\\mathcal R$. The construction preserves sums of equal-degree maps, identities, composition, chain-map equations, and filtered chain-homotopy identities. It therefore carries Maslov-graded Alexander-filtered chain homotopy equivalences to graded chain homotopy equivalences of $t$-modified complexes. Moreover the product basis gives a natural graded chain isomorphism\n$$(C\\otimes_{\\mathbb F_2[U]}D)_t\\cong C_t\\otimes_{\\mathcal R}D_t.$$\nThe coefficient extension uses $U=v^2$ before the differential and the maps are reweighted; the construction is not ordinary scalar extension of the original differential.",
