          "quote": "Let $G$ be any $n\\times n$ grid diagram representing a smooth oriented knot $K\\subset S^3$. Form the diagonal grid complex by setting every marking variable $U_i$ equal to a single variable $U$, and define $\\Upsilon_G(t)$ by the t-modified non-torsion grading on that complex for $0\\le t\\le1$, extended by $\\Upsilon_G(t)=\\Upsilon_G(2-t)$ for $1<t\\le2$. Then for every $t\\in[0,2]$,\n$$ \\Upsilon_G(t)=\\Upsilon_K(t), $$\nwhere $\\Upsilon_K$ is the finite cycle-minimax invariant defined from $\\mathrm{CFK}^{\\infty}(K)$. In this statement the quotient with all $U_i$ identified carries the factor $W^{\\otimes(n-1)}$, where $W$ has generators in Maslov/Alexander bidegrees $(0,0)$ and $(-1,-1)$; this factor is retained in the proof and is not counted as an improvement to the grid-state complexity bound.",
