          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "In the vertical complex, the differential is $x_1\\mapsto x_2$, so its degree-zero homology generator is $x_0$ and first appears at Alexander level $1$. The normalized comparison in [F4], after quotient by the chosen $U$ action, identifies this filtered hat complex with the specified-data complex in [[def-knot-floer-filtration-and-tau]]; hence $\\tau(T_{2,3})=1$. For the exact epsilon maps at $s=1$, the target of $F_1$ contains $U^{-1}x_1$ with boundary $x_0$: its other differential term $U^{-1}x_2$ has $j<1$ and is killed there. Thus $F_1=0$. The source of $G_1$ contains the degree-zero cycle $x_0$, while $U^{-1}x_1$ has $i>0$ and is excluded, so that class survives and maps to the nonzero vertical class. Thus $G_1\\ne0$ and the exact three-case definition gives epsilon $1$ for this complex.",
