        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-ip-analytic-wavefront-fbi-transform",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $u$ be a distribution, not necessarily compactly supported, or a distributional density (a continuous functional on compactly supported smooth scalar functions), on a real-analytic $n$-manifold $X$. Let $x_0$ lie in an analytic coordinate chart and let $\\xi_0\\in T^*_{x_0}X\\setminus\\{0\\}$ have coordinate components in that chart. For $\\chi\\in C_c^\\infty$ supported in the chart and equal to $1$ near $x_0$, define the Gaussian FBI packet\n$$\n\\mathcal F_\\chi u(x,\\lambda\\omega) =\\left\\langle u(y),\\chi(y) \\exp\\!\\left(i\\lambda(x-y)\\cdot\\omega-\\tfrac{\\lambda}{2}|x-y|^2\\right)\\right\\rangle, \\quad \\lambda\\ge1,\\quad |\\omega|=1.\n$$\nWhen $u$ is a scalar distribution, the pairing is with the displayed function times coordinate density $|dy|$; when $u$ is a distributional density, the pairing is with the displayed scalar function. In both cases $\\lambda\\omega$ is the cotangent frequency. The covector $(x_0,\\xi_0)$ is analytically regular for $u$ in this chart if there are such a cutoff $\\chi$, a neighborhood $U$ of $x_0$, an open neighborhood $\\Gamma$ of $\\xi_0/|\\xi_0|$ in the unit sphere, and constants $c,C>0$ such that\n$$\n|\\mathcal F_\\chi u(x,\\lambda\\omega)|\\le C e^{-c\\lambda} \\quad(x\\in U,\\ \\omega\\in\\Gamma,\\ \\lambda\\ge1).\n$$\nThe analytic wavefront set $\\operatorname{WF}_A(u)$ is the set of nonzero cotangent vectors for which this exponential estimate fails. This is a chart-local definition. The separate local FBI-invariance claim needed for a geometric interpretation is stated by the companion lemma.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ip-analytic-cutoff-sequence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U\\subset\\mathbb R^n$ be open, and let $K\\subset U$ be compact. There are constants $A,C>0$ and functions $\\chi_N\\in C_c^\\infty(U)$ for each integer $N\\ge1$ such that $0\\le\\chi_N\\le1$, $\\chi_N=1$ on a fixed neighborhood of $K$, and\n$$\n|\\partial^\\alpha\\chi_N(x)|\\le C(AN)^{|\\alpha|} \\qquad (x\\in\\mathbb R^n,\\ |\\alpha|\\le N).\n$$\nThese are smooth compact cutoffs; no compactly supported analytic function is asserted.",
          "uses": [
