          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-ip-analytic-nonstationary-incidence-localization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be an analytic double-fibration transform and $u\\in\\mathcal E'(X)$ with support $K$. Fix a nonzero data covector $(z_0,\\zeta_0)$. Suppose there is no relation point $(z_0,\\zeta_0;x,\\xi)\\in C_Z$ with $x\\in K$. Then $(z_0,\\zeta_0)\\notin\\operatorname{WF}_A(Ru)$. More precisely, the transpose of a data Gaussian packet, localized near $z_0$, is exponentially small with every fixed number of object derivatives on a neighborhood of $K$, uniformly for data centers and directions near $(z_0,\\zeta_0/|\\zeta_0|)$.",
