          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-ip-double-fibration-conormal-kernel",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $Z\\subseteq G\\times X$ be an embedded incidence submanifold of codimension $k>0$, and let $(g_0,x_0)\\in Z$. Choose coordinates near this point and a submersion $F:G\\times X\\to\\mathbb R^k$ with $Z=\\{F=0\\}$. Write $F=(F_1,\\ldots,F_k)$. For every $\\tau\\in\\mathbb R^k\\setminus\\{0\\}$, the conormal covector at $(g,x)\\in Z$ is\n$$\n(g,x;D_gF(g,x)^T\\tau,\\ D_xF(g,x)^T\\tau).\n$$\nConsequently the incidence kernel has local delta representation $b(g,x)\\delta(F(g,x))|dg\\,dx|$, with a smooth density coefficient $b$, and its cotangent relation consists exactly of\n$$\n(g,D_gF^T\\tau;\\ x,-D_xF^T\\tau),\\qquad (g,x)\\in Z,\\quad \\tau\\ne0.\n$$\nNo general Fourier-integral-operator composition calculus is used.",
