          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Choose analytic fiber coordinates for $\\pi_X$, $ (t,x)\\longmapsto (z(t,x),x)\\in Z,\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb R^d. $ The matrix $D_tz$ is injective because this map is an immersion with $x$ retained. The conormal equations from [F1] are $ (D_tz)^Tp=0,\\qquad \\xi=(D_xz)^Tp. $ The first equations define an analytic bundle of rank $\\dim G-d$ in the $p$ variables, so $(t,x,p)$ with these equations parameterize $C_Z$ locally. The map to data cotangent space is $(t,x,p)\\mapsto(z(t,x),p)$. Its derivative is injective by the hypothesis; selecting a full-rank coordinate minor and applying [F3] makes it an analytic embedding on a smaller neighborhood. Denote its image by $V$.",
