          "id": "step-2-2",
          "claim": "Pair $Ru$ with the data Gaussian and use the typed transpose in [F1]. Up to the harmless unit factor $e^{i\\lambda q\\cdot p}$ its object kernel is $ K_\\lambda(x,v)=\\int e^{i\\lambda\\Psi(t,x,v)}b(t,x)\\,dt,\\qquad \\Psi=-z(t,x)\\cdot p+\\frac i2|z(t,x)-q|^2. $ The analytic coefficient $b$ is nowhere zero by [F2] and the fiber-coordinate Jacobian. Data and fiber cutoffs are one near the base incidence point. Their transition pieces have $|z-q|\\ge r>0$ after shrinking $x,v$; their integrals are $O(e^{-c\\lambda})$ in every fixed object derivative by the finite-order distribution estimates and the Gaussian factor. Properness ensures the remaining relevant incidence portion is compact, so finitely many such estimates suffice. A fixed fiber cutoff can therefore be inserted without changing the formula except for these errors.",
