          "claim": "The critical-value and derivative identities are $ \\psi(X(v),v)=-q\\cdot p,\\qquad \\psi_x(X(v),v)=-D_xz(t_0,X(v))^Tp=-\\Xi(v). $ The imaginary part and its first object derivative vanish there. Taylor's integral formula and the strict Hessian bound in step 3.1 therefore give $\\operatorname{Im}\\psi(x,v)\\ge c|x-X(v)|^2$ for real $x,v$ nearby. This fixes the sign for the FBI pairing: the test function has derivative $-\\Xi$, while the distributional covector detected is $+\\Xi$.",
