          "source": "def-locally-flat-topological-knot-concordance",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $K_0,K_1$ be smooth oriented knots in the standard oriented three-sphere $S^3$, and let $I=[0,1]$. They are locally flat topologically concordant if there is a topological proper embedding $f:S^1\\times I\\to S^3\\times I$ whose image is a locally flat annulus, whose boundary circles are $K_0\\times\\{0\\}$ and $K_1\\times\\{1\\}$, and whose annulus orientation induces the boundary $-K_0\\times\\{0\\}\\sqcup K_1\\times\\{1\\}$. The annulus must have product collars at both ends. No differentiability of the annulus is assumed.",
