          "claim": "First consider smooth concordances. Pick one point on each endpoint knot. By [F4], apply separate endpoint ambient isotopies carrying both marked points to a common point $p\\in S^3$; extend them over disjoint product collars of the concordance and interpolate by the identity between the collars. This changes the representatives only within their ambient-isotopy classes. Choose a smooth spanning arc in each annulus joining the marked points and fixed in product collars. For one annulus, write this arc as $\\alpha$ and the standard product arc as $\\beta(s)=(p,s)$. Since $S^3\\times(0,1)$ is simply connected by [F3], the middle portions of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are homotopic rel endpoints after their common endpoint collars are deleted. Relative smooth approximation in [F3] gives a smooth homotopy $H(s,t)$ fixed on those collars. We now perturb this homotopy through a finite-dimensional family. First, local coordinate bumps whose $s$-derivatives span the four target coordinates at each zero of $\\partial_sH$ make the total derivative family transverse to the zero section of the rank-four tangent bundle; its source has dimension two, so a generic parameter has $\\partial_sH\\ne0$ everywhere. Compactness then supplies a uniform $\\delta>0$ for local injectivity of every slice when $|s-s'|<\\delta$. On the compact configuration set $|s-s'|\\ge\\delta$, use two disjoint source-supported coordinate bumps near each pair to vary $H(s,t)$ and $H(s',t)$ independently. A finite cover of the possible diagonal preimage makes the total pair map transverse to the diagonal in $(S^3\\times I)^2$. Its source-pair-time dimension is three and the diagonal has codimension four, so the generic slice has no double points. Both perturbations are supported away from the endpoint collars and can be chosen small enough to preserve immersion and local injectivity. Thus every time-slice is a smooth embedding, giving an isotopy of proper arcs rel collars. The isotopy is stationary on common source end collars, so restrict to the compact middle arcs containing its moving part; these lie in $S^3\\times(0,1)$, a boundaryless smooth manifold. Apply [F3] there with support in the interior, choosing the extension to fix the adjacent stationary arc collars, and extend it by the identity across the fixed end collars. This gives an ambient isotopy of $S^3\\times I$ fixed near both end levels and carrying the whole spanning arc to the vertical product arc without changing the concordance or its oriented endpoint knot types.",
