          "source": "def-reverse-mirror-of-oriented-knot",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix the orientation-reversing reflection $r:S^3\\to S^3$ chosen for the mirror convention in the oriented connected-sum definition. If $K$ is a smooth oriented knot, its mirror $r(K)$ carries the orientation induced from $K$ by $r$. The reverse mirror of $K$, denoted $K^\\dagger$, is the image $r(K)$ with its knot orientation reversed. Thus $K^\\dagger$ changes both the ambient orientation convention and the orientation of the knot.",
