          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Choose a $\\mathbb Q$-basis $v_1,\\ldots,v_g$ of $L$. Clearing the finitely many denominators in the coordinates of each $v_i$ gives nonzero integer multiples $x_i\\in H\\cap L$. The $x_i$ remain $\\mathbb Q$-linearly independent, so $M=H\\cap L$ has rank at least $g$; it has rank at most $\\dim_{\\mathbb Q}L=g$. Hence $\\operatorname{rank}M=g$.",
