          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Choice** (AC) is the following statement.\n\n> Every family of nonempty sets has a choice function\n> (Choice function).\n\nWritten out: for every set $\\mathcal{F}$ all of whose members are nonempty,\nthere exists a function $g$ with domain $\\mathcal{F}$ satisfying $g(S) \\in S$ for\nall $S \\in \\mathcal{F}$.\n\nAn equivalent formulation is that a product of nonempty sets is nonempty: if\n$X_i \\ne \\emptyset$ for every $i \\in I$, then $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i \\ne \\emptyset$.\nHere $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i$ is the set of functions $f$ with domain $I$ such that\n$f(i) \\in X_i$ for every $i \\in I$; when a family of nonempty sets is indexed by\nitself, such an $f$ is precisely a choice function for it.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "4.1",
            "8.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-locally-flat-proper-surface-and-concordance-collars",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a four-dimensional manifold with boundary and let $W$ be a compact surface with boundary. An embedding $e:(W,\\partial W)\\to(X,\\partial X)$ is proper when $e^{-1}(\\partial X)=\\partial W$. It is locally flat at an interior point of $W$ when there are neighborhoods of the point and its image and a homeomorphism of pairs from those neighborhoods to $(\\mathbb R^4,\\mathbb R^2)$, with the standard linear plane $\\mathbb R^2\\subset\\mathbb R^4$. It is locally flat at a boundary point when there are such neighborhoods and a homeomorphism of pairs to $(\\mathbb R^4_+,\\mathbb R^2_+)$, where $\\mathbb R^4_+=\\{x_4\\geq0\\}$ and $\\mathbb R^2_+=\\{x_2=x_3=0,\\ x_4\\geq0\\}$; the line $\\partial\\mathbb R^2_+$ lies in $\\partial\\mathbb R^4_+$. A collar of a boundary circle of $W$ is an embedding of that circle times $[0,\\varepsilon)$ into $W$ that is the identity on the circle at parameter $0$; a concordance collar is required to agree with the corresponding product collar of the ambient end. A smooth proper surface has the analogous smooth charts and collars, which are also topological locally flat charts.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "6.1",
            "8.1",
            "8.2",
            "8.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-time-dependent-vector-fields-have-local-smooth-evolution-operators",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval, and let $X_t$ be a smooth\ntime-dependent vector field on $M$ over $I$. For every $(s,p)\\in I\\times M$\nthere exist an open interval $J\\subseteq I$ containing $s$, open\nneighbourhoods $U_r$ of the evolving points, and a smooth map\n\n$$ \\Psi:\\{(t,s,q): t,s\\in J,\\ q\\in U_s\\}\\to M $$\n\nsuch that $t\\mapsto \\Psi_{t,s}(q)$ is the unique solution of\n$\\dot\\gamma(t)=X_t(\\gamma(t))$ with $\\Psi_{s,s}(q)=q$.",
