      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Set $\\lambda:=\\mu-\\nu$. If $K\\subset\\Omega$ is compact and nonempty, then for every sufficiently large $m$, rational inner balls with doubled closures in $\\Omega\\cap\\{x:\\operatorname{dist}(x,K)<1/m\\}$ cover $K$; [F2] gives a finite subcover, and ordering finite rational lists by natural-number codes gives a least such cover. Put the fixed bump [F3] on each selected ball and combine them as $\\eta_m=1-\\prod_j(1-\\psi_{m,j})$. Then $0\\le\\eta_m\\le1$, it equals one on $K$, is supported in the $1/m$-neighborhood of $K$, and $\\eta_m(x)\\to\\mathbf1_K(x)$. Since each $\\eta_m$ is a smooth compactly supported test function, $\\int\\eta_m\\,d\\lambda=0$; dominated convergence [F4] with respect to the finite regular total-variation measure [F1] gives $\\lambda(K)=0$. The empty compact set has measure zero directly.",
