      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $\\Omega=\\varnothing$, the empty family proves the claim. Otherwise, for $m\\ge1$ set $K_m=\\{x:|x|\\le m,\\ \\operatorname{dist}(x,\\Omega^c)\\ge1/m\\}$ when $\\Omega\\ne\\mathbb R^n$, and set $K_m=\\overline B(0,m)$ when $\\Omega=\\mathbb R^n$; put $K_m=\\varnothing$ for $m\\le0$. Each $K_m$ is compact by [F1], the sets are nested, $K_m\\subset\\operatorname{int}K_{m+1}$, and their interiors cover $\\Omega$. The compact shells $S_m:=K_m\\setminus\\operatorname{int}K_{m-1}$ cover $\\Omega$ and lie in the open sets $U_m:=\\operatorname{int}K_{m+1}\\setminus K_{m-2}$. The family $(U_m)$ is locally finite: any compact subset of $\\Omega$ lies in some $\\operatorname{int}K_N$ and hence in $K_{m-2}$ for all sufficiently large $m$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Fix once a smooth nonnegative cutoff $\\theta$ equal to one on $\\overline B(0,1)$ and supported in $B(0,2)$, whose existence is [F3]. In each $U_m$, consider the rational inner balls $B(q,r)$ for which $\\overline B(q,2r)\\subset U_m\\cap V_\\ell$ for some cover index $\\ell$. Indexed by $(\\ell,q,r)$, these balls form a countable cover of $S_m$: for each point choose a cover member containing it, then density [F2] gives a rational center and radius with the required doubled closure. Compactness of $S_m$ gives a finite subcover. Order all finite lists of eligible indexed balls by natural-number codes and take the first list covering $S_m$; thus no choice principle is needed. For each selected ball use the fixed rescaled cutoff $\\psi_{m,j}(x):=\\theta((x-q)/r)$. The family is locally finite because each shell contributes finitely many cutoffs supported in $U_m$, and each support also lies in its assigned cover member. Its sum $s:=\\sum_{m,j}\\psi_{m,j}$ is smooth and positive on $\\Omega$ because the shells cover $\\Omega$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "step 1.1",
            "choose",
            "construct"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Define $\\eta_{m,j}:=\\psi_{m,j}/s$. Then each function is smooth, nonnegative and compactly supported in $\\Omega$, the family is locally finite, and $\\sum_{m,j}\\eta_{m,j}=1$. Each support remains in its assigned cover member, and enumeration gives the required countable family.",
