      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $f\\in C_0(\\Omega)$ and $\\varepsilon>0$. The set $K:=\\{x\\in\\Omega:|f(x)|\\ge\\varepsilon/3\\}$ is compact by the definition of vanishing at infinity. If $K=\\varnothing$, the zero function approximates $f$ within $\\varepsilon/3$. Otherwise cover $K$ by finitely many inner balls whose doubled closed balls lie in $\\Omega$, using compactness [F1]. Choose the corresponding bumps from [F2] and combine them as $\\chi:=1-\\prod_j(1-\\chi_j)$. Then $\\chi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)$ and $\\chi=1$ on $K$, so $\\|f-\\chi f\\|_\\infty\\le\\varepsilon/3$.",
