          "claim": "Set $v_0=1$. Suppose the current strand meridian on $K_j$ is represented by $v_{i-1}^{-1}x_jv_{i-1}$. At crossing $c_i$, if the component passes source-to-target, [F1] replaces it by $x_{o(c_i)}^{-1}v_{i-1}^{-1}x_jv_{i-1}x_{o(c_i)}$, which is $v_i^{-1}x_jv_i$ for $v_i=v_{i-1}x_{o(c_i)}$. If it passes target-to-source, solving the same relation for the source meridian gives the same formula with $v_i=v_{i-1}x_{o(c_i)}^{-1}$. Thus after one traversal the ordered product is exactly $W_j(D)$.",
