      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The interior of the parametrized PL ball is a contractible boundaryless topological three-manifold. Its second mod-two homology is zero by [F4]. Hence [F1] and [F4] show that its complement of $T$ cannot be connected. The same is true in $B$: push its outer boundary collar slightly inward, fixing the compact interior torus; if $B\\setminus T$ were connected, its connected pushed image and the collar homotopy would make the interior complement connected. There are exactly two components. Indeed the two open product-collar sides of connected $T$ are connected, and every complementary component must meet one: otherwise its closure misses $T$ and it is open and closed in connected $B$. More explicitly, at any point of $T$ in the closure of a component, a local flat chart puts some collar-side patch in that component; the connected full side collar then belongs to it. Thus there are at most two components. Their closures $W_1,W_2$ are compact orientable topological three-manifolds, with the corresponding copies of $T$ in their boundaries.",
