        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-nontrivial-knot-with-supplied-product-tube-has-injective-exterior-boundary",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $e:S^1\\times D^2\\to S^3$ be a supplied orientation-preserving smooth embedding, let $K=e(S^1\\times\\{0\\})$ with its core orientation, let $N=e(S^1\\times D^2)$, and put $E=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{Int}N$ and $T=\\partial E$. If there is a smooth properly embedded disk in $E$ whose boundary is essential in $T$, then $K$ is smoothly ambient isotopic, through orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms, to the standard oriented unknot. Consequently, if $K$ is not that unknot, $T$ has no such disk and $\\pi_1(T)\\to\\pi_1(E)$ is injective. No choice axiom is assumed beyond the supplied input data.\n\nAll ambient isotopies asserted here are jointly smooth and may be stationary near their time endpoints.",
