          "quote": "Let $P$ be a compact smooth $k$-manifold with boundary, let $N$ be a Hausdorff smooth $n$-manifold without boundary, and let $f:P\\times[0,1]\\to N$ be jointly smooth with every $f_t$ a smooth embedding. Suppose the family is stationary on neighborhoods of both time endpoints. For every open neighborhood $W$ of its compact track $f(P\\times[0,1])$, there is a jointly smooth isotopy $H_t:N\\to N$ of diffeomorphisms with $H_0=\\operatorname{id}$ and $H_t\\circ f_0=f_t$, supported in a fixed compact subset of $W$ and stationary near its time endpoints. No choice axiom is assumed. The empty source and zero-dimensional source are allowed.",
