          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a smoothly parametrized product $T^2\\times[0,1]$. Let $S$ be a finite disjoint family of smoothly embedded two-sided tori in its interior. Then all component maps $\\pi_1(S_i)\\to\\pi_1(X)$ are injective if and only if there is no smooth embedded disk whose boundary is essential on one $S_i$ and whose interior misses all of $S$. In that case every component of the smooth cut-open manifold $X\\mathbin{\\|}S$ is injective on fundamental groups into $X$. No irreducibility or choice assumption is required.\n\nThis is an interface for a supplied smooth product. It asserts neither triangulability of an arbitrary topological three-manifold nor smoothing of an arbitrary ambient PL marking.",
