          "claim": "Choose the finite compatible triangulation of [F3] once. If $E_K$ itself is atoroidal or Seifert, the empty family proves existence and is minimal. Otherwise start with the empty family, and whenever a current component $C$ is neither atoroidal nor Seifert, choose an incompressible torus not boundary-parallel in $C$, by [F8]'s definition of failure of atoroidality. It is two-sided: the torus and ambient orientations orient its normal line, and a finite normal-field flow gives a smooth product neighborhood. Every cut component has nonempty torus boundary. Indeed a boundaryless cut component would have no cutting face and no original boundary, hence would give a closed component of the original connected exterior, impossible by step 1.1. Irreducibility of the successive pieces will follow from [F5]. This construction is needed only for a bounded finite number of steps, as established below.",
