          "claim": "Put $B=4t+\\beta-1$, a fixed finite integer from [F4]. If no stage had become good after at most $B$ cuts, the construction could be extended through $B+1$ cuts by finite induction: at each of these finitely many stages use step 2.1. Steps 3.1 and 4.1 would then give an incompressible torus family with no product cut component and $B+1$ members, contradicting [F4]. Thus a finite good family exists. This argument selects only a bounded finite list of cuts, rather than postulating an infinite sequence of independent choices. The zero-cut empty family in the nongood initial case also satisfies [F4], so $B\\ge0$ there.",
