        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-transverse-preimage-theorem",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $F:M^m\\to N^n$ be smooth and let $Z\\subseteq N$ be an embedded submanifold\nof codimension $c$, and suppose $F\\pitchfork Z$. If $c\\le m$, then\n$F^{-1}(Z)$ is an embedded submanifold of $M$ of codimension $c$ (possibly empty). If $c>m$,\nthen $F^{-1}(Z)=\\varnothing$. In the first case, for each $p\\in F^{-1}(Z)$,\n\n$$ T_pF^{-1}(Z)=\\{v\\in T_pM:dF_p(v)\\in T_{F(p)}Z\\}. $$",
