          "source": "lem-link-seifert-matrix-enlargement-under-arc-surgery",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $L$ be a nonempty smooth oriented link with $r$ components, let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented spanning surface of genus $g$, and let $F'$ be obtained by choosing an embedded solid cylinder $[0,1]\\times D^2$ that meets $F$ exactly in its two end disks and lies on the same local side at both disks, then replacing those disks by the cylinder's lateral annulus with the compatible orientation. This surgery preserves $L$. Put $m=2g+r-1$, choose an ordered integral basis of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ represented away from the two end disks, and let $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$ be its positive-push Seifert matrix. The surviving classes of that basis extend by two classes to an integral basis of $H_1(F';\\mathbb Z)$, and for some column vectors $x,y\\in\\mathbb Z^m$ and integer $z$, the new Seifert matrix is one of\n$$\\begin{pmatrix}V&x&0\\\\y^T&z&0\\\\0^T&1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\begin{pmatrix}V&x&0\\\\y^T&z&1\\\\0^T&0&0\\end{pmatrix}.$$",
