          "quote": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $L$ be a nonempty smooth oriented link in the oriented $3$-sphere, and let $F_0,F_1$ be connected compact smooth oriented embedded surfaces with the same oriented boundary $L$. There is a finite sequence of such spanning surfaces from $F_0$ to $F_1$ in which each consecutive pair differs either by an ambient isotopy fixed on $L$ or by one embedded arc surgery or its reverse.",
