          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented standard $3$-sphere, let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented surface with oriented boundary $K$, let $V$ be the matrix of the Seifert pairing $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$ in an ordered integral basis, and let $\\omega\\in S^1\\setminus\\{1\\}$. Define the **Levine–Tristram Hermitian matrix** by\n$$H_\\omega(V)=(1-\\omega)V+(1-\\bar\\omega)V^T.$$\nIt is Hermitian because $V$ is real and $\\bar\\omega=\\omega^{-1}$. Its signature is the number of positive eigenvalues minus the number of negative eigenvalues, both counted with multiplicity and with zero eigenvalues omitted. When $\\Delta_K(\\omega)\\ne0$, define $\\sigma_\\omega(K)$ to be this signature. At a root $\\omega_0\\ne1$ of $\\Delta_K$, define $\\sigma_{\\omega_0}(K)$ to be the arithmetic mean of the two one-sided limits of $\\sigma_{e^{i\\theta}}(K)$ as $\\theta$ approaches an argument of $\\omega_0$ from below and above. The invariance and one-sided-existence lemmas justify treating these values as independent of the chosen surface and basis.",
