          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $g=0$, the matrix and homology group are empty, $\\Delta_K^\\#=1$, and $\\operatorname{Arf}(K)=0$, so the congruence holds. Assume $g\\ge1$. Choose a symplectic integral basis and, in each pair, arrange $v_{2i-1,2i}\\equiv1$ and $v_{2i,2i-1}\\equiv0\\pmod2$. This is possible because their difference is $1$; if the odd entry is in the reverse position, replace $(a_i,b_i)$ by $(b_i,-a_i)$, which keeps $a_i\\cdot b_i=1$. Let $A(t)=V^T-tV$. For indices $r,s$ in a paired position, its entries modulo two are $a_{2i,2i-1}=1$ and $a_{2i-1,2i}=t$; for every other position $a_{rs}=(1+t)v_{rs}$. The diagonal case is included, as $(1-t)v_{rr}=(1+t)v_{rr}$ modulo two.",
