      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Since $P$ is real, $H_\\omega(P^TVP)=P^TH_\\omega(V)P$. An invertible congruence is a change of coordinates in the associated Hermitian form, so its positive and negative indices are unchanged: a maximal positive subspace maps bijectively by $P$, and likewise for negative subspaces. Hence the signature is invariant under basis change.",
