        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Write $\\nabla_K(z)=1+a_2z^2+a_4z^4+\\cdots$. For a knot the matrix size is $2g$, so $D_K(u^{-1})=\\det(u^{-1}V-uV^T)=\\det(uV^T-u^{-1}V)=D_K(u)$, using even size in the first equality and transposition in the second. Since replacing $u$ by $u^{-1}$ sends $z=u-u^{-1}$ to $-z$, and substitution into the Laurent polynomial ring is injective (the highest Laurent power of a nonzero polynomial in $z$ cannot cancel), this identity gives $\\nabla_K(z)=\\nabla_K(-z)$ and hence all odd coefficients vanish. Set $u^2=t$. Then $z^2=(u-u^{-1})^2=t+t^{-1}-2\\equiv(1+t)^2/t\\pmod{(2,(1+t)^4)}$, and $z^4$ is divisible by $(1+t)^4$ in that quotient. Hence [F4] gives\n$$\\Delta_K^\\#(t)\\equiv1+a_2(\\nabla_K)(1+t)^2/t\\pmod{(2,(1+t)^4)}.$$\nComparing with [F5], and using that $(1+t)^2/t$ is nonzero modulo $(1+t)^4$, yields $a_2(\\nabla_K)\\equiv\\operatorname{Arf}(K)\\pmod2$.",
