          "source_section": "Example",
          "quote": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $T$ and $E$ be the oriented boundaries of the standard one-boundary square plumbings of two positive Hopf bands and of one positive with one negative Hopf band, respectively; these are the right-handed trefoil and the figure-eight knot. A positive Hopf band is an oriented annulus whose induced boundary components have linking number $+1$; its core, the central simple closed curve, has self-pairing $-1$. a negative Hopf band has boundary linking number $-1$ and core self-pairing $+1$. A square plumbing identifies a square in the boundary collars of the two annuli so that its edges alternate between them, then smooths the corners; use the gluing for which the resulting boundary is one component. Order the two cores $a,b$ with the positive Hopf core first, orient them so $a\\cdot_F b=+1$, and use the standard plumbing side for which $a^+$ bounds a disk disjoint from $b$. In the positive-push convention $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$, their Seifert matrices are\n\n$$V_T=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&0\\\\-1&-1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad V_E=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&0\\\\-1&1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nTheir determinant representatives are $\\Delta_T(t)=1-t+t^2$ and $\\Delta_E(t)=-1+3t-t^2$. They both evaluate to $1$ at $t=1$; at $t=-1$ the displayed representatives evaluate to $3$ and $-5$, so the unit-invariant absolute values are $3$ and $5$. These determinant classes are unchanged up to units by oriented ambient isotopy and integral basis changes. The connected sum satisfies\n\n$$\\Delta_{T\\#E}(t)\\doteq(1-t+t^2)(-1+3t-t^2)=-t^4+4t^3-5t^2+4t-1.$$\n\nThis displayed representative has values $1$ at $t=1$ and $-15$ at $t=-1$.",
