          "claim": "For each displayed enlargement, its skew part has block form\n$$E_i-E_i^T=\\begin{pmatrix}J&u&0\\\\-u^T&0&s_i\\\\0^T&-s_i&0\\end{pmatrix},$$\nwhere $J=V-V^T$, $u=x-y$, $s_0=-1$, and $s_1=1$. If $V$ is knot-derived, [A1] is the choice hypothesis for its Seifert-pairing convention; the following lattice calculation itself is choice-free. Since $J$ is unimodular, choose the integral vector $c=-J^{-1}u$ and replace the penultimate basis vector by itself plus the old-basis combination $c$. This integral basis change removes the $u$ block and leaves $J\\oplus\\begin{pmatrix}0&s_i\\\\-s_i&0\\end{pmatrix}$. Both blocks are unimodular, so each enlargement is an integral Seifert lattice.",
