          "id": "step-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "Since $V$ and $V^T$ are invertible over $\\mathbb Q$, $T=V^{-1}V^T$ is invertible. Direct multiplication gives\n$$\nT^TBT=V(V^T)^{-1}(V+V^T)V^{-1}V^T=V+V^T=B,\n$$\nbecause the two summands in the middle expression simplify respectively to $V$ and $V^T$. Therefore $T$ is a $B$-isometry.",
