          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented standard $3$-sphere, and let $F,F'$ be any connected compact smooth oriented spanning surfaces for $K$. For any ordered integral bases of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ and $H_1(F';\\mathbb Z)$, the matrices of the positive-push Seifert pairing are related by a finite sequence of integral unimodular congruences and the two rank-two elementary Seifert enlargements or their reverses.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-seifert-matrix-s-enlargement-preserves-algebraic-concordance-class",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC for any knot-derived Seifert matrix. Let $V$ be an integral Seifert matrix and let $E_0(V;x,y,z)$ or $E_1(V;x,y,z)$ be either elementary enlargement in the definition of S-equivalence, where $x,y\\in\\mathbb Z^{2g}$ and $z\\in\\mathbb Z$. Then $E_0(V;x,y,z)$ and $E_1(V;x,y,z)$ are integral Seifert lattices, and each represents the same element of $G_{\\mathbb Z}$ as $V$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-seifert-matrix-s-equivalence-under-isotopy",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $(K,F)$ and $(K',F')$ be oriented knot and spanning-surface pairs in the oriented standard three-sphere, and let $h_t:S^3\\to S^3$ be a smooth ambient isotopy with $h_0$ the identity, $h_1(K)=K'$, and $h_1(F)=F'$, preserving the given orientations. If $V$ and $V'$ are their Seifert matrices in any integral bases, then the basis transported by $h_1$ has matrix $V$, and any other target basis with transition matrix $P$ has matrix $V'=P^TVP$. Hence $V$ and $V'$ are S-equivalent, meaning they are related by a finite sequence of integral unimodular congruences and the two elementary rank-two enlargement moves or their reverses.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "def-knot-connected-sum-and-prime-knot",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix a coordinate orientation-reversing reflection $r:S^3\\to S^3$ for the mirror convention. Let $K$ and $J$ be smooth oriented knots in the standard oriented three-sphere. A connected-sum datum consists of one smoothly embedded closed three-ball around a short subarc of $K$ and one around a short subarc of $J$, each meeting its knot in a single trivial properly embedded arc, together with the fixed standard orientation-reversing boundary identification of the two standard oriented ball boundaries that joins the oriented arcs into one circle. Choose this standard map once in the standard two-ball model so that it commutes with $r$ and an orientation-preserving half-turn interchanging the two balls preserves the joining convention. Here a trivial arc is an embedded interval in a ball that is carried by an orientation-preserving diffeomorphism of ball-arc pairs to a straight diameter. Remove the interiors of the two balls and glue the remaining boundary spheres using this fixed identification; the resulting oriented knot in the standard oriented three-sphere is a connected sum of $K$ and $J$, denoted $K\\#J$ for the specified datum.\n\nThe **standard unknot** is the oriented unit circle in a fixed coordinate two-plane of $S^3\\subset\\mathbb R^4$. A knot is **nontrivial** if it is not ambient isotopic through orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms of $S^3$ to the standard unknot. A nontrivial knot is **prime** if it has no connected-sum presentation whose two summand knots are both nontrivial.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-knot-concordance-is-an-abelian-group",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. The set of smooth oriented knot concordance classes in the standard three-sphere is an abelian group under connected sum, with identity the standard unknot and inverse of $[K]$ represented by the reverse mirror $K^\\dagger$. Separately, the set of locally flat topological oriented knot concordance classes is an abelian group under connected sum, with the same identity and inverse convention.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "lem-smooth-slice-iff-concordant-to-unknot",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. A smooth oriented knot in the standard oriented three-sphere bounds a smooth properly embedded disk in the unit four-ball $B^4=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^4:\\lVert x\\rVert^2\\le1\\}$ if and only if it is smoothly concordant to the standard unknot.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-linking-number-equals-signed-intersection",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ and $J$ be disjoint oriented smooth\nembedded circles in the oriented three-sphere, and let $\\Sigma$ be a compact\noriented smooth surface embedded in the three-sphere with boundary $K$, whose\noutward-normal-first boundary orientation is the specified orientation of $K$.\nHere outward-normal-first means that an outward-pointing normal followed by a\npositive boundary tangent gives the orientation of $\\Sigma$. Assume\n$J$ is transverse to $\\Sigma$, and fix a regular oriented diagram $D$ of\n$J\\cup K$. Let $\\eta$ be a positively oriented meridian of $K$ and let\n$m\\in\\mathbb Z$ be the unique integer such that\n$[J]=m[\\eta]$ in $H_1(S^3\\setminus K;\\mathbb Z)$. Define the topological\nlinking number by $\\operatorname{lk}(J,K):=m$. Let\n$\\operatorname{lk}_D(J,K)$ be the half-sum of the signs of the mixed crossings\nof $D$. Orient the normal line of $\\Sigma$ by the ambient orientation. A point\nof $J\\cap\\Sigma$ has sign $+1$ if the oriented curve $J$ crosses from the\nnegative side of $\\Sigma$ to its positive side, and sign $-1$ for the reverse\npassage. Then\n$$\\operatorname{lk}_D(J,K)=\\operatorname{lk}(J,K)=\\sum_{p\\in J\\cap\\Sigma}\\operatorname{sign}_\\Sigma(p).$$\nThe statement is conditional on a supplied spanning surface and regular\ndiagram; it asserts no surface- or diagram-existence theorem.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "lem-slice-disk-induces-seifert-metabolizer",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented standard $3$-sphere, let $F\\subset S^3$ be a connected compact smooth oriented Seifert surface of genus $g$, and let $D\\subset B^4$ be a locally flat properly embedded disk with oriented boundary $K$. Then the positive-push Seifert lattice $(H_1(F;\\mathbb Z),V)$ is metabolic: it has a rank-$g$ primitive direct summand on which $V$ vanishes identically.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
