          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For a smooth oriented knot $K$, choose a surface and basis from [F1] and define $a(K)=[V_F]\\in G_{\\mathbb Z}$. The class is independent of this choice: [F4] relates any two such matrices by finitely many congruences and elementary enlargements or their inverses. A congruence is an isomorphism of the integral lattice, and each enlargement preserves the class. This also handles every integral basis choice. Applied to a transported surface under an oriented ambient isotopy, the same surface-independence statement and the pairing convention give a function on oriented knot types. This part is proved without a slice-disk premise.",
