        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "If $s(x)=0$, each of the finitely many nonzero primary components of $x$ has all its signatures zero. By [F4] four times each such component is zero; the primary direct-sum isomorphism [F3] gives $4x=0$. Thus $4\\ker s=0$. The same holds for the kernel of $s\\iota$ on $G_{\\mathbb Z}$, since $\\iota$ is injective. Applying [F6] separately to these two countable groups gives decompositions of each with at most countable free, order-two and order-four multiplicities. In particular every torsion class has order dividing four; the proof has used signatures to identify all torsion, rather than merely exhibiting some finite-order classes.",
