          "source": "lem-invertible-seifert-matrix-gives-rational-isometric-structure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC for the knot Seifert-pairing convention. Let $V\\in M_{2g}(\\mathbb Z)$ be an invertible Seifert matrix and put $B=V+V^T$ and $T=V^{-1}V^T$ on $\\mathbb Q^{2g}$. Then $B$ is a nonsingular symmetric bilinear form, $T$ is an invertible $B$-isometry, and $I-T$ is invertible; hence $(\\mathbb Q^{2g},B,T)$ is a rational Seifert isometric structure.",
