          "claim": "**Crossing order and planar isotopy.** Reordering adjacent crossing coordinates $a,b$ is corrected by the diagonal state factor $s(v)=(-1)^{v(a)v(b)}$: on an $a$-edge its ratio is $(-1)^{v(b)}$, and on a $b$-edge it is $(-1)^{v(a)}$, exactly the sign change from swapping their order. Thus local crossings can be ordered first, and can be restored to the original order afterward by explicit chain isomorphisms. A planar isotopy bijects labelled resolution circles and saddles, so its factor permutations give a grading-preserving chain isomorphism.",
