          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "**The determinant sign of each curl.** A Reidemeister-I return joins one of the four adjacent endpoint pairs of [F7]. For the right-hand return choose the strand direction $SW\\to NE\\to SE\\to NW$. At the crossing the over and under tangents are respectively $(1,1)$ and $(-1,1)$, whose determinant is $2>0$. A-smoothing closes the return $NE$--$SE$ into the small circle and leaves the left-hand continuing arc; B-smoothing has only the continuing arc. Thus this positive curl has the multiplication differential, small circle in local degree zero, used in the curl contraction. For the top return choose $SW\\to NE\\to NW\\to SE$. The tangents are $(1,1)$ and $(1,-1)$, with determinant $-2<0$. B-smoothing closes the top return into the small circle while A-smoothing has only the continuing arc. Thus this negative curl has the comultiplication differential, small circle in local degree one. Rotation by $180$ degrees gives the left and bottom returns without changing A/B labels or determinant sign. Reversing the component direction negates both tangents and also leaves the determinant sign unchanged. These four return pairs and the two directions exhaust the oriented local R1 pictures; no orientation-reversing chart or reflection is used.",
