          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $D,D'$ be finite regular oriented link diagrams related by a planar isotopy or one oriented Reidemeister move. Let $\\bar C(D)$ be the integral signed state cube before the writhe shifts, with cohomological degree $|v|$ and quantum degree $|v|+\\sum\\deg(a)$, and normalize it by $C(D)=\\bar C(D)[n_-]\\{2n_--n_+\\}$ to obtain the state degrees $i=|v|-n_-$ and $j=|v|+n_+-2n_-+\\sum\\deg(a)$. Before normalization, a positive type-I curl gives $\\bar C(D_+)\\simeq\\bar C(D)\\{1\\}$, a negative type-I curl gives $\\bar C(D_-)\\simeq\\bar C(D)[-1]\\{-2\\}$, a type-II move gives $\\bar C(D_{II})\\simeq\\bar C(D)[-1]\\{-1\\}$, and a type-III move gives an unshifted equivalence. Consequently the normalized complexes are bigraded chain homotopy equivalent. If $D,D'$ are based knot diagrams and the move disk is disjoint from the basepoint, the same chain homotopy equivalence descends to their reduced quotient complexes, equivalently to the cut-tangle complexes with interval module $M=\\mathbb Z$, $X\\cdot1=0$.",
