        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-chain-homotopy-equivalence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A chain map $f:C_\\bullet\\to D_\\bullet$ is a **chain homotopy equivalence** if\nthere exists a chain map $g:D_\\bullet\\to C_\\bullet$ such that\n$$g\\circ f\\simeq1_C,\\qquad f\\circ g\\simeq1_D.$$\n\nSuch a map $g$ is called a **homotopy inverse** of $f$.",
