      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Under AC$_\\omega$ in [F1], apply [F3] to $(D,p)$ and $(D',p')$. Its moving-ball construction uses the compact isotopy-extension clause of [F2]. It gives a finite Reidemeister movie of their cut one-interval diagrams whose endpoints and short product collars remain fixed throughout. Closing the boundary collars by the same crossing-free cap recovers the two based diagrams. In each resolution this closure replaces the distinguished interval by the based circle and adds no crossing, so it preserves $n_+,n_-$, cohomological degree and reduced quantum degree. The quotient/interval identification is the one proved in the defining reduced-complex item.",
