    "thm-khovanov-euler-characteristic-is-jones": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Choice** (AC) is the following statement.\n\n> Every family of nonempty sets has a choice function\n> (Choice function).\n\nWritten out: for every set $\\mathcal{F}$ all of whose members are nonempty,\nthere exists a function $g$ with domain $\\mathcal{F}$ satisfying $g(S) \\in S$ for\nall $S \\in \\mathcal{F}$.\n\nAn equivalent formulation is that a product of nonempty sets is nonempty: if\n$X_i \\ne \\emptyset$ for every $i \\in I$, then $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i \\ne \\emptyset$.\nHere $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i$ is the set of functions $f$ with domain $I$ such that\n$f(i) \\in X_i$ for every $i \\in I$; when a family of nonempty sets is indexed by\nitself, such an $f$ is precisely a choice function for it.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-choice-implies-dependent-implies-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "In ZF,\n\n$$\\mathrm{AC}\\Longrightarrow\\mathrm{DC}\\Longrightarrow\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega\\Longrightarrow\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega,\\mathrm{fin}}\\Longrightarrow\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega,2},\\qquad \\mathrm{AC}\\Longrightarrow\\mathrm{AC}_2.$$\n\nDC here includes a prescribed initial point.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-khovanov-graded-euler-characteristic-jones-normalization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $D$ be a finite regular oriented diagram of a link with $n_+$ positive crossings, $n_-$ negative crossings, writhe $w=n_+-n_-$, and $n=n_++n_-$. For each resolution state $v$, let $k(v)$ be its number of circles and let $D_v$ use the A-smoothing at coordinates $0$ and B-smoothing at coordinates $1$. Put $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$ and define the normalized bracket\n$$f_D(A):=(-A^3)^{-w}\\sum_{v:C(D)\\to\\{0,1\\}} A^{n-2|v|}\\delta^{k(v)-1}.$$\nFor integral unreduced Khovanov cohomology, define $\\chi_q(Kh(D))=\\sum_{i,j}(-1)^i\\operatorname{rank}_{\\mathbb Z}Kh^{i,j}(D)q^j$. For reduced cohomology use its basepoint quantum grading $\\widetilde j$ and define $\\widetilde\\chi_q=\\sum_{i,\\widetilde j}(-1)^i\\operatorname{rank}_{\\mathbb Z}\\widetilde{Kh}^{i,\\widetilde j}(D,p)q^{\\widetilde j}$. Under $q=-A^{-2}$ and $t=q^2=A^{-4}$,\n$$\\chi_q(Kh(D))=(q+q^{-1})f_D(A),\\qquad \\widetilde\\chi_q(D,p)=f_D(A).$$\nThus the unreduced unknot factor is $q+q^{-1}$ and the reduced unknot factor is $1$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-bracket-state-sum-matches-library-jones-specialization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $A$ and $t$ be formal variables and $K$ a\nnonempty oriented link. At each crossing of a regular diagram $D$ use the\nsource chart with over-strand southwest-to-northeast: A joins left and right\nendpoints with coefficient $A$, and B joins top and bottom endpoints with\ncoefficient $A^{-1}$. A state $S:C(D)\\to\\{A,B\\}$ assigns one smoothing at every\ncrossing; let $a(S)$ and $b(S)$ count these choices and $|S|$ count the\nresulting circles. Fix a unit viewing normal $n$ and orient the projection\nplane $P$ so $(u,v)$ is positive exactly when $(n,u,v)$ is positive in the\nambient oriented $3$-sphere. Define\n$$\\operatorname{sgn}(c)=\\operatorname{sgn}\\det_P(v_{\\rm over},v_{\\rm under}), \\qquad \\operatorname{wr}(D)=\\sum_c\\operatorname{sgn}(c),$$\n$$f_K(A)=(-A^3)^{-\\operatorname{wr}(D)} \\sum_{S:C(D)\\to\\{A,B\\}}A^{a(S)-b(S)}(-A^2-A^{-2})^{|S|-1}.$$\nFor an $n$-strand braid $\\beta$ whose oriented closure is $K$, let\n$e:B_n\\to\\mathbb Z$ be the homomorphism $e(\\sigma_i)=1$, where $\\sigma_i$\nis the positive geometric Artin half twist. Let $H(n)$ be the type-A Hecke\nalgebra with generators $T_i$, quadratic relation $T_i^2=(v-1)T_i+v$, braid\nrelations, and distant commutation, and let $\\pi_n(\\sigma_i)=T_i$. Its\nnormalized Markov trace $\\operatorname{tr}_n$ satisfies\n$\\operatorname{tr}_n(1)=1$, cyclicity, tower restriction, and\n$\\operatorname{tr}_{n+1}(xT_n)=z\\operatorname{tr}_n(x)$. Define the library\nJones value by\n$$V_K(t)=s^{e(\\beta)}\\left(-\\frac{s^2+1}{s}\\right)^{n-1} \\operatorname{tr}_n(\\pi_n(\\beta))\\Big|_{v=s^2,\\,z=-1/(s^2+1),\\,t=s^2},$$\nwhere $s=t^{1/2}$. With $A=t^{-1/4}$, these values satisfy\n$$V_K(t)=f_K(t^{-1/4}).$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-khovanov-homology-is-an-oriented-link-invariant",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. For every nonempty oriented link $L$, the bigraded integral groups $Kh^{i,j}(L):=H^i(C^{*,j}(D))$, where $D$ is any finite regular oriented diagram of $L$ and $C(D)$ is the normalized Khovanov cochain complex, are independent of the choice of $D$ up to bigraded isomorphism.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-reduced-khovanov-basepoint-and-reidemeister-invariance",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $K$ be an oriented knot and let $(D,p)$ and $(D',p')$ be finite regular oriented diagrams of $K$ with basepoints away from all crossings. Then the reduced integral groups $\\widetilde{Kh}^{i,\\widetilde j}(D,p)$ and $\\widetilde{Kh}^{i,\\widetilde j}(D',p')$ are isomorphic for every $(i,\\widetilde j)$. In particular, they are invariant under Reidemeister moves supported away from the basepoint and under transport of the basepoint along the knot.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "By [A1] and [F1], full AC supplies AC$_\\omega$. Hence [F4] identifies the bigraded groups computed from any finite diagram $D$ with $Kh^{i,j}(L)$, and in the knot case identifies the reduced groups with $\\widetilde{Kh}^{i,\\widetilde j}(K,p)$ for every allowed basepoint. The fixed-diagram complexes have finite rank and bounded support, so their rank Euler sums are finite.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
