          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "By [F2], those Euler sums are $(q+q^{-1})f_D(A)$ and $f_D(A)$, respectively. By [F3], $f_D(A)=V_L(A^{-4})$ under the stated full-AC hypothesis. Substituting $q=-A^{-2}$ and $t=q^2=A^{-4}$ gives exactly the two formulas in the Statement. For a crossingless unknot the unreduced complex has its two generators in quantum degrees $1,-1$, whereas the reduced interval module has one generator in reduced degree zero, so the respective factors are $q+q^{-1}$ and $1$. Since [F4] makes the groups diagram- and basepoint-independent, these are the claimed link and knot Euler characteristics.",
