          "quote": "Let $D$ be a finite regular oriented link diagram, order its crossings as $c_1<\\cdots<c_n$, and form the direct sum of state modules $\\mathcal A^{\\otimes k(v)}$ over all functions $v:C(D)\\to\\{0,1\\}$. Here $\\mathcal A=\\mathbb Z[X]/(X^2)$, each crossing is changed from its A-smoothing at $0$ to its B-smoothing at $1$, and the edge map is the multiplication $m$ for a merge or comultiplication $\\Delta$ for a split, multiplied by $(-1)^{\\sum_{i<j}v(c_i)}$ on the edge at $c_j$. Then the sum $d$ of all edge maps satisfies $d^2=0$.",
