          "id": "step-1.2",
          "claim": "In the positive curl, the $0$-state contributes $(q+q^{-1})^2$ and the $1$-state contributes $-q(q+q^{-1})$, because the state coordinate raises quantum degree by one and homological degree by one. Hence $\\chi_q^{\\mathrm{raw}}(U_+)=(q+q^{-1})^2-q(q+q^{-1})=1+q^{-2}=q^{-1}(q+q^{-1})$. In the negative curl, the $0$-state contributes $q+q^{-1}$ and the $1$-state contributes $-q(q+q^{-1})^2$. Hence $\\chi_q^{\\mathrm{raw}}(U_-)=(q+q^{-1})-q(q+q^{-1})^2=-q^3-q=-q^2(q+q^{-1})$. These computations use only the state modules and gradings before the writhe normalization.",
