          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. For every smooth oriented knot $K\\subset S^3$, let $B^4=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^4:\\lVert x\\rVert^2\\le1\\}$ with boundary $S^3$. The oriented connected sum $K\\#K^\\dagger$ bounds a smooth properly embedded disk $D\\subset B^4$ for which the squared radial function $\\rho(x)=\\lVert x\\rVert^2$ restricts to a Morse function on the interior of $D$ with all critical points of index $0$ or $1$.",
