            "4.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For each $p\\in K$, [F2] supplies a local inverse neighborhood for $E$. Form the set of all tuples consisting of a local trivialization, an open base set $O$ containing its center, and a radius $r>0$ such that $O\\times\\{v:\\|v\\|<r\\}$ lies in that injectivity neighborhood. These base sets cover $K$. Compactness gives finitely many such tuples whose base sets $O_i$ cover $K$; their recorded radii have a positive finite minimum $r_0$. The tuples are collected as a set of all witnesses and only a finite subfamily is extracted, so no point-indexed choice is used.",
