          "claim": "Apply [F3] to the finite cover $\\{O_i\\}$ of the metric space $K$, obtaining $\\delta>0$. Choose $0<\\varepsilon<\\min\\{r_0,\\delta/3\\}$. If $E(p,v)=E(q,w)$ with $\\|v\\|,\\|w\\|<\\varepsilon$, then $\\|p-q\\|=\\|w-v\\|<2\\varepsilon<\\delta$. Thus $\\{p,q\\}$ lies in one $O_i$, and both $(p,v)$ and $(q,w)$ lie in the same recorded neighborhood where $E$ is injective; hence $(p,v)=(q,w)$. Every point of the radius-$\\varepsilon$ tube also lies in one of those local-diffeomorphism neighborhoods, so the restriction is an injective local diffeomorphism.",
