          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice. Let $P$ be a single arc in a disk and let $Z=P\\sqcup O$ add a small disjoint circle next to it. Let $m:Z\\to P$ merge the circle into the arc by an elementary saddle and let $\\Delta:P\\to Z$ be the reversed saddle. In the open Bar-Natan category the two normalized kink complexes $C_+=(Z\\{1\\}\\xrightarrow{m}P\\{2\\})$ in cochain degrees $0,1$, and $C_-=(P\\{-2\\}\\xrightarrow{\\Delta}Z\\{-1\\})$ in degrees $-1,0$, both have explicit internal degree zero strong deformation retractions onto the one-term complex $P$ in degree zero. These retractions are preserved by insertion into an arbitrary planar surrounding complex.",
