          "quote": "Assume countable choice. In the open Bar-Natan category on four boundary points of a rectangle, let $I$ be the vertical two-strand identity pairing and let $E$ be the pairing consisting of a top cap and bottom cup. Let $t:I\\to E$ and $s:E\\to I$ be the elementary saddle surfaces. Define the formal crossing complexes $K_+=(I\\{1\\}\\xrightarrow{t}E\\{2\\})$, in cochain degrees $0,1$, and $K_-=(E\\{-2\\}\\xrightarrow{s}I\\{-1\\})$, in degrees $-1,0$. Then both planar stackings $K_+K_-$ and $K_-K_+$ have explicit internal degree zero strong deformation retractions onto the one-term complex $I$ in degree zero, with no grading shift. All maps and homotopies can be inserted into an arbitrary planar surrounding complex. Consequently adjoining either of these crossing complexes preserves simplicity in both directions.",
