          "quote": "Assume countable choice. Assign to births, deaths and saddles their elementary formal surfaces, and to the Reidemeister kink, inverse-crossing and third-move constructions the explicit formal retractions specified below. Then the two sides of each Euclidean Morse movie relation MM11, MM12, MM13, MM14 and MM15 induce chain maps equal up to an overall sign. This includes both directions, reflected models, all compatible orientations, and insertion into a fixed planar surrounding complex. It asserts the five Morse movie identities for those choices; it asserts no spherical sweep-around identity.",
