          "quote": "Let $\\mathsf{Cob}_3$ be the additive monoidal category of oriented cobordisms before the S, T, and four-tube relations are imposed, and let $\\mathsf{Cob}_{BN}$ be its quotient by those relations. Suppose $F:\\mathsf{Cob}_3\\to\\mathsf{GrAb}$ is a symmetric monoidal functor to graded abelian groups and homogeneous maps, with a circle sent to $\\mathcal A=\\mathbb Z[X]/(X^2)$, a cup to $\\eta(1)=1$, a cap to $\\epsilon(1)=0,\\epsilon(X)=1$, a merge pair of pants to $m$, and a split pair of pants to $\\Delta(1)=1\\otimes X+X\\otimes1,\\ \\Delta(X)=X\\otimes X$. Then every sphere component is sent to zero, every disjoint torus component acts by multiplication by $2$, and the two sides of the four-tube relation induce the same map. Therefore $F$ factors through an additive monoidal functor on $\\mathsf{Cob}_{BN}$.",
