d goes from first top endpoint to third bottom endpoint, so its two crossings are the first two source factors and last two target factors. The remaining third source/first target crossing is the fixed internal crossing, positive in I–II and negative in III–IV. This specifies the physical variants without relying on an unlabelled picture or an omitted six-valent foam.",
