          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Apply [F2] to the two-point isotopy of step 1.1, starting at the cap level. The extended sphere isotopy transports the short cap arc through simple arcs on the intervening levels. Their union is an embedded strip because distinct levels are disjoint; adjoining the cap disk gives an embedded disk with boundary $a\\cup\\beta_0$ for a simple arc $\\beta_0\\subset S_c$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F2",
            "step 1.1",
