          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Let $\\gamma_0$ be the initial cap arc on the reference $S^2$, and let $f_r$ be the ambient isotopy from [F2] carrying its endpoint pair to the two intersection points on level $S_r$. The arc $f_c^{-1}(\\beta)$ is a simple arc with the same endpoints as $\\gamma_0$. Bigon elimination gives an isotopy $g_t$ of $S^2$, fixed at those endpoints, with $g_1(\\gamma_0)=f_c^{-1}(\\beta)$. Precompose the transported cap arc by $g_{\\lambda(r)}$ before applying $f_r$, where $\\lambda$ is zero near the cap level and increases smoothly to $1$ at $r=c$. Every $g_t$ fixes the reference endpoints, so the joining arcs still have the required endpoint tracks; at $r=c$ the joining arc is exactly $\\beta$. The union of this family with the cap disk is therefore an embedded disk bounded by $a\\cup\\beta$. Reversing height proves the lower-ball statement.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
