          "claim": "Apply [F1] and list the finitely many crossings of the resulting projection. Around each crossing choose a closed disk meeting the image in exactly two transverse arcs, with all such disks pairwise disjoint. Subdivide the remaining compact arcs into finitely many subarcs contained in planar coordinate disks where each arc is a graph over a line interval and where nonincident pieces are separated. Compactness and finiteness give a positive minimum for the separations between the disjoint pieces.",
