          "source": "lem-seifert-matrices-differ-rank-one-under-crossing-change",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $D_+$ and $D_-$ be finite regular oriented diagrams that agree outside one crossing neighborhood and differ inside it by switching which branch is over. Let $V_+$ and $V_-$ be the Seifert matrices obtained from their oriented disk-and-band surfaces. There are corresponding integral bases in which either $V_+=V_-$ or $V_+-V_-=\\pm vv^T$ for some integral column vector $v$. In particular, $\\operatorname{rank}(V_+-V_-)\\le1$.",
