        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-rank-one-hermitian-signature-perturbation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $A$ and $B$ be Hermitian forms on the same finite-dimensional complex vector space, and suppose that the linear map representing $A-B$ has rank at most one. Then $|\\operatorname{sign}(A)-\\operatorname{sign}(B)|\\le 2$, where the signature is the number of positive eigenvalues minus the number of negative eigenvalues, with multiplicity and with zero eigenvalues omitted.",
          "uses": [
