          "claim": "Flatten each boundary chart, apply the local half-space trace lift, and patch the finitely many chart lifts with a smooth partition. The resulting $Ef\\in H^1(M)$ has trace $f$ and norm bounded by $C\\|f\\|_{H^{1/2}(\\partial M)}$ by [F5]. For $h\\in L^2(M)$ take $G(z)=-\\int_Mh\\overline z\\,dV_g-a_\\gamma(Ef,z)$ in step 2.1 and set $v=Ef+w$. Then $v$ has trace $f$ and satisfies the weak equation. If $v_1,v_2$ are two such solutions, their difference $w$ lies in $H_0^1$ and $a_\\gamma(w,w)=0$; since $\\gamma\\geq\\gamma_*>0$, $\\nabla w=0$, and step 1.1 gives $w=0$.",
