        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-ip-sobolev-spaces-on-compact-riemannian-domain",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice.\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be a compact smooth Riemannian manifold with smooth boundary, with no orientability assumption. Fix a finite smooth atlas of interior and boundary charts and a smooth partition of unity subordinate to it. For an integer $k\\geq0$, define $H^k(M)$ as the completion of $C^\\infty(M)$ in the sum of the Euclidean $W^{k,2}$ norms of the localized coordinate representatives; derivatives in a boundary chart are taken on the corresponding half-space. Define $H_0^1(M)$ as the closure of $C_c^\\infty(M^\\circ)$ in $H^1(M)$. Define $H^{1/2}(\\partial M)$ by the fixed finite boundary atlas and partition of unity, using the Euclidean fractional Slobodeckij space $W^{1/2,2}(\\mathbb R^{n-1})$ for each localized representative. Define $H^{-1/2}(\\partial M)$ as the continuous dual of $H^{1/2}(\\partial M)$ with the Riemannian boundary density pairing. These are the fixed-atlas norms used on this page; no atlas-independence assertion is part of this definition.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
