          "source": "thm-complex-hahn-banach-norm-preserving-extension",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $X$ be a complex normed space, let $M \\subseteq X$ be a linear subspace, and\nlet $f_0:M \\to \\mathbb{C}$ be a bounded complex linear functional. Then there\nexists a bounded complex linear functional $F:X \\to \\mathbb{C}$ such that\n$F|_M=f_0$ and $\\|F\\|=\\|f_0\\|$.",
