          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $(M,g)$ be a compact connected smooth Riemannian domain with nonempty smooth boundary and no orientability assumption, and let $\\gamma\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$ satisfy $\\gamma>0$. There is a constant $C_P>0$ such that $\\|w\\|_{L^2(M)}\\leq C_P\\|\\nabla_gw\\|_{L^2(M)}$ for every $w\\in H_0^1(M)$. For every $h\\in L^2(M)$ and $f\\in H^{1/2}(\\partial M)$ there is a unique $v\\in H^1(M)$ with trace $f$ satisfying $\\int_M\\gamma\\,g(\\nabla_gv,\\nabla_g\\overline z)\\,dV_g=-\\int_Mh\\overline z\\,dV_g$ for every $z\\in H_0^1(M)$. If $h$ and $f$ are smooth, this weak solution is smooth up to the boundary.",
