          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $(M,g)$ be a transversally anisotropic product domain, let $q\\in C^\\infty(\\overline M,\\mathbb R)$, and let $\\varphi=\\sigma x_1$ for $\\sigma\\in\\{-1,1\\}$. For $0<h\\leq h_0$ define\n$$P_{\\varphi,h,q}=e^{\\varphi/h}h^2(-\\Delta_g+q)e^{-\\varphi/h}.$$\nThere is a constant $C$ such that every $w\\in C_c^\\infty(M^\\circ)$ satisfies\n$$\\|w\\|_{L^2(M)}\\leq Ch^{-1}\\|P_{\\varphi,h,q}w\\|_{L^2(M)}.$$\nMoreover, for every $F\\in L^2(M)$ there is an $R\\in L^2(M)$ solving $P_{\\varphi,h,q}R=F$ in distributions on $M^\\circ$ and satisfying\n$$\\|R\\|_{L^2(M)}\\leq Ch^{-1}\\|F\\|_{L^2(M)}.$$\nNo boundary trace is prescribed for $R$.",
