          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Since $M_0$ is a surface, choose two unit directions $v_1,v_2\\in S_pM_0$ with $v_2\\ne\\pm v_1$. Nontrapping extends each geodesic through $p$ in both directions to a boundary-to-boundary segment, and strict convexity makes its boundary intersections nontangential. Their distinct tangent lines make the segments transverse at $p$. If they met again at a distinct point $z$, the two different subsegments from $p$ to $z$ would violate the unique-geodesic conclusion of [F5]. Thus the only intersection is $p$.",
