          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Fix unit tangent vectors $e_1,e_2$ at the crossing and their normal linear forms $\\ell_1,\\ell_2$ on the tangent plane. Their determinant has absolute value $|\\sin\\angle(e_1,e_2)|$. The normalized Gaussian\n$$\\frac{\\tau}{\\pi}e^{-\\tau(\\ell_1(y)^2+\\ell_2(y)^2)}$$\nhas integral $c=|\\sin\\angle(e_1,e_2)|^{-1}>0$, by the linear substitution $z_j=\\sqrt\\tau\\,\\ell_j(y)$. Choose this unit Gaussian normalization for the constant in the statement. This calculation fixes $c$ and does not claim estimates for any exact-solution beam remainders.",
