          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ip-cubic-dn-third-linearization-identity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice.\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be a compact smooth Riemannian domain with smooth boundary, let $q\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$, and let $\\Lambda_q^{\\rm NL}$ be the small-data nonlinear Dirichlet-to-Neumann map for $-\\Delta_g u+qu^3=0$. For smooth boundary directions $h_1,h_2,h_3,h_4$, let $v_j$ be the harmonic solution with boundary value $h_j$. If\n$$w_{123}=\\left.\\partial_{\\epsilon_1}\\partial_{\\epsilon_2}\\partial_{\\epsilon_3}u_\\epsilon\\right|_{\\epsilon=0},$$\nwhere $u_\\epsilon$ has boundary value $\\epsilon_1h_1+\\epsilon_2h_2+\\epsilon_3h_3$, then\n$$-\\Delta_gw_{123}+6qv_1v_2v_3=0,\\qquad w_{123}|_{\\partial M}=0,$$\nand\n$$\\left\\langle (D^3\\Lambda_q^{\\rm NL})_0[h_1,h_2,h_3],h_4\\right\\rangle =6\\int_Mq\\,v_1v_2v_3\\overline{v_4}\\,dV_g.$$",
          "uses": [
