        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-ip-intersecting-gaussian-beam-four-factor-limit",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice.\n\nLet $M\\Subset\\mathbb R\\times M_0^\\circ$ be a three-dimensional transversally anisotropic product domain with compact connected simple surface transversal $(M_0,g_0)$. For every $p\\in M_0^\\circ$ choose two nontangential unit-speed geodesic segments $\\gamma_1,\\gamma_2$ meeting transversely at $p$ and nowhere else. For every $\\xi\\in\\mathbb R$ and every $Q\\in C^\\infty(\\overline M)$, there are four exact harmonic solutions $u_{\\tau,1}^+,u_{\\tau,1}^-,u_{\\tau,2}^+,u_{\\tau,2}^-\\in H^1(M)$, with no prescribed boundary values, such that\n$$\\lim_{\\tau\\to\\infty}\\int_MQ(x_1,x')u_{\\tau,1}^+u_{\\tau,1}^-u_{\\tau,2}^+u_{\\tau,2}^-\\,dV_g =c(p,\\gamma_1,\\gamma_2)\\int_{I_p}e^{-i\\xi x_1}Q(x_1,p)\\,dx_1,$$\nwhere $I_p=\\{x_1\\in\\mathbb R:(x_1,p)\\in M^\\circ\\}$ and $c(p,\\gamma_1,\\gamma_2)>0$ is the nonzero Gaussian normalization divided by $|\\sin\\angle(\\dot\\gamma_1(p),\\dot\\gamma_2(p))|$.",
