          "source": "lem-ip-conductivity-liouville-transform-and-dn-conjugacy",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice.\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be a compact smooth Riemannian domain with smooth boundary, let $\\gamma\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$ be strictly positive, put $\\rho=\\sqrt{\\gamma}$, and define $q=(\\Delta_g\\rho)/\\rho$. If $v$ solves $\\operatorname{div}_g(\\gamma\\nabla_gv)=0$ and $u=\\rho v$, then $u$ solves $(-\\Delta_g+q)u=0$. The potential $q$ has trivial Dirichlet kernel. For boundary data $f=v|_{\\partial M}$, with $\\rho_b=\\rho|_{\\partial M}$ and the physical flux convention $\\Lambda_\\gamma f=\\gamma\\partial_{\\nu_{\\rm out}}v|_{\\partial M}$, the exact boundary relation is\n$$\\Lambda_\\gamma f=\\rho_b\\Lambda_q(\\rho_b f)-\\rho_b(\\partial_{\\nu_{\\rm out}}\\rho)|_{\\partial M}f.$$",
          "uses": [
