          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A transversally anisotropic product domain of dimension $n\\geq3$ is a compact connected smooth $n$-dimensional Riemannian domain $(M,g)$ with smooth boundary, together with a compact connected smooth $(n-1)$-dimensional Riemannian manifold with boundary $(M_0,g_0)$ and an isometric embedding of $(M,g)$ as a smooth domain compactly contained in $(\\mathbb R\\times M_0^\\circ,dx_1^2\\oplus g_0)$. The coordinate $x_1$ on $\\mathbb R$ is the distinguished Euclidean coordinate; $M_0$ is the transversal manifold. All Laplacians use $\\Delta_g=\\operatorname{div}_g\\nabla_g$. Neither $M$ nor $M_0$ is assumed orientable. A positive smooth conformal factor is not included in this definition; claims using a conformally related metric must state and prove the required conformal transformation separately.",
