          "quote": "Let $(I,A,D,P,P^{\\vee},q)$ be a symmetrizable Cartan datum for a quantum group ([[def-symmetrizable-cartan-datum-for-a-quantum-group]]) and put $q_i=q^{d_i}$. Write $K_i:=K_{d_i h_i}$ and $K_i^{-1}:=K_{-d_i h_i}$. Let $V$ be the $\\mathbb Q(q)$-vector space with basis the symbols $\\{E_i,F_i\\}_{i\\in I}\\cup\\{K_h\\}_{h\\in P^{\\vee}}$, and let $T:=T(V)$ be its free unital associative $\\mathbb Q(q)$-algebra ([[def-tensor-algebra-of-a-vector-space]], [[thm-universal-property-of-the-tensor-algebra]]). Let $I_{\\mathrm{DJ}}$ be the two-sided ideal of $T$ generated by ([[def-generated-and-principal-ideals]]) the following relations:\n\n$$K_0-1,\\qquad K_hK_{h'}-K_{h+h'}\\qquad(h,h'\\in P^{\\vee});$$\n\n$$K_hE_i-q^{\\langle\\alpha_i,h\\rangle}E_iK_h,\\qquad K_hF_i-q^{-\\langle\\alpha_i,h\\rangle}F_iK_h\\qquad(h\\in P^{\\vee},\\ i\\in I);$$\n\n$$E_iF_j-F_jE_i-\\delta_{ij}\\frac{K_i-K_i^{-1}}{q_i-q_i^{-1}}\\qquad(i,j\\in I);$$\n\n$$\\mathrm{Serre}^+_{ij}:=\\sum_{r=0}^{1-a_{ij}}(-1)^r\\binom{1-a_{ij}}{r}_iE_i^{1-a_{ij}-r}E_jE_i^r,\\qquad \\mathrm{Serre}^-_{ij}:=\\sum_{r=0}^{1-a_{ij}}(-1)^r\\binom{1-a_{ij}}{r}_iF_i^{1-a_{ij}-r}F_jF_i^r\\qquad(i\\ne j),$$\n\nwhere the Gaussian binomials are those of [[def-quantum-integers-factorials-and-divided-powers-at-q-i]]. The **Drinfeld-Jimbo quantized enveloping algebra** is\n\n$$U_q(\\mathfrak g):=T/I_{\\mathrm{DJ}}$$\n\n([[def-quotient-ring]]), with $E_i,F_i,K_h$ denoting the images of the generators. In this quotient, $K_i^{-1}$ is the two-sided inverse of $K_i$.\n\nIt is graded by the root lattice $Q=\\bigoplus_{i\\in I}\\mathbb Z\\alpha_i$ ([[def-kac-moody-root-lattice-height-and-positive-cone]]), with $\\deg E_i=\\alpha_i$, $\\deg F_i=-\\alpha_i$ and $\\deg K_h=0$; thus $U_q(\\mathfrak g)=\\bigoplus_{\\beta\\in Q}U_q(\\mathfrak g)[\\beta]$.\n\nFor every unital associative $\\mathbb Q(q)$-algebra $B$, any assignment of elements $E_i',F_i',K_h'\\in B$ satisfying these relations extends uniquely to a $\\mathbb Q(q)$-algebra homomorphism $U_q(\\mathfrak g)\\to B$ ([[thm-quotient-ring-universal-property]]).",
