          "source": "thm-the-drinfeld-jimbo-formulas-define-a-hopf-algebra",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $T$ and $I_{\\mathrm{DJ}}$ be the free $\\mathbb Q(q)$-algebra and defining ideal of [[def-drinfeld-jimbo-quantized-enveloping-algebra]], and write $K_i=K_{d_i h_i}$. Let $\\Delta:T\\to T\\otimes_{\\mathbb Q(q)}T$ and $\\varepsilon:T\\to\\mathbb Q(q)$ be the algebra homomorphisms determined by\n\n$$\\Delta(K_h)=K_h\\otimes K_h,\\quad \\Delta(E_i)=E_i\\otimes K_i^{-1}+1\\otimes E_i,\\quad \\Delta(F_i)=F_i\\otimes1+K_i\\otimes F_i,\\quad \\varepsilon(K_h)=1,\\quad\\varepsilon(E_i)=\\varepsilon(F_i)=0.$$\n\nLet $S:T\\to T$ be the $\\mathbb Q(q)$-linear algebra anti-homomorphism determined by\n\n$$S(K_h)=K_{-h},\\qquad S(E_i)=-E_iK_i,\\qquad S(F_i)=-K_i^{-1}F_i.$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\\Delta(I_{\\mathrm{DJ}})\\subseteq I_{\\mathrm{DJ}}\\otimes T+T\\otimes I_{\\mathrm{DJ}},\\qquad \\varepsilon(I_{\\mathrm{DJ}})=0,\\qquad S(I_{\\mathrm{DJ}})\\subseteq I_{\\mathrm{DJ}}.$$\n\nHence these maps descend to $U_q(\\mathfrak g)=T/I_{\\mathrm{DJ}}$ and make it a Hopf algebra over $\\mathbb Q(q)$ ([[def-bialgebra-counit-and-antipode]]): $\\Delta$ is coassociative, $\\varepsilon$ is a counit, and\n\n$$m(S\\otimes\\operatorname{id})\\Delta=\\eta\\circ\\varepsilon=m(\\operatorname{id}\\otimes S)\\Delta.$$\n\nThe antipode $S$ is unique for this multiplication, unit, coproduct and counit ([[lem-an-antipode-is-unique]]), and its square satisfies\n\n$$S^2(E_i)=q_i^{-2}E_i,\\qquad S^2(F_i)=q_i^{2}F_i,\\qquad S^2(K_h)=K_h.$$",
