          "source": "lem-colored-jones-generic-quotient-is-laurent",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. For every integer $N\\ge1$ and every finite braid word $\\beta$ on $b\\ge1$ strands whose closure is a knot, the normalized generic quotient\n$$\\lambda_N^{-w(\\beta)}\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}(G_N^{\\otimes b}\\rho_N(\\beta))}{d_N}$$\nbelongs to $\\mathbb Z[A^4,A^{-4}]$. Consequently there is a unique $J_N(K;q)\\in\\mathbb Z[q,q^{-1}]$ whose substitution $q=A^4$ equals that quotient. It is independent of the braid representative, has $J_N(\\bigcirc;q)=1$, and agrees with the normalized colored Jones convention of Murakami’s explicit matrix definition in the variable $q$. Its value at every nonzero complex $q$, in particular $q_N=e^{2\\pi i/N}$, means evaluation of this Laurent polynomial; it never means division by the specialized quantum dimension.",
