          "quote": "Let $A$ be indeterminate, $F=\\mathbb Q(A)$, $q_K=A^2$, and $q_L=A^{-2}$. For every integer $N\\ge1$, the concrete module, finite $R$ series, duality, pivotal comparison $G_N$, and twist $\\lambda_N$ in the normalized colored Jones definition are admissible ribbon data. More precisely, take the $F$-linear category generated by all those modules under finite tensor products, chosen contragredient duals, finite direct sums, and images of module-idempotents, with all module maps as morphisms. Its braiding on weight vectors is the finite series\n$$R_{X,Y}=D_{X,Y}\\sum_{r\\ge0}q_K^{r(r-1)/2}\\frac{(q_K-q_K^{-1})^r}{[r]!}E_X^r\\otimes F_Y^r,\\qquad D_{X,Y}(x_h\\otimes y_k)=A^{hk}x_h\\otimes y_k.$$\nThe sum is finite on each pair. Its pivotal comparison on weight $h$ is $(-1)^h q_K^h$, and its twist on $V_N$ is $(-1)^{N-1}A^{N^2-1}I$. These give natural invertible braidings with both hexagons, both duality snakes, the balancing identity and dual compatibility of twist. In particular all colors $N$, rather than a fixed bounded range of colors, are covered.",
