          "claim": "Put $E=\\overline{W\\setminus N}$, $C=A\\times S^1$, and $E_i=E\\cap S_i^3$, $N_i=N\\cap S_i^3$, $C_i=C\\cap S_i^3$. The supplied product identifies $N$ with $S^1\\times I\\times D^2$, $N_i$ with $S^1\\times\\{i\\}\\times D^2$, $C$ with $S^1\\times I\\times S^1$, and $C_i$ with its endpoint torus. Attach $F=D^2\\times S^1\\times I$ along $C$, identifying its disk-boundary circle with the annulus longitude and its other circle with the normal meridian. Each endpoint boundary is then $E_i$ filled by $F_i=D^2\\times S^1\\times\\{i\\}$ along the preferred longitude, precisely $M(K_i)$ by [F1]. The common annular-side collar gives a manifold after gluing, with the same smooth or topological category as the supplied data; in the smooth case round the product corners. This constructs $V=E\\cup_C F$ with the prescribed oriented ends.",
