        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-amenable-folner-kernel-approximation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Work under the standing AC convention for finite von Neumann modules. Let $G$ be a countable discrete amenable group, so that for every finite $S\\subseteq G$ and $\\varepsilon>0$ there is a nonempty finite $F\\subseteq G$ with $|SF\\setminus F|<\\varepsilon|F|$. Let $B\\in M_{m,n}(\\mathbb CG)$ act by left convolution on $\\ell^2(G)^n$. The Hilbert closure of $\\ker(B:(\\mathbb CG)^n\\to(\\mathbb CG)^m)$ is the full Hilbert kernel of $B$. More precisely, if the finite coefficient support of $B$, together with the identity, is contained in $S$, and $K_F$ is the space of vectors in that kernel supported in $F$, then, writing $d=\\tau_n(P_{\\ker B})$ and $r=\\tau_m(P_{\\overline{\\operatorname{im}B}})=n-d$,\n$$n|F|-r|SF|\\le\\dim_{\\mathbb C}K_F\\le d|F|.$$\nThe closure of the right $\\mathcal N G$-span of the algebraic kernel is therefore the full Hilbert kernel, and the quotient of the algebraic $\\mathcal N G$-kernel by that span has dimension zero.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
