          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "First let $K\\subseteq R^n$ be generated by finitely many columns, and let $B:R^s\\to R^n$ be the corresponding matrix map onto $K$. Right exactness of tensor products identifies $K\\otimes_R A$ with $A^s/\\operatorname{im}((\\ker_R B)\\otimes_R A)$. The kernel of its natural map to $A^n$ is therefore $\\ker_A B/\\operatorname{im}((\\ker_R B)\\otimes_R A)$. This quotient has dimension zero by [F3]. The tensor-product identifications follow directly from the presentation $\\ker_R B\\to R^s\\to K\\to0$: relations among the chosen generators are exactly the elements of $\\ker_R B$.",
