          "source": "thm-topological-lifted-half-pairs-force-amenable-signature-defect-zero",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $V$ be a compact connected oriented topological four-manifold with a supplied collar and connected boundary $M$, and choose a based loop $\\mu\\subset M$ such that\n$$H_1(M;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z[\\mu],\\qquad H_1(M;\\mathbb Z)\\xrightarrow{\\cong}H_1(V;\\mathbb Z),\\qquad H_2(V;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z^{2r}.$$\nPut $\\pi=\\pi_1(V)$, take $n\\ge0$, and supply classes $x_i,y_i\\in H_2(V;\\mathbb Z[\\pi/\\pi^{(n)}])$, $1\\le i\\le r$, satisfying $\\lambda_n(x_i,x_j)=0$ and $\\lambda_n(x_i,y_j)=\\delta_{ij}$. Supply classes $\\widetilde x_i\\in H_2(V;\\mathbb Z[\\pi/\\pi^{(n+1)}])$ mapping to $x_i$ with $\\lambda_{n+1}(\\widetilde x_i,\\widetilde x_j)=0$. These are actual lifted half-pair data on the supplied manifold; existence of such a manifold or lifts is not asserted.\n\nLet $k=\\mathbb Q$ or $\\mathbb F_p$ for any prime $p$. Let $G$ be a discrete amenable group in $D(k)$ with $G^{(n+1)}=1$, and supply $\\phi:\\pi\\to G$ such that $\\phi(\\mu)$ has infinite order. Use its based regular unitary local system and the finite-projective topological intersection convention. Then\n$$\\operatorname{sign}^{(2)}_G(V,\\phi)=0=\\operatorname{sign}(V),$$\nso its actual bounding signature defect is zero. This applies to the full supplied locally flat topological category as well as smooth manifolds; no finite CW type, smoothing, closed-manifold ordinary-versus-$L^2$ index equality or rho bordism-independence theorem is assumed. If a separately applicable bordism-independence result identifies a rho invariant with this bounding defect, that invariant is consequently zero.",
