          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-unimodular-infection-tower-data-force-mixed-derived-meridian-survival",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix $n\\ge1$, $q\\ge1$ and finitely many marked smooth infection towers $J_{a,j+1}=P_{a,j}(J_{a,j})$, $1\\le a\\le q$, $0\\le j<n$, whose unknotted axes $\\eta_{a,j}$ have winding zero. Supply compatible finite disk-band models, ambient roundings, peripheral product tubes and paths for all their knots and patterns. Let $E_{a,j}$ be their actual standard infection cobordisms. Supply a compact connected oriented topological four-manifold $W_n$ with disjoint marked collared boundary components $M(J_{a,n})$, allowing orientation reversals, such that $H_1(W_n;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z$ and each positive meridian $\\mu_{a,n}$ represents either generator. Form the actual collared adjunctions\n$$W_j=W_{j+1}\\cup_{\\bigsqcup_aM(J_{a,j+1})}\\bigsqcup_aE_{a,j},\\qquad G_j=\\pi_1(W_j),$$\nwith each piece oriented to make the attachment oriented; other boundary components are allowed. Based paths through these finite gluings are supplied.\n\nFix an odd prime $p$. Define the mixed series by $P^0G=G$ and\n$$P^{i+1}G=\\ker\\{P^iG\\longrightarrow(P^iG/[P^iG,P^iG])\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}R_i\\},\\qquad R_0=\\cdots=R_{n-1}=\\mathbb Q,\\quad R_n=\\mathbb F_p.$$\nFor $0\\le j<n$ set $s_j=n-j$, $\\Gamma_j=G_{j+1}/P^{s_j}G_{j+1}$, and $k_j=\\mathbb Q$ if $j>0$, $k_0=\\mathbb F_p$. Let $A_j=k_j[\\Gamma_j]$ and let $K_j$ be its Ore fraction division ring, with standard involution. Use on $W_{j+1}$ the quotient coefficient homomorphism and based standard parallel Hermitian structure.\n\nAssume for every $a,j$ that the classical axis class on $M(P_{a,j}(U))$ has nonzero self-pairing over $k_j[t,t^{-1}]$. Assume also the following actual intersection data for each $j$: there is a finite list $\\ell_1,\\ldots,\\ell_{m_j},d_1,\\ldots,d_{m_j}\\in H_2(W_{j+1};A_j)$ with\n$$\\lambda(\\ell_a,\\ell_b)=0,\\qquad\\lambda(\\ell_a,d_b)=\\lambda(d_b,\\ell_a)=\\delta_{ab},\\qquad\\dim_{K_j}\\operatorname{coker}\\{H_2(\\partial W_{j+1};K_j)\\to H_2(W_{j+1};K_j)\\}\\le2m_j.$$\nExistence of these intersection data is a hypothesis. Then for every $1\\le a\\le q$ and $0\\le j\\le n$ the actual meridian satisfies\n$$\\mu_{a,j}\\in P^{n-j}G_j,\\qquad[\\mu_{a,j}]\\ne0\\text{ in }P^{n-j}G_j/P^{n-j+1}G_j.$$\nIts image has infinite order for $j>0$ and order exactly $p$ for $j=0$.\n\nA sufficient condition for all the displayed intersection-data hypotheses is that $W_n$ is obtained by finitely many marked standard connected-sum and infection adjunctions from one compact connected oriented topological manifold $V$ with boundary a knot zero surgery, $H_1(V;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z$, $H_2(V;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z^{2r}$, and exactly $r$ supplied integral pairs $x_1,\\ldots,x_r,y_1,\\ldots,y_r\\in H_2(V;\\mathbb Z[\\pi_1(V)/\\pi_1(V)^{(n)}])$ satisfying $\\lambda(x_i,x_j)=0$ and $\\lambda(x_i,y_j)=\\delta_{ij}$. The stipulated meridian generator condition on $W_n$ remains part of the hypotheses. In this sufficient condition no existence of $V$ or of its pairs is asserted.\n\nIn particular, if all integral classical axis self-values are nonzero, their rational hypotheses hold automatically, and the bottom prime hypothesis holds for all odd primes outside an explicitly finite exceptional set. The integral self-values may be supplied in the knot exteriors: the actual exterior-to-surgery identifications carry them to the values used here. This theorem applies in the supplied topological and smooth scopes without a choice axiom; it does not assert that a topological concordance relation supplies the hypothesized intersection data.",
