          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P$ be a smooth winding-zero satellite pattern with unknotted axis $\\eta$ and nonzero rational classical axis self-pairing. Fix $n\\ge1$ and a smooth knot $J$. Put $J^1_0=J^2_0=J$, $J^0_0=J\\#J$ and $J^a_{h+1}=P(J^a_h)$ for $0\\le a\\le2$, $0\\le h<n$. Supply finite disk-band models and local ambient roundings, peripheral product tubes and paths for this finite collection and $P(U)$. Put $K=J^1_n\\#J^2_n\\#(-J^0_n)$, where the inverse knot uses the marked mirror-and-reverse convention. Supply a compact connected oriented topological four-manifold $V$ with collared boundary $M(K)$, with $H_1(M(K);\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(V;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z$ an isomorphism and $H_2(V;\\mathbb Z)=0$.\n\nLet $C$ be the actual standard connected-sum cobordism and put $W_n=V\\cup_{M(K)}C$, with other boundary $M(J^1_n)\\sqcup M(J^2_n)\\sqcup(-M(J^0_n))$. Recursively attach the actual three standard infection pieces, reversing the distinguished branch's orientation:\n$$W_h=W_{h+1}\\cup E_{1,h}\\cup E_{2,h}\\cup(-E_{0,h}).$$\nAll attachments are along their outgoing components, with supplied compatible collars and signed-surgery markings preserving the positive meridian and the zero slope. Fix coherent base paths through these finite pieces.\n\nThere is an explicit quotient homomorphism $\\phi:\\pi_1(W_0)\\twoheadrightarrow G$ with $G$ PTFA of derived length at most $n+1$, in $D(\\mathbb Q)$ and with finite Folner sets. The meridian of $K$ has infinite order in $G$. Its restriction to $\\pi_1(M(J^0_0))$ is trivial. Each restriction to $\\pi_1(M(J^i_0))$, $i=1,2$, is trivial or has infinite cyclic image, and at least one is infinite cyclic.\n\nThere is also the following finite-prime variant. Fix an odd prime $p$ for which the pattern-axis classical self-value over $\\mathbb F_p[t,t^{-1}]$ is nonzero. Then there is such a quotient of derived length at most $n+1$ in $D(\\mathbb F_p)$, with finite Folner sets and with the meridian of $K$ still of infinite order, whose