          "quote": "Let $R$ be an associative unital ring with $1\\ne0$ and no zero divisors, embedded as a unital subring in a division ring $K$, put $N=K/R$ as a right $R$-module, and let $C_*$ be a right $R$-module chain complex concentrated in nonnegative degrees. Supply an identification $C_0=R$. If the right ideal $\\operatorname{im}(d_1)$ is principal, restriction to cycles gives an isomorphism\n$$H^1(\\operatorname{Hom}_R(C_*,N))\\xrightarrow{\\sim}\\operatorname{Hom}_R(H_1(C_*),N).$$\nNeither a principal ideal domain hypothesis on $R$ nor a choice principle is required.",
