        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-smooth-integral-filtration-is-compatible-with-deep-axis-infection",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. For an integer $h\\ge0$ or a half-integer $h=n+1/2$, let $\\mathcal F_h^{\\mathrm{sm}}$ be the set of smooth concordance classes whose preferred-longitude zero surgery bounds an integral $h$-solution. Use the integral lifted-pair definition: $H_1$ is identified with the boundary meridian $\\mathbb Z$, $H_2$ is free of rank $2r$, there are exactly $r$ zero/unit pairs over the indicated derived quotient, and at a half level the isotropic classes lift one further derived stage. Every smooth pattern preserves smooth knot concordance. Then $\\mathcal F_h^{\\mathrm{sm}}$ is a subgroup of smooth knot concordance, $\\mathcal F_{h'}^{\\mathrm{sm}}\\subseteq\\mathcal F_h^{\\mathrm{sm}}$ for $h'\\ge h$, and every smooth knot lies in $\\mathcal F_0^{\\mathrm{sm}}$.\n\nMore specifically, let $R$ be a smooth slice knot and let $\\eta$ be a supplied unknotted infection axis in its exterior with $[\\eta]\\in\\pi_1(S^3\\setminus R)^{(k)}$, where $k\\ge1$. For every smooth knot $J$, the infection $R(\\eta,J)$ has an actual smooth integral $k$-solution. All constructions use finite smooth disk-band, peripheral product-tube, collar and path data; these data may be chosen under the stated AC.\n\nConsequently, if $P$ is a winding-zero smooth pattern, then for every $k\\ge1$ and every smooth knot $J$,\n$$[P^k(J)]-[P^k(U)]\\in\\mathcal F_k^{\\mathrm{sm}},\\qquad \\langle P^k(\\mathcal C_{\\mathrm{sm}})\\rangle\\subseteq\\mathcal F_k^{\\mathrm{sm}}+\\langle[P^k(U)]\\rangle.$$\nNo locally flat tubular neighborhood or TOP realization theorem is assumed or concluded.",
