        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "A cochain $f:C_1\\to N$ is a cocycle precisely when $f(B_1)=0$. Restricting to $Z_1$ therefore induces a map $H_1=Z_1/B_1\\to N$. A coboundary $g d_1$ vanishes on $Z_1$, so this induces the stated well-defined map $\\kappa$. It is onto if every map $Z_1\\to N$ vanishing on $B_1$ extends to $C_1$. It is injective if every map $B_0\\to N$ extends to $C_0$: indeed a cocycle restricting to zero on $Z_1$ factors uniquely through $d_1:C_1\\to B_0$, and such an extension expresses it as a coboundary.",
