          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "By steps 2.1 and 3.1, the adjoint of any sesquilinear pairing on $TH_1(M;\\Lambda)$ with target $K/\\Lambda$ has nonzero source and zero target, and therefore is not an isomorphism. This includes the coefficient Bockstein–duality pairing whenever expressed in those conventions. Together with step 2.2 this refutes the asserted implication. Every object and calculation is explicit and finite; no choice assumption is needed.",
