          "claim": "Dropping all coefficients outside $H$ defines an $A$-bimodule map $p:B\\to A$ with $p(1)=1$: multiplication by a group element of $H$ on either side preserves both $H$ and its complement. Balancing therefore defines $\\rho_M:M\\otimes_A B\\to M$, $\\rho_M(m\\otimes b)=mp(b)$. It is right-$A$ linear and satisfies $\\rho_M(m\\otimes1)=m$. This proves the split unit assertion. If $f\\otimes1=0$ for a module homomorphism $f$, then $f(m)=\\rho_N((f\\otimes1)(m\\otimes1))=0$ for each $m$; the functor is faithful. Apply step 2.1 to the exact sequences defining cycles, boundaries and their quotient. It identifies tensor cycles with the kernel of the tensor differential, tensor boundaries with its image, and the tensor quotient with their quotient. The resulting map is $[z]\\otimes b\\mapsto[z\\otimes b]$, proving the natural homology assertion degree by degree. Replacing left cosets by right cosets gives the same finite-coordinate proof for left modules, and the same coefficient projection splits their unit map.",
