          "source": "lem-choice-free-low-degree-coefficient-bockstein-on-compact-manifolds",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $M$ be a compact connected Hausdorff manifold with a basepoint, and let $0\\to\\mathcal A\\xrightarrow{i}\\mathcal B\\xrightarrow{q}\\mathcal C\\to0$ be a short exact sequence of local systems of abelian groups on $M$. There is a natural coefficient Bockstein making the sequence\n$$H^1(M;\\mathcal B)\\xrightarrow{q_*}H^1(M;\\mathcal C)\\xrightarrow{\\beta}H^2(M;\\mathcal A)\\xrightarrow{i_*}H^2(M;\\mathcal B)$$\nexact at its two middle terms. In particular $\\beta$ is an isomorphism if $H^1(M;\\mathcal B)=H^2(M;\\mathcal B)=0$. No choice principle is assumed. If the local systems and maps have a commuting coefficient-ring action, the sequence and Bockstein respect it.",
          "uses": [
