        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-ptfa-augmentation-detects-projective-injectivity-without-choice",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a commutative field and $G$ a PTFA group. For every homomorphism $f:P\\to Q$ between projective right-$k[G]$ modules, if\n$$f\\otimes1:P\\otimes_{k[G]}k\\longrightarrow Q\\otimes_{k[G]}k$$\nis injective under the augmentation $k[G]\\to k$, then $f$ is injective. Projective means the lifting property for surjections, applied to right modules; it does not mean a supplied free basis. Thus this is the right-module defining property of Strebel's class $D(k)$. The left-module version holds too.\n\nMoreover, if $k[G]\\subseteq K$ is a supplied division ring of Ore fractions, every finite matrix $T$ over $k[G]$ satisfies\n$$\\operatorname{rank}_K(T\\otimes K)\\ge\\operatorname{rank}_k(\\varepsilon T).$$\nBoth assertions require no choice axiom. The group need not be finitely generated, its series need not be normal in all of $G$, and its successive extensions need not split.",
          "uses": [
