      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Choose a finite generating list for $P$, giving a surjection $\\pi:A^n\\to P$. Projectivity gives one section $s:P\\to A^n$. The matrix $E=s\\pi$ is idempotent, and after either base change $P$ identifies with the image of that idempotent. Put $r=\\operatorname{rank}_k E_k$. By [F1], $\\operatorname{rank}_K E_K\\ge r$ and $\\operatorname{rank}_K(1-E)_K\\ge n-r$. Idempotency gives the actual complementary decomposition $K^n=\\operatorname{im}E_K\\oplus\\operatorname{im}(1-E)_K$: every vector is the sum of its two displayed images, and their intersection is zero after applying $E_K$. Their dimensions therefore add to $n$, forcing equality in both inequalities. Hence $\\dim_K P_K=r=\\dim_k P_k$. Only one finite generating list and one projectivity section were used.",
