    "lem-ptfa-subgroup-scalar-extension-preserves-blanchfield-self-pairings": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-subgroup-group-ring-extension-is-faithfully-flat-and-preserves-fraction-quotients",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a commutative unital ring and $H\\le G$ a subgroup. Set $A=k[H]\\subseteq B=k[G]$. Extension $-\\otimes_A B$ on right modules is exact and faithful, and for each right $A$-module $M$ the map $m\\mapsto m\\otimes1$ is split injective as an $A$-module map. For every right-$A$ chain complex $C_*$, without a boundedness or finiteness assumption, there is the natural isomorphism\n$$H_i(C_*)\\otimes_A B\\cong H_i(C_*\\otimes_A B).$$\nThe corresponding left-module assertions hold with the tensor factors reversed.\n\nSuppose additionally that $A$ and $B$ have $1\\ne0$, no zero divisors and both Ore conditions, and are embedded in their right-fraction division rings $F$ and $K$, respectively. Then the inclusion $A\\to B$ extends uniquely to an injective ring map $F\\to K$. Under this identification,\n$$F\\cap B=A,\\qquad F/A\\longrightarrow K/B\\text{ is injective as an }A\\text{-bimodule map}.$$\nAll assertions require no choice principle, including when $G/H$ is infinite. No splitting of a group extension is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "4.1",
            "5.1",
            "6.1"
