      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Intersect a PTFA series of $G$ with $H$. Each successive intersection is normal in the next, and its quotient embeds in the corresponding torsion-free abelian quotient of $G$. Subgroups of a torsion-free abelian group are torsion-free and abelian, directly from the definitions. Thus $H$ is PTFA, without choosing a global transversal. By [F2] both group rings have the asserted fractions and involutions. Apply [F1] to identify $F$ with its subring in $K$ and obtain the injective map $j$. The inclusions preserve involution because they agree on every group element and on $k$, and the inverse of a fraction denominator is forced in both rings.",
