          "claim": "On a connected component use the finite-atlas based paths in [F3] for compatible fiber frames of all four coefficient systems. Their singular complexes are literally related by tensor base change on those generators. Hence [F1] gives $H_1(M;B)=H_1(M;A)\\otimes_A B$, with the split injective unit asserted there. By [F2], vanishing over $F$ means that every $x\\in H_1(M;A)$ has $xa=0$ for some nonzero $a\\in A$. The composite functor $-\\otimes_A B\\otimes_B K$ is exact by [F1, F2], and therefore commutes with chain homology. Every such $x$ dies after tensoring with $K$, since $x\\otimes z=(xa)\\otimes a^{-1}z=0$. Thus $H_1(M;K)=0$. The same localization criterion says both first homology modules in the Statement are entirely torsion over their respective coefficient rings.",
