          "source": "thm-finite-geometric-complex-chains-dominate-compact-manifold-chains-in-zf",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $L$ be a finite geometric simplicial complex with an ordered vertex set, and let $\\mathcal R$ be a local system of rank-one free right modules over an arbitrary unital ring $R$. Its finite simplicial chain complex $F_*(L;\\mathcal R)$ and intrinsic singular chain complex $C_*(L;\\mathcal R)$ admit $R$-linear chain maps\n$$P:C_*(L;\\mathcal R)\\to F_*(L;\\mathcal R),\\qquad J:F_*(L;\\mathcal R)\\to C_*(L;\\mathcal R)$$\nwith $PJ=1$ and an explicitly constructed chain homotopy $JP\\simeq1$. Choices of bases at its finitely many vertices make $F_*$ bounded finite-free.\n\nConsequently, for every compact connected Hausdorff topological manifold $M$, with boundary allowed, and every such local system supplied with a base-fiber identification with $R$, its nonnegative singular chain complex is free with a formula-specified basis and is $R$-linearly chain-homotopy dominated by a bounded finite-free complex. No choice principle, triangulation of $M$, or assertion of finite CW type for $M$ is assumed.",
