        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ptfa-integral-and-field-group-rings-have-compatible-ore-involutions",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\Gamma$ be PTFA and let $k$ be either $\\mathbb Z$ or a commutative field. The group ring $A=k[\\Gamma]$ has no zero divisors, satisfies both Ore conditions, and has a fraction division ring $K$ in which every element is both a right and a left fraction of elements of $A$. The involution $\\overline{\\sum c_g g}=\\sum c_g g^{-1}$ extends uniquely to an involutive anti-automorphism of $K$.\n\nEvery intermediate unital ring $A\\subseteq R\\subseteq K$ has no zero divisors, satisfies both Ore conditions, and has this same $K$ as its fraction division ring. If $R$ is stable under the extended involution, that involution restricts to $R$ and descends to its additive quotient $K/R$. None of these assertions requires a choice principle.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-topological-collaring-for-manifold-boundaries",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "If $M$ is a compact topological manifold with boundary $A=\\partial M$, there is an open neighborhood $V$ of $A$ and a homeomorphism\n$$c:A\\times[0,1)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}V,\\qquad c(x,0)=x.$$\nConsequently $A\\hookrightarrow M$ is an unbased cofibration, and $M\\setminus A\\hookrightarrow M$ is a homotopy equivalence. The manifold is Hausdorff and second countable by convention. All three conclusions require no AC.",
          "uses": [
            "2.2",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-compact-collared-manifold-local-coefficient-lefschetz-duality-in-zf",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a compact oriented Hausdorff topological $n$-manifold with boundary $A$ and a supplied boundary collar $c:A\\times[0,1)\\to W$. Let $\\mathcal L$ be a local system of abelian groups. Cap with the integral relative orientation class $z=[W,A]$ gives isomorphisms in every integer degree:\n$$H^p(W,A;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(W;\\mathcal L),\\qquad H^p(W;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(W,A;\\mathcal L).$$\nThe maps commute with every coefficient action commuting with transport, including noncommutative ring actions on the underlying abelian-group systems. No choice principle, smoothness, triangulation or finite CW structure is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "2.2",
            "4.1"
