        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-involutive-twisted-chain-duals-realize-local-coefficient-duality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(M,o)$ be a compact connected based Hausdorff manifold, let $R$ be an involutive unital ring, and supply a rank-one right-$R$ local system $\\mathcal R$ with an identification $\\mathcal R_o=R$. Assume every based-loop monodromy is left multiplication by a unit $u$ satisfying $\\bar u=u^{-1}$. Equip the base fiber with the standard Hermitian form $h_o(a,b)=\\bar a b$. Transport extends this to a path-independent parallel Hermitian form $h$ on $\\mathcal R$. Put $C_*=C_*(M;\\mathcal R)$. For a right $R$-module $P$, write $\\overline P$ for its conjugate left module, with $r\\cdot\\bar p=\\overline{p\\bar r}$.\n\nThe left-$R$ cochain complex $\\operatorname{Hom}_R(C_*,R)$ is the intrinsic cochain complex of the left-$R$ local system with fiber $R$ and transport $a\\mapsto au^{-1}$. Relative to the supplied parallel Hermitian form, that local system is naturally isomorphic to $\\overline{\\mathcal R}$ by $\\bar v\\mapsto[w\\mapsto h(v,w)]$. The identifications are independent of unitary fiber frames; an arbitrary change of Hermitian structure is not asserted to preserve them. If $M$ is oriented, boundaryless and of dimension $n$, cap duality therefore gives\n$$H^p(\\operatorname{Hom}_R(C_*,R))\\cong\\overline{H_{n-p}(C_*)}.$$\nIf $R\\subseteq K$ is an embedding into an involutive division ring extending the involution, the same conclusion is valid for $K$, with $C_*\\otimes_R K$ in the homology target. If $R$ is involution-stable in $K$, the complex $\\operatorname{Hom}_R(C_*,K/R)$ is the corresponding intrinsic left-$R$ cochain complex with fiber $K/R$ and transport by right multiplication by $u^{-1}$. These identifications require no choice principle and commute with the coefficient maps $R\\to K\\to K/R$.",
          "uses": [
