      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Apply [F1] to the actual $k[G]$ singular complex of $W$ and to each of the finitely many boundary components. Tensoring the specified chain equivalences and homotopies with $k$ or $K$ preserves their equations. On singular generators augmentation sends every group transport to $1$, so these are exactly the ordinary $k$ and twisted $K$ chains. The bounded projective models show that all homology dimensions are finite. By [F2] their alternating homology dimensions are equal; denote the common number by $\\chi$. Apply [F1] over $k$ as well when needed. If a coefficient homomorphism is trivial, its actual singular $K$ complex is the constant singular $k$ complex tensored with $K$. Its bounded projective $k$ model is a bounded finite-dimensional vector-space complex; finite elimination splits it into its homology and contractible pairs. Tensoring those finite splittings with $K$ proves equality of all ordinary and $K$ Betti numbers in the trivial case, without a choice of a basis in an infinite vector space.",
