        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "For a connected space with nontrivial $\\phi$, $H_0(-;K)=0$: paths identify all point fibers with the base fiber in degree zero, and a based loop with image $g\\ne1$ imposes $(g-1)K=K$, because the nonzero element $g-1$ is invertible in $K$. This argument uses one path for each individual zero-cycle, not a simultaneous path selection. If the homomorphism is trivial, $H_0(-;K)=K$. For $W$ write $\\beta_i=\\dim_k H_i(W;k)$ and $b_i=\\dim_KH_i(W;K)$. If its homomorphism is nontrivial, $\\beta_0=1,b_0=0$, so [F2] gives $b_1\\le\\beta_1-1$. This uses the nonnegative bounded projective model from step 1.1, not an unproved finite CW structure.",
