          "id": "step-2-2",
          "claim": "Here is the exact rank formula for either coefficient system. Write $c_i$ for its dimensions on $W$ and $a_i$ for those on $M$. Finite projective models over the division field identify dual cohomology dimensions with homology dimensions by finite elimination, and [F3] therefore gives $H_i(W,M)$ dimension $c_{4-i}$ and boundary dimensions $a_i=a_{3-i}$. If $M$ is nonempty, $H_4(W)=0$: under relative duality it is degree-zero relative cohomology, whose parallel sections vanishing on the nonempty boundary vanish on connected $W$. The top of the pair sequence is then $$0\\to H_4(W,M)\\to H_3(M)\\to H_3(W)\\to H_3(W,M)\\to H_2(M)\\to H_2(W).$$ Successive image dimensions are $c_0$, $a_0-c_0$, $c_3-a_0+c_0$, and $c_1-c_3+a_0-c_0$. Hence the image of $H_2(M)\\to H_2(W)$ has dimension $a_1-c_1+c_3-a_0+c_0$, and its cokernel has dimension $$r_*=c_2-a_1+c_1-c_3+a_0-c_0=\\chi+2c_1-2c_0-a_1+a_0.$$ In the last equality $H_4(W)=0$ and higher homology vanishes by duality. If $M$ is empty, closed duality gives $c_4=c_0,c_3=c_1$ and $r_*=c_2$, yielding the same formula with $a_0=a_1=0$. Thus the formula is valid in both boundary cases.",
          "step": "2.2",
          "inputs": [
