        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-equivariant-intersection-pairings-are-preserved-by-collared-bordism-gluing",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W,X$ be compact oriented topological four-manifolds with supplied boundary collars and decompositions $\\partial W=A\\sqcup D$, $\\partial X=A\\sqcup B$. Glue their copies of $A$ by a supplied orientation-reversing identification, obtaining $Y=W\\cup_A X$ with $\\partial Y=D\\sqcup B$. Supply one ambient rank-one right-$R$ local system on $Y$, where $R$ is an involutive unital ring. On each connected component supply a base-fiber identification with $R$ and unitary monodromy, and use its transported standard Hermitian form. Use its restrictions and the induced orientations on $W,X$.\n\nFor the intersection pairings defined by inverse relative cap duality, passage to absolute cohomology and evaluation,\n$$\\lambda_Y(i_*p,i_*q)=\\lambda_W(p,q)\\qquad(p,q\\in H_2(W;R)).$$\nIn particular all isotropic and dual-pair identities for homology classes in $W$ persist under their inclusion in $Y$. The result applies to topological manifolds and requires no geometric surface transversality or choice principle.",
