          "source": "lem-relative-unitary-equivariant-intersection-pairing-is-hermitian",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a compact connected oriented topological four-manifold with supplied boundary collar, and let $R$ be an involutive unital ring. Supply a based rank-one right-$R$ local system $\\mathcal R$, a base-fiber identification with $R$, unitary monodromy and its parallel standard Hermitian form. For $p\\in H_2(W;\\mathcal R)$ let $a_p\\in H^2(W,\\partial W;\\mathcal R^\\vee)$ be the inverse cap-duality image of $\\bar p$, using the form to identify the intrinsic dual system with $\\overline{\\mathcal R}$. Define\n$$\\lambda(p,q)=\\langle j(a_p),q\\rangle,$$\nwhere $j$ forgets the relative condition and the last pairing is intrinsic cochain evaluation. Then\n$$\\lambda(p,q)=\\overline{\\lambda(q,p)}$$\nfor all $p,q$. In particular $\\lambda(\\ell_i,d_j)=\\delta_{ij}$ implies $\\lambda(d_j,\\ell_i)=\\delta_{ij}$. No choice axiom, triangulation or geometric transversality of surfaces in dimension four is required.",
