        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-ptfa-localized-boundary-intersection-rank-is-no-larger-than-ordinary-rank",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a compact connected oriented Hausdorff topological four-manifold and put $M=\\partial W$, allowing $M$ empty. Let $k$ be a commutative field, $G$ a PTFA group, and $\\phi:\\pi_1(W)\\to G$ a supplied coefficient homomorphism. Write $K$ for the fraction division ring of $k[G]$, with its standard involution, and use the induced rank-one right-coefficient systems. Suppose $\\dim_kH_1(M_j;k)=1$ for each connected component $M_j$ of $M$. Then\n$$\\dim_K\\operatorname{coker}\\{H_2(M;K)\\to H_2(W;K)\\}\\le\\dim_k\\operatorname{coker}\\{H_2(M;k)\\to H_2(W;k)\\}.$$\nAll dimensions in the formula are finite. No choice axiom, smoothness, triangulation, or supplied finite CW model of $W$ is assumed.",
