          "quote": "If $M$ is a compact topological manifold with boundary $A=\\partial M$, there is an open neighborhood $V$ of $A$ and a homeomorphism\n$$c:A\\times[0,1)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}V,\\qquad c(x,0)=x.$$\nConsequently $A\\hookrightarrow M$ is an unbased cofibration, and $M\\setminus A\\hookrightarrow M$ is a homotopy equivalence. The manifold is Hausdorff and second countable by convention. All three conclusions require no AC.",
