          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The factorization supplies an involution-preserving ring homomorphism $\\mathbb Z[\\Pi_s]\\to A$, and hence maps of all actual coefficient chain systems on $V$. Cap, dual-system identification and evaluation commute with this change of coefficients. Explicitly a dual cochain $f$ changes to $c\\otimes a\\mapsto\\rho(f(c))a$; balancing and the finite face formulas show compatibility with coboundaries and cap. Both relative cap maps are isomorphisms by [F5], so their inverse duality maps commute too. Thus the image classes on $V$ retain the displayed zero and unit pairings. The standard base vector $1$ gives compatible transported Hermitian structures before and after change of ring. Hermitian symmetry [F2] supplies the reverse cross-pairing $\\lambda_A(d_j,\\ell_i)=\\delta_{ij}$.",
