          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Write $M=\\partial W$. Under relative cap duality, the map $j:H^2(W,M;K^\\vee)\\to H^2(W;K^\\vee)$ corresponds to the intersection map on $H_2(W;K)$. This map is zero under the given boundary-generation hypothesis. Indeed, if $z=i_*b$ for $b\\in H_2(M;K)$, closed duality represents $\\bar b$ by a degree-one cohomology class on $M$. Its pair connector is the relative dual class of $\\bar z$, by the cap boundary identity, and its image under $j$ is zero by exactness. Every $z$ has this form by hypothesis. Thus $j=0$, with intrinsic dual systems identified using the supplied Hermitian form.",
