          "claim": "Extend $x$ by zero from $N$ to $H_1(M;R)$. Since it dies in $W$, the pair sequence supplies $a\\in H_2(W,M;R)$ with $\\partial a=x$. Absolute cap duality sends its conjugate to $u\\in H^2(W;R^\\vee)$, whose boundary restriction is the dual of $\\bar x$, by the signed cap boundary formula in degree two. The image of $x$ in $H_1(M;K)$ is zero: on selected components this is the assumed vanishing and on other components $x$ was zero. Hence $u_K|_M=0$. Pair exactness puts $u_K$ in the image of $j$, which is zero by step 1.1. Choose one $R^\\vee$-valued two-cocycle representing $u$. Since its image represents zero over $K$, one whole $K^\\vee$-valued one-cochain $b$ satisfies $\\delta b=u$. Its quotient $\\nu=b\\bmod R$ is a $(K/R)^\\vee$-valued cocycle on $W$, and on each selected component its coefficient Bockstein is the dual of $\\bar x$. This constructs a whole cochain, rather than choosing lifts of infinitely many quotient coefficients.",
