    "thm-winding-zero-infection-preserves-classical-blanchfield-pairings": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-standard-infection-cobordisms-have-boundary-generated-second-homology",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P\\cup\\eta$ be a smooth oriented two-component link in $S^3$ with unknotted axis $\\eta$, and let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot. Supply disjoint closed product tubes and positive meridian/preferred zero-linking-longitude peripheral data for the knots and axis. Write $P(K)$ for infection along $\\eta$ with the untwisted companion $K$. For a knot $L$, write $M(L)$ for its actual chosen zero-longitude filling, with the orientation extending its exterior. Let $w=\\operatorname{lk}(P,\\eta)$.\n\nThere is a compact oriented smooth cobordism $E$ with\n$$\\partial E=M(P)\\sqcup M(K)\\sqcup(-M(P(K))).$$\nFor any commutative unital coefficient ring $R$, it has $H_1(E;R)=R$ and $H_2(E;R)=R^2$. The two first boundary components induce the displayed basis in degree two. If $s_L=\\alpha_L\\cap[M(L)]$ where $\\alpha_L\\in H^1(M(L);R)$ evaluates as $1$ on the positive meridian, then, in those coordinates,\n$$i_*s_{P(K)}=i_*s_P+w\\,i_*s_K.$$\nIn degree one the meridians of $P$, $K$ and $P(K)$ map to $1,w,1$, respectively.\n\nLikewise, for any finite nonempty list of knots $K_1,\\ldots,K_q$ with the same supplied peripheral data, there is a compact oriented smooth cobordism $C$ from $\\bigsqcup_j M(K_j)$ to $M(K_1\\#\\cdots\\#K_q)$, with $H_1(C;R)=R$ and $H_2(C;R)=R^q$. The incoming degree-two classes are its coordinate basis and the outgoing class maps to their sum. In particular, for $X=E$ or $C$, the outgoing inclusions are injective on $H_1,H_2$ and the union of incoming components surjects onto $H_2(X;R)$.\n\nThe peripheral and framing data are supplied, rather than selected by an existence theorem. Their subsequent construction and the homology assertions use no additional choice principle. This is an ordinary-coefficient assertion; arbitrary twisted-coefficient boundary generation is not asserted.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1",
            "3.2",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-ptfa-localized-boundary-intersection-rank-is-no-larger-than-ordinary-rank",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a compact connected oriented Hausdorff topological four-manifold and put $M=\\partial W$, allowing $M$ empty. Let $k$ be a commutative field, $G$ a PTFA group, and $\\phi:\\pi_1(W)\\to G$ a supplied coefficient homomorphism. Write $K$ for the fraction division ring of $k[G]$, with its standard involution, and use the induced rank-one right-coefficient systems. Suppose $\\dim_kH_1(M_j;k)=1$ for each connected component $M_j$ of $M$. Then\n$$\\dim_K\\operatorname{coker}\\{H_2(M;K)\\to H_2(W;K)\\}\\le\\dim_k\\operatorname{coker}\\{H_2(M;k)\\to H_2(W;k)\\}.$$\nAll dimensions in the formula are finite. No choice axiom, smoothness, triangulation, or supplied finite CW model of $W$ is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "3.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ptfa-localization-kills-first-homology-of-betti-one-manifolds",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $N$ be a compact connected Hausdorff topological manifold, with boundary allowed, and let $k$ be a commutative field with $\\dim_k H_1(N;k)=1$. Let $\\phi:\\pi_1(N)\\to G$ be nontrivial with $G$ PTFA, and let $K$ be the Ore fraction division ring of $k[G]$. Then $H_0(N;K)=H_1(N;K)=0$. No choice principle or finite CW model for $N$ is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "3.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-zero-localized-intersection-rank-forces-finite-boundary-union-kernel-isotropy",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a compact connected oriented topological four-manifold with a supplied boundary collar. Supply a unital involution-stable inclusion $R\\subseteq K$ into an involutive division ring and a based rank-one right-$R$ coefficient system on $W$, with unitary monodromy and the transported standard Hermitian form. Suppose\n$$H_2(W;K)=\\operatorname{im}\\{H_2(\\partial W;K)\\longrightarrow H_2(W;K)\\}.$$\nLet $N$ be a finite union of connected boundary components, each satisfying $H_1(N_j;K)=0$, with its induced boundary orientation and coefficient system. On each component define the linking form by inverse coefficient Bockstein, inverse oriented cap duality and evaluation; let $B_N$ be their orthogonal sum. Then\n$$B_N(x,y)=0\\quad\\text{whenever }x,y\\in\\ker\\{H_1(N;R)\\longrightarrow H_1(W;R)\\}.$$\nNo choice axiom or finite CW structure is assumed. No vanishing condition is imposed on the unselected boundary components.",
          "uses": [
            "3.2",
            "5.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-excision-and-mayer-vietoris-with-local-coefficients",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal L$ be one local system on $X$.\n\n1. If $Z\\subseteq A\\subseteq X$ and $\\overline Z\\subseteq\\operatorname{int}_X(A)$, inclusion induces excision isomorphisms in both local homology and local cohomology between $(X\\setminus Z,A\\setminus Z)$ and $(X,A)$, using the restrictions of $\\mathcal L$.\n2. For an open cover $X=U\\cup V$, there are natural exact sequences\n   $$\\cdots\\to H_n(U\\cap V;\\mathcal L)\\to H_n(U;\\mathcal L)\\oplus H_n(V;\\mathcal L)\\to H_n(X;\\mathcal L)\\to\\cdots$$\n   and\n   $$\\cdots\\to H^n(X;\\mathcal L)\\to H^n(U;\\mathcal L)\\oplus H^n(V;\\mathcal L)\\to H^n(U\\cap V;\\mathcal L)\\to\\cdots,$$\n   where all systems are restrictions and the middle difference map in cohomology is $u|_{U\\cap V}-v|_{U\\cap V}$.\n\nThe same conclusions hold for the standard excisive-cover condition after replacing the cover by interiors. A local system given only on a subspace is not silently assumed to extend to $X$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
