          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Use the actual product gluing from [F1]. Put $S=N(\\eta)=V_K$, $T_0=\\partial S$, $A=M(P)\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(\\eta)$ and $X_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$. Its spine is simultaneously $Z=M(P)\\cup_S M(K)$ and $Z=(A\\cup_{T_0}X_K)\\cup_{T_0}S=M(P(K))\\cup_{T_0}S$. The product-coordinate deformation to this spine fixes the remaining bottom faces $A$ and $X_K$; the rounded torus collars identify their union with the outgoing boundary. Hence it gives an equivalence of pairs $(E,M(P(K)))\\simeq(Z,M(P(K)))$. Excision in these collars identifies its relative homology with $H_*(S,T_0)$. These are actual subspaces and product homotopies, rather than an inference from ordinary homology.",
