      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Each $P^{i+1}L$ is a subgroup of $P^iL$. An automorphism of $L$ preserves $P^iL$ inductively, and induces an automorphism of its abelianization and of the displayed tensor group; their maps commute with $a\\mapsto a\\otimes1$. Its kernel is therefore preserved, proving that all $P^iL$ are characteristic and in particular normal. Also $L^{(i)}\\subseteq P^iL$ by induction: the assertion is equality at zero, and commutators of elements of $L^{(i)}$ lie in $[P^iL,P^iL]$, which maps to zero under abelianization and hence lies in $P^{i+1}L$. Derived subgroups are descending by their finite commutator definition. Consequently $N\\subseteq G^{(r)}\\subseteq G^{(i)}\\subseteq P^iG$ for every $i\\le r$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
