          "claim": "Put $A=M(P)\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(\\eta)$, $X_K=M(K)\\setminus\\operatorname{int}V_K$ and $S=N(\\eta)=V_K$. Collapse the interval coordinates in the two defining products to their identified bottom ends. The homotopies agree on $S$, so descend to a deformation to $Z=M(P)\\cup_S M(K)$. Rewriting $M(P)=A\\cup S$ and $M(K)=X_K\\cup S$ gives $$Z=(A\\cup_{\\partial S}X_K)\\cup_{\\partial S}S=M(P(K))\\cup_{\\partial S}S.$$ The deformation fixes $A$ and $X_K$ at their bottom ends; the explicit rounded torus collars identify this fixed union with the outgoing boundary. It therefore supplies the relative homotopy equivalence needed for the actual outgoing inclusion, rather than just an unmarked homotopy equivalence of spaces.",
