        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Apply [F2] to product-collared open neighborhoods in this last spine. On its overlap torus the two generators, written using companion peripheral coordinates, are $\\mu_K,\\lambda_K$. The solid torus $S$ has infinite-cyclic group generated by its core $c$, and the gluing sends $\\mu_K$ to $c$ and $\\lambda_K$ to $1$. Thus the pushout group has presentation relative to $G=\\pi_1(M(P(K)))$ as $$\\bigl(G*\\langle c\\rangle\\bigr)/\\langle\\!\\langle\\,\\mu_Kc^{-1},\\lambda_K\\,\\rangle\\!\\rangle.$$ Eliminate $c$: the map from $G/\\langle\\!\\langle\\lambda_K\\rangle\\!\\rangle$ to this group is induced by $G$, while the reverse map is induced by the quotient on $G$ and $c\\mapsto[\\mu_K]$. They respect the displayed relations and are inverse on both generating factors. This proves the first asserted isomorphism and surjectivity for the actual inclusion. The core $c$ was precisely $\\lambda_\\eta$, the oriented axis core; hence it also proves the marked meridian-axis identity. Neither torus-to-manifold map was assumed injective.",
