          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "For the manifold adjunction, the supplied boundary collars give open neighborhoods with the same homotopy types as $W$, $E$ and their common surgery component. Apply [F2] again. Put $B=\\pi_1(W)$ and let $f:G\\to B$ be its marked boundary inclusion map. By step 2.1, the other pushout factor is the quotient $G/\\langle\\!\\langle\\lambda_K\\rangle\\!\\rangle$. Every compatible pair of homomorphisms from these two factors is uniquely determined by a homomorphism from $B$ that kills $f(\\lambda_K)$: its values on the second factor are forced by its values on $G$, and they descend exactly when that relator is killed. The group $B/\\langle\\!\\langle f(\\lambda_K)\\rangle\\!\\rangle$ has precisely this universal property, with the actual inclusion from $B$. Explicitly send its coset of $b$ to the inclusion image of $b$; in the reverse direction use the quotient on $B$ and the homomorphism from $G/\\langle\\!\\langle\\lambda_K\\rangle\\!\\rangle$ induced by $f$. The composites are identities on the two pushout factors. This proves the second isomorphism and its stated map without an injectivity hypothesis on $f$.",
