          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "On the peripheral torus $T$, the supplied meridian and longitude give $H_1(T;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z[\\mu]\\oplus\\mathbb Z[\\lambda]$, as its finite square cell model shows. The tube retracts onto its core and has $H_1(N(K);\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z$. The longitude bounds the trimmed parallel Seifert surface in $X_K$, so its class there is zero, while it maps to the core generator in $N(K)$; the meridian maps to zero in that tube. Apply [F1] to $S^3=X_K\\cup N(K)$ with slightly thickened collars. The segment $0=H_2(S^3)\\to H_1(T)\\to H_1(X_K)\\oplus H_1(N(K))\\to H_1(S^3)=0$ makes its middle map an isomorphism. Its values on the two displayed generators therefore give $H_1(X_K)=\\mathbb Z[\\mu]$ exactly, including the marked generator.",
