    "lem-finite-winding-zero-infection-towers-preserve-required-derived-quotients": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-standard-infection-cobordism-adjunction-kills-the-companion-longitude",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $E$ be the actual standard infection cobordism from $M(P)\\sqcup M(K)$ to $M(P(K))$, constructed from the two surgery products by identifying $N(\\eta)$ with the filling solid torus $V_K$. Supply the oriented product tubes and peripheral paths, with $\\mu_\\eta=\\lambda_K$ and $\\lambda_\\eta=\\mu_K$ on the common torus, where $\\lambda_K$ is the companion's preferred longitude. No winding-number condition is needed. The inclusion-induced homomorphism is onto and induces\n$$\\pi_1(M(P(K)))/\\langle\\!\\langle\\lambda_K\\rangle\\!\\rangle\\ \\cong\\ \\pi_1(E).$$\nThe marked companion meridian and pattern-axis core have the same image in $\\pi_1(E)$, with the supplied base paths.\n\nMore generally, if a connected manifold $W$ with supplied boundary collar is glued to $E$ along the marked outgoing component $M(P(K))$, the inclusion-induced map is onto and gives\n$$\\pi_1(W)/\\langle\\!\\langle i_*(\\lambda_K)\\rangle\\!\\rangle\\ \\cong\\ \\pi_1(W\\cup_{M(P(K))}E).$$\nChanging a peripheral base path changes the relator by conjugation and leaves its normal closure unchanged. The statements hold for topological collared $W$ as well as smooth $W$ and use no choice axiom.",
          "uses": [
