          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "For $g\\in G$ and any representative loop $a$, define the right action by $[\\gamma]\\cdot g=[a^{-1}*\\gamma]$. Replacing $a$ by another representative gives the same path class, since $N$ is normal; replacing $\\gamma$ by an equivalent path also does. The action law follows from $b^{-1}*a^{-1}=(a*b)^{-1}$, and its maps carry the basic sets in step 1.1 to basic sets. On each fiber it is free and transitive: for paths $\\gamma,\\delta$ to the same endpoint take the quotient class of $\\gamma*\\delta^{-1}$, which sends $[\\gamma]$ to $[\\delta]$. The formula specifies the action uniquely without choosing representatives for all quotient elements. Free $k$-linearization of each fiber gives $\\mathcal R_x$; path transport commutes with this right action because it appends a path at the end, while deck action prepends $a^{-1}$. Thus it is a right-$k[G]$ local system, each fiber individually having a torsor point as a free basis. At the basepoint the constant-path point is a specified basis, and transport along $a$ sends it to $[a]=[1]\\cdot g^{-1}$, giving exactly the stated inverse convention and a right-linear map.",
