          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-compact-manifolds-have-finite-presentation-complexes-without-choice",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $M$ be a compact connected Hausdorff manifold, with boundary allowed, and $o\\in M$. Supply any finite list of based loops $\\gamma_1,\\ldots,\\gamma_\\ell$. There is a finite connected two-dimensional CW complex $K$ with one vertex $v$, a based map $f:(K,v)\\to(M,o)$ inducing an isomorphism on fundamental groups, and marked oriented one-cells which $f$ parametrizes by the specified loops. In particular $\\pi_1(M,o)$ is finitely presented without a choice axiom.\n\nFor any normal subgroup $N\\triangleleft\\pi_1(M,o)$ and commutative unital ring $k$, use on $M$ the associated right $k[\\pi_1(M)/N]$ normal-cover system and on $K$ its pullback. The actual induced map on $H_1$ with these coefficients is an isomorphism. No finite CW type, triangulation or smoothing of $M$ is asserted.",
