    "thm-integral-classical-blanchfield-self-values-survive-rational-and-prime-reduction-without-choice": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-compact-betti-one-manifolds-have-primitive-alexander-annihilators-without-choice",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $M$ be a compact connected Hausdorff manifold, with boundary allowed, with a specified based loop $\\mu$ whose integral homology class freely generates $H_1(M;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z$. Let $\\phi:\\pi_1(M)\\to\\mathbb Z$ be the abelianization taking $\\mu$ to $1$, put $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t,t^{-1}]$, and use its associated normal-cover right coefficient system, whose transport around a loop $a$ is left multiplication by $t^{-\\phi(a)}$ in the based fiber.\n\nThere is a finite Laurent matrix $A(t)$ such that\n$$H_1(M;\\Lambda)\\cong\\operatorname{coker}A(t),$$\nnaturally on changing the constant coefficient ring from $\\mathbb Z$ to any commutative unital ring $k$. More precisely the actual coefficient map gives\n$$H_1(M;\\Lambda)\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}k\\cong H_1(M;k[t,t^{-1}]).$$\nThere is a polynomial $\\Delta(t)\\in\\mathbb Z[t]$ with $\\Delta(0)\\ne0$ and $\\Delta(1)=1$ annihilating $H_1(M;\\Lambda)$; its coefficient image annihilates $H_1(M;k[t,t^{-1}])$ for every $k$. In particular $\\Delta$ is primitive and its reduction modulo any prime is nonzero. No choice principle, finite CW type, triangulation, smoothness or Seifert presentation for $M$ is assumed.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
