          "quote": "For every $0<\\theta_0<\\pi$ and every open interval $I\\subset(0,\\pi)$ containing $\\theta_0$, there is an explicit integral $8\\times8$ matrix $V$ with $\\det(V-V^T)=1$ such that the finite Hermitian matrix\n$$H_\\theta(V)=(1-e^{i\\theta})V+(1-e^{-i\\theta})V^T$$\nhas signature $2$ at $\\theta_0$ and signature zero for all $\\theta\\in[0,\\pi]\\setminus I$. Its signature takes only the values $0,1,2$ on $[0,\\pi]$ and is invariant under $\\theta\\mapsto-\\theta$. Moreover, its signature equals $2$ throughout an open interval containing $\\theta_0$. No choice principle, classification of Seifert forms, realization by a knot, or infinite-dimensional spectral theorem is assumed.",
