      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $\\Theta$ be the finite set $\\{0,\\pi\\}\\cup\\{2\\pi r/p_j:1\\le j\\le m,\\ 1\\le r\\le(p_j-1)/2\\}$. All displayed interior angles are distinct except when both indices and residues agree: equality $r/p_j=s/p_\\ell$ for distinct primes would force $p_j$ to divide $r$ or $p_\\ell$, impossible in the stated residue ranges. The target $\\theta_i=2\\pi/p_i$ is one of these interior angles. Its distance from every other member of $\\Theta$ is positive; let $\\delta_i$ be one third of the finite minimum of these distances. Thus $I_i=(\\theta_i-\\delta_i,\\theta_i+\\delta_i)\\subset(0,\\pi)$ contains none of the other angles in $\\Theta$. Choose the least positive integer $N_i$ with $2N_i>C_i$, which exists by the Archimedean property of the reals. All these are finite operations on the supplied list.",
