          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ be open and let $X=L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$. Every $u\\in X$ is integrable on compact subsets by Cauchy–Schwarz. Define its extended distributional total variation by\n$$TV_2(u;\\Omega):=\\sup\\left\\{\\int_\\Omega u\\,\\operatorname{div}\\varphi\\,dx:\\ \\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^2),\\ \\sup_{x\\in\\Omega}|\\varphi(x)|\\le1\\right\\}\\in[0,+\\infty],$$\nwhere $C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^2)$ denotes smooth compactly supported vector fields, $|\\cdot|$ is the Euclidean norm, and $\\operatorname{div}\\varphi=\\partial_1\\varphi_1+\\partial_2\\varphi_2$. This definition treats $L^2$ functions as almost-everywhere classes and does not require $u\\in L^1(\\Omega)$.",
