          "id": "derive-1-1",
          "claim": "The zero function has $TV_2(0;\\Omega)=0$, so the functional is proper; its defining test class is symmetric under $\\varphi\\mapsto-\\varphi$, hence its supremum is nonnegative. For $\\lambda>0$, linearity of every test integral gives $TV_2(\\lambda u;\\Omega)=\\lambda TV_2(u;\\Omega)$, and the equality also holds for $\\lambda=0$. For $\\theta\\in[0,1]$, every admissible field gives $\\int(\\theta u+(1-\\theta)v)\\operatorname{div}\\varphi\\le\\theta TV_2(u;\\Omega)+(1-\\theta)TV_2(v;\\Omega)$; taking the supremum proves convexity, with the extended-real cases automatic.",
