        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-ip-bv-strict-approximation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. For every open $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ and $u\\in BV(\\Omega)$ there is a sequence $u_k\\in C^\\infty(\\Omega)$ such that $u_k\\to u$ in $L^1(\\Omega)$ and $\\int_\\Omega |\\nabla u_k|\\,dx\\to TV(u;\\Omega)$. When $\\Omega=\\mathbb R^n$, the approximating functions may be chosen compactly supported.",
