          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open and let $u\\in C^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)\\cap L^1(\\Omega)$ satisfy $\\int_\\Omega|\\nabla u|\\,dx<\\infty$. For $t>0$ set $E_t^+:=\\{x\\in\\Omega:u(x)>t\\}$ and for $t<0$ set $E_t^-:=\\{x\\in\\Omega:u(x)<t\\}$. Then the level sets have finite perimeter relative to $\\Omega$ for almost every applicable $t$, and\n$$\\int_\\Omega|\\nabla u|\\,dx=\\int_0^\\infty P(E_t^+;\\Omega)\\,dt+\\int_{-\\infty}^0P(E_t^-;\\Omega)\\,dt.$$",
