          "id": "derive-2-1",
          "claim": "Now let $E$ be as in the Statement and put $u=\\chi_E$. By [F1], choose $u_j\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^2)$ with $e_j:=\\|u_j-\\chi_E\\|_1\\to0$ and $a_j:=\\int|\\nabla u_j|\\to P(E;\\mathbb R^2)$. If $|E|=0$, the result is immediate. If some $e_j=0$, continuity forces $u_j$ to take only the values $0$ and $1$ everywhere; connectedness of $\\mathbb R^2$ and compact support then force $u_j=0$, contradicting $|E|>0$. Thus $e_j>0$. Let $\\tau_j=\\sqrt{e_j}$ and discard finitely many terms so $0<\\tau_j<\\min\\{1/2,|E|/2\\}$. For every $t\\in I_j:=[\\tau_j,1-\\tau_j]$, a point where $\\chi_E$ and $\\chi_{\\{u_j>t\\}}$ differ contributes at least $\\tau_j$ to $|u_j-\\chi_E|$; hence $|\\{u_j>t\\}\\mathbin\\triangle E|\\le e_j/\\tau_j=\\tau_j$.",
