          "id": "derive-2-2",
          "claim": "By [F2], the measurable level-perimeter function has integral at most $a_j$ on $I_j$, whose length is $1-2\\tau_j$. For any $\\varepsilon>0$, the set of $t\\in I_j$ with $P(\\{u_j>t\\};\\mathbb R^2)\\le a_j/(1-2\\tau_j)+\\varepsilon$ has positive measure; otherwise its integral over $I_j$ would exceed $a_j$. The critical values of $u_j$ form a null set by [F2], so choose such a regular value $t_j$ and take $\\varepsilon=1/j$. Since $t_j>0$ and $u_j$ is compactly supported, $G_j:=\\{u_j>t_j\\}$ is bounded and its closure is a compact smooth domain with boundary $\\{u_j=t_j\\}$. Thus step 1.2 applies to $G_j$, and\n$$|G_j\\mathbin\\triangle E|\\le\\tau_j,\\qquad P(G_j;\\mathbb R^2)\\le\\frac{a_j}{1-2\\tau_j}+\\frac1j.$$\nThe right side has limit $P(E;\\mathbb R^2)$, while $|G_j|\\to|E|$.",
