          "quote": "Let $X,Y$ be real Banach spaces, let $F:D(F)\\subseteq X\\to Y$, let $x^\\dagger\\in D(F)$ with exact datum $y=F(x^\\dagger)$, and let $R:X\\to(-\\infty,+\\infty]$ be proper and convex with $x^\\dagger\\in\\operatorname{dom}R$. Fix $\\xi^\\dagger\\in\\partial R(x^\\dagger)$, an exponent $1\\le p<\\infty$, a continuous nondecreasing concave function $\\psi:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$ with $\\psi(0)=0$ and $\\psi(t)>0$ for $t>0$, a coefficient $0\\le\\beta<1$, and a level $R_0\\ge R(x^\\dagger)$. The **variational source condition** with these data holds on the named regularizer sublevel $L_{R_0}:=\\{x\\in D(F):R(x)\\le R_0\\}$ when\n\n$$-\\langle\\xi^\\dagger,x-x^\\dagger\\rangle_{X^*,X}\\le\\beta D_R^{\\xi^\\dagger}(x,x^\\dagger)+\\psi\\!\\left(\\|F(x)-F(x^\\dagger)\\|_Y^p\\right)\\qquad(x\\in L_{R_0}).$$\n\nThe condition is an assumption on the selected subgradient and the stated sublevel; it makes no assertion that a subgradient exists at every point or that a regularized minimizer exists.",
