          "source": "thm-monotone-convergence-for-the-integral",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ be an arbitrary measure space. Let $f_n:X\\to[0,+\\infty]$ be measurable for every $n\\ge1$, with $0\\le f_1\\le f_2\\le\\cdots$, and suppose $f_n(x)\\uparrow f(x)$ for every $x\\in X$. Then\n$$\\int f_n\\,d\\mu\\uparrow\\int f\\,d\\mu.$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "derive-1-1",
          "claim": "By [F1], choose compactly supported $v_R\\in BV(\\mathbb R^2)\\cap L^1$ with $v_R\\to u$ in $L^2$ and $\\limsup_RTV(v_R)\\le TV_2(u;\\mathbb R^2)$. For each fixed $t\\ne0$, $\\chi_{E_{R,t}}\\to\\chi_{E_t}$ in $L^1$: the symmetric difference is outside $B(0,R)$ for the cutoffs constructed in [F1] and contained in $\\{|u|>|t|\\}$, whose tail measure is at most $|t|^{-2}\\int_{\\mathbb R^2\\setminus B(0,R)}|u|^2$. Here $E_{R,t}$ and $E_t$ are the corresponding signed superlevel or sublevel sets.",
