        {
          "id": "derive-2-1",
          "claim": "For $t>0$, $|E_t^+|\\le t^{-2}\\|u\\|_2^2$, and for $t<0$, $|E_t^-|\\le |t|^{-2}\\|u\\|_2^2$. The indicator-valued maps are Borel on each half-line: on positive levels they are right-continuous in $L^1$ when $t_j\\downarrow t>0$, by continuity from below of measure; on negative levels they are left-continuous when $t_j\\uparrow t<0$. Composing with the lower semicontinuous extended variation in [F3] makes their perimeter functions measurable. Lower semicontinuity in [F3] and step 1.1 give $P(E_t^\\pm;\\mathbb R^2)\\le\\liminf_{R\\to\\infty}P(E_{R,t}^\\pm;\\mathbb R^2)$ for every applicable nonzero $t$. Fatou's lemma [F5], the BV coarea identity [F2], and the variation bound in step 1.1 imply, for every $\\varepsilon>0$,\n$$\\int_\\varepsilon^\\infty P(E_t^+;\\mathbb R^2)\\,dt+\\int_{-\\infty}^{-\\varepsilon}P(E_t^-;\\mathbb R^2)\\,dt\\le TV_2(u;\\mathbb R^2).$$\nLetting $\\varepsilon\\downarrow0$ and using monotone convergence [F5] proves that the full perimeter sum is at most $TV_2(u;\\mathbb R^2)$; its finiteness and [F3] give finite perimeter for almost every applicable level.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F5",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
