        {
          "id": "derive-3-1",
          "claim": "Let $\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^2;\\mathbb R^2)$ with $\\|\\varphi\\|_\\infty\\le1$. The signed layer-cake identity is $u(x)=\\int_0^\\infty\\chi_{E_t^+}(x)\\,dt-\\int_{-\\infty}^0\\chi_{E_t^-}(x)\\,dt$. On the compact support of $\\operatorname{div}\\varphi$, $\\int |u|\\,|\\operatorname{div}\\varphi|<\\infty$, so Tonelli and Fubini [F4] permit integration of this identity against $\\operatorname{div}\\varphi$. At almost every level the absolute value of the resulting indicator test integral is at most its perimeter by [F3]. Therefore $\\int u\\operatorname{div}\\varphi$ is at most the perimeter sum in step 2.1. Taking the supremum over admissible $\\varphi$ gives $TV_2(u;\\mathbb R^2)$ at most that sum, which together with step 2.1 proves equality.",
