          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain, meaning a bounded open set whose boundary has a finite cover by Lipschitz graph neighborhoods with $\\Omega$ on one side of each graph. Total variation is lower semicontinuous under $L^1(\\Omega)$ convergence of BV functions. Every sequence $(u_k)\\subset BV(\\Omega)$ satisfying $$\\sup_k\\bigl(\\|u_k\\|_{L^1(\\Omega)}+TV(u_k;\\Omega)\\bigr)<\\infty$$ has a subsequence converging in $L^1(\\Omega)$ to a function in $BV(\\Omega)$.",
