          "claim": "Use [F2] to attach the smooth cylinder $[0,\\infty)\\times\\partial M$ to $M$ along its boundary. By [F3], the metric coefficients extend smoothly across each boundary point to the double. Compactness of $\\partial M$ gives a finite such cover; [F4] patches these local extensions by a smooth partition of unity. After shrinking the collar, the patched tensor remains positive definite, since it agrees with $g$ on $M$ and positive definiteness is open. Solve the geodesic ODE for the extended metric from each boundary point in the outward unit-normal direction. At $(x,0)$ the derivative of $(x,s)\\mapsto\\exp_x(s\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}(x))$ sends $(w,a)$ to $w+a\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}(x)$, an isomorphism; [F15] therefore gives local inverse charts along the zero section. A finite subcover gives a common domain where this map is a local diffeomorphism. If no uniform collar width made it injective, there would be distinct pairs $(x_j,s_j)$ and $(y_j,t_j)$ with equal images and $0\\le s_j,t_j\\downarrow0$; [F20], first for $(x_j)$ and then for $(y_j)$ along the resulting subsequence, gives a common subsequence converging to $(x,0)$ and $(y,0)$, equality of the images forces $x=y$, and both pairs then lie in one local inverse chart at $(x,0)$, a contradiction. Thus a uniform outward normal collar exists.",
