          "quote": "Let $d,N\\ge1$ and let $A\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be compact. For every multi-index $\\alpha$ prescribe a continuous function $f_\\alpha:A\\to\\mathbb R^N$. Define $P_a^k(x)=\\sum_{|\\alpha|\\le k}f_\\alpha(a)(x-a)^\\alpha/\\alpha!$. Assume the full Whitney compatibility conditions: for every $k\\ge0$ and $|\\alpha|\\le k$,\n$$D^\\alpha P_a^k(b)-f_\\alpha(b)=o(|a-b|^{k-|\\alpha|})\\quad(a,b\\in A,\\ |a-b|\\to0),$$\nuniformly in $a,b$. Then a smooth $F:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R^N$ exists with $D^\\alpha F|_A=f_\\alpha$ for all $\\alpha$. The construction uses no choice axiom. For a compact parameter family of jets on the same $A$, all choices of scales can be made common, and the resulting extensions have uniformly bounded seminorms on compact sets, provided all coefficient bounds and all the Whitney remainder moduli are uniform in that family.",
