          "claim": "The empty-set case has the zero extension. Otherwise use the fixed Whitney cubes and partition $\\psi_Q$ constructed in [F1]: outside $A$, their side lengths satisfy $\\ell(Q)\\asymp\\operatorname{dist}(Q,A)$, enlarged cubes have bounded overlap and comparable sizes when they meet, and $|D^\\alpha\\psi_Q|\\le C_\\alpha\\ell(Q)^{-|\\alpha|}$. These facts follow from the fixed maximal dyadic retention test and rescaled bump quotient in that proof, independently of the jet order. Put $\\sigma(z)=\\sum_Q\\ell(Q)\\psi_Q(z)$. This is smooth and positive off $A$, and for $t=\\operatorname{dist}(z,A)$ it satisfies $c t\\le\\sigma(z)\\le C t$ and $|D^\\alpha\\sigma(z)|\\le C_\\alpha t^{1-|\\alpha|}$. Each derivative estimate follows by bounded overlap and the side-length comparison. Fix $\\chi\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R)$ with $\\chi=1$ on $(-\\infty,1]$ and $\\chi=0$ on $[2,\\infty)$. Then $\\eta_\\delta(z)=\\chi(\\sigma(z)/\\delta)$ equals one for $t\\le\\delta/C$, vanishes for $t\\ge2\\delta/c$, and obeys $|D^\\alpha\\eta_\\delta|\\le B_\\alpha t^{-|\\alpha|}$ on its transition, with constants independent of $\\delta$.",
