        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "For completeness the needed high-order embedding also has a finite-chart proof with this axiom base. In a half-chart extend across $x_n=0$ by $\\sum_{j=1}^{k+1}a_jv(x',-jx_n)$ for $x_n<0$, where the finite Vandermonde system $\\sum_j a_j(-j)^\\ell=1$ for $0\\le\\ell\\le k$ matches the derivatives at the interface. After a cutoff this is a bounded $H^k$ extension; the assertion follows first on smooth functions and then by the weak derivative identities and approximation. On a bounded support box, iterated one-dimensional integration gives $\\|D^\\alpha w\\|_\\infty\\le C\\|D_1\\cdots D_nD^\\alpha w\\|_2$ for smooth compactly supported $w$. Apply this also to first derivatives of $D^\\alpha w$ and to differences of mollifications. For $k\\ge n+a+1$ these mollifications and all derivatives through order $a$ are uniformly Cauchy and their limits are continuous, with the asserted norm bound; passing to the coordinate segment integral identifies them as classical derivatives. Sum the finite chart extensions. This proves the embedding and completes the lemma.",
