    "thm-ip-variable-metric-wave-ibvp-energy-wellposedness": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-ip-compact-manifold-dirichlet-spectrum-and-regularity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $(M,g)$ be a nonempty compact smooth Riemannian manifold of positive dimension with smooth boundary and $q$ a smooth real function. Set $H=L^2(M,dV_g)$, $V=H^1_0(M)$ and $c=1+\\|q\\|_\\infty$. Then\n$$b(u,v)=\\int_M(\\langle\\nabla u,\\nabla\\bar v\\rangle+(q+c)u\\bar v)\\,dV_g$$\nis an equivalent Hilbert inner product on $V$. There are an $H$-orthonormal sequence $(e_j)$ complete in $H$ and positive numbers $\\mu_j\\to\\infty$ such that $b(e_j,v)=\\mu_j(e_j,v)_H$ for every $v\\in V$, and\n$$b(u,u)=\\sum_j\\mu_j|(u,e_j)_H|^2\\qquad(u\\in V).$$\nFor $A=-\\Delta_g+q$, weak solutions $v\\in V$ of $Av=f\\in H^k(M)$ satisfy\n$$\\|v\\|_{H^{k+2}(M)}\\le C_k(\\|f\\|_{H^k(M)}+\\|v\\|_{L^2(M)}),\\qquad k=0,1,\\ldots.$$\nHere integer Sobolev norms use any finite smooth atlas. For every integer $a$, the inclusion $H^k(M)\\to C^a(M)$ is bounded for all sufficiently large integers $k$.",
          "uses": [
