        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "If two energy solutions have the same data and forcing, test their difference against $e_j$. The scalar coefficient is a distributional solution of $d_j''+(\\mu_j-c)d_j=0$ with zero strong data. Its integral equation, or the scalar fundamental solution, gives $d_j=0$. Completeness in [F1] makes the difference zero for every time. The estimate of step 1.1 passes to the strong limit, including its zero-data version. Replacing $t$ by $T-t$ proves terminal well-posedness with the same bound.",
