      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Cover the parameter interval by finitely many small overlapping intervals on which the immersed base curve is embedded. In such an interval choose coordinates $(s,y)$ with the curve $y=0$ and with $s$ its prescribed parameter. The central covector satisfies $p=0$ and $p_{\\xi_s}\\ne0$, since the Hamilton velocity in these coordinates is a nonzero multiple of $\\partial_s$. The formal implicit equation $p(s,y,\\partial_s\\phi,\\partial_y\\phi)=0$ can thus be solved recursively for the jets of $\\partial_s\\phi$. This is an evolution eikonal equation in $s$, with a smooth real reduced Hamiltonian in the real variables. Its zeroth and first jet equations are exactly the given Hamilton curve (after its parameter change). Initialize the transverse Hessian by $H(0)=iI$ in the chosen transverse coordinates.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
