          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The quadratic jet equation is the matrix Riccati equation $$H'+D+BH+HB^T+HCH=0,$$ where $C,D$ are real symmetric and $B$ real, the corresponding blocks of the reduced Hamiltonian Hessian. Solve instead $Y'=B^TY+CZ$, $Z'=-DY-BZ$, $Y(0)=I$, $Z(0)=iI$. Direct differentiation gives $Y^TZ-Z^TY=0$ and $Y^*Z-Z^*Y=2iI$. If $Yv=0$ the second identity gives $0=2i|v|^2$, so $Y$ is invertible on the whole interval. Consequently $H=ZY^{-1}$ is symmetric, solves the Riccati equation, and $$\\operatorname{Im}H=(Y^{-1})^*Y^{-1}>0.$$ Compactness gives uniform positive lower and finite upper bounds. At an overlap transform all jets by the coordinate chain rule, carry these initial data to the next chart, and use ODE uniqueness. Positivity is unchanged by real coordinate change and persists on the finite cover.",
