          "claim": "The set of embeddings of the compact circle into $\\mathbb R^3$ is open in the $C^1$ topology. To verify this for the given compact family, cover $S^1$ by finitely many parameter intervals on which the derivative of each $K_s$ has a uniform positive lower bound; a sufficiently small $C^1$ perturbation remains an immersion there. On the compact complement of a neighborhood of the diagonal in $S^1\\times S^1$, injectivity has a uniform positive separation because $(s,x,y)\\mapsto\\|K_s(x)-K_s(y)\\|$ is continuous and positive. A sufficiently small $C^0$ perturbation preserves that separation. Thus a small perturbation of $h$ alone keeps every slice embedded and fixed at the two endpoint collars. The straight interpolation between $h$ and its perturbation is also $C^1$-small, hence stays embedded; [F6] extends this path to ambient isotopy.",
