          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Cut the knot at regular levels inside the fixed critical neighborhoods. Choose the tangle pieces containing critical points within the neighborhoods fixed by the horizontal deformation; each intervening tangle has no critical points and has fixed boundary points. By [F14], their degreewise integrals compose, and gluing the cut endpoints restores exactly the original circle pairing: the cuts add no integration levels. Thus it suffices to compare one no-critical tangle $T$. Fix a degree-$m$ branch chamber for $T$. Since $T$ is embedded and has no critical points, distinct branches at one height have a uniform positive horizontal separation on the compact closed chamber, so every logarithmic factor is smooth there. For a nonzero branch difference $\\Delta=z_i-z_j$, $d\\log\\Delta=d\\Delta/\\Delta$ is closed because $d(d\\Delta/\\Delta)=-(d\\Delta\\wedge d\\Delta)/\\Delta^2=0$. Extend each factor to the full differential in $(t_1,\\dots,t_m,s)$; the product sum $\\omega_m$ is then closed, with equal-level coefficients interpreted in the 4T quotient. Apply Stokes to the compactified chamber cylinder from [F2].",
