          "source": "thm-vassiliev-invariant-induces-weight-system",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $n\\ge0$. For an unframed $R$-valued invariant $V$ of type at most $n$, the degree-$n$ derivative induces an $R$-linear functional on degree-$n$ chord diagrams modulo 4T and 1T. For a framed $R$-valued invariant $V$ of type at most $n$, assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$; its degree-$n$ derivative induces an $R$-linear functional on degree-$n$ chord diagrams modulo 4T. Framed derivatives are not subject to a universal 1T vanishing law: integer-valued framed self-linking has value $2$ on the one-chord diagram with blackboard framing.",
