          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $W\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb Q}(\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{un}},\\mathbb C)$ be any weight system. Define $V_W(K)=W(I_n(K))$, using the complex-linear extension of $W$. By [F6] this is an ambient-isotopy invariant. Since $I_{\\le n}$ is of type at most $n$ by [F4], each homogeneous coefficient, and hence $V_W$, is of type at most $n$. For an $n$-singular knot with diagram $D$, [F5] gives $D_nV_W(K)=W(D)$. Thus $\\sigma_n([V_W])=W$, proving surjectivity; in particular this holds for rational-valued weight systems.",
