          "quote": "Let $T_1\\subset\\mathbb C\\times[a,c]$ and $T_2\\subset\\mathbb C\\times[c,b]$ be compact strict Morse tangles whose boundary points and orientations match at the regular level $c$, with the joined tangle $T=T_2\\circ T_1$ smooth and embedded. Their unframed configuration integrals converge absolutely degreewise and satisfy\n$$\nZ(T_2\\circ T_1)=Z(T_2)\\,Z(T_1),\n$$\nwhere multiplication stacks tangle diagrams with $T_2$ above $T_1$. The equality holds in the completed unframed tangle diagram space and uses only the finite-degree integrals defined on the matched pieces.",
