          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $X,H$ be separable real Hilbert spaces, let $K:X\\to H$ be bounded and linear, and let $\\epsilon>0$. Let $U$ be a Borel Gaussian prior with mean $m_0$ and positive self-adjoint, injective, trace-class covariance $C_0$, independent of a jointly Gaussian centered family $Z$ indexed by $H$, linear into $L^2$ with covariance $\\mathbb E[Z(g)Z(k)]=\\langle g,k\\rangle_H$. For parameter $x\\in X$, the observation field is $Y_x(g)=\\langle Kx,g\\rangle_H+\\epsilon Z(g)$. Fix a feature vector $h\\in X$. Let\n$$S=C_0^{1/2},\\qquad B=SK^*KS,\\qquad R=(B+\\epsilon^2I_X)^{-1},\\qquad \\Phi_h=KSRSh,$$\nand define the raw threshold\n$$c_h=\\langle Km_0,\\Phi_h\\rangle_H-\\langle m_0,h\\rangle_X.$$\nInput a white-noise observation field $y\\in\\mathbb R^H$. Compute $q=y(\\Phi_h)-c_h$. Return $1$ when $q>0$ and return $0$ when $q\\le0$. This strict raw comparison defines the **Gaussian MAP feature test** for every field input $y$.",
