        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-square-summable-sequences-form-a-hilbert-space",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The real sequence space\n$$\\ell^2(\\mathbb N,\\mathbb R)=\\left\\{x=(x_n):\\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb N}|x_n|^2<\\infty\\right\\},$$\nwith its canonical inner product and norm from\n[[def-square-summable-family-on-an-arbitrary-index-set]], is complete and\ntherefore is a real Hilbert space.",
