          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Use the solid-torus side with core the first-coordinate circle, so the second coordinate is the meridional disk coordinate. At longitudinal angle $u\\in\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z$ in the first coordinate, the knot meets this disk at the $p$ points with second-coordinate angles $2\\pi q(u+k)/p$, $k=0,\\ldots,p-1$. Place these points at the vertices of a regular $p$-gon. A counterclockwise rotation by $2\\pi/p$, tapered to fix the disk boundary, carries each point to the next and crosses consecutive points once in the order $\\sigma_1,\\ldots,\\sigma_{p-1}$; each $\\sigma_i$ is the positive half twist of adjacent points. Thus one such increment is the braid block $\\delta=\\sigma_1\\cdots\\sigma_{p-1}$, and the rotation through $2\\pi q/p$ gives $\\delta^q$. The lifted curve has winding vector $(p,q)$ in the fixed Heegaard-torus coordinates, exactly the parameterization in [F1]. The braid block permutes the points by a $p$-cycle, so its $q$th power has one cycle because $\\gcd(p,q)=1$.",
