          "claim": "If $n=0$, the codomain and image are both the zero group, so the cokernel is trivial and has order $1=|\\det A|$. Now suppose $n>0$. Multiplication on the left or right by an integer matrix with determinant $\\pm1$ preserves the isomorphism type of the cokernel and preserves the absolute determinant: left multiplication changes the basis of the target, and right multiplication changes the basis of the domain.",
