        {
          "id": "derive-2.1",
          "claim": "Put $G_q=\\ker(\\phi\\bmod q)$. For $g\\in G_q$, write $\\phi(g)=qk$ and set $n=g s^{-qk}\\in N$. Then $g=n s^{qk}$, and the expression is unique because $\\phi(s^{qk})=qk$. Thus $G_q$ is the split extension of $N$ by the infinite cyclic group generated by $s^q$, acting on $N$ by conjugation. By [F5] and [F1], $G_q$ is the fundamental group of $E_q$.",
