        {
          "id": "derive-3.1",
          "claim": "Abelianizing this split extension kills the commutators in $N$ and the relations $s^qns^{-q}=n$ for $n\\in N$. By [F3], those relations impose $(t^q-1)A_K=0$ on $N^{\\mathrm{ab}}$; if the inverse deck convention is used, $t^{-q}-1=-t^{-q}(t^q-1)$ generates the same submodule. The homomorphism $G_q\\to\\mathbb Z$, $g\\mapsto\\phi(g)/q$, splits by $1\\mapsto s^q$, so $H_1(E_q;\\mathbb Z)\\cong A_K/(t^q-1)A_K\\oplus\\mathbb Z[s^q]$.",
