          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot, let $F$ be a connected compact oriented Seifert surface of genus $g$, and choose any ordered integral basis $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ with positive-push Seifert matrix $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. For an integer $q\\ge2$, let $M_q(V)$ be the symmetric block matrix of size $2g(q-1)$ whose $2g\\times2g$ block in position $(k,\\ell)$, for $1\\le k,\\ell\\le q-1$, is $V+V^T$ if $k=\\ell$, $-V^T$ if $\\ell=k+1$, $-V$ if $k=\\ell+1$, and $0$ if $|k-\\ell|\\ge2$. Then\n$$\nH_1(\\Sigma_q(K);\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\operatorname{coker}(M_q(V)).\n$$\nFor $q=2$ this presentation matrix is $V+V^T$; when $g=0$ the empty matrix has trivial cokernel.",
