          "source": "thm-seifert-matrix-presents-knot-alexander-module",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented standard three-sphere, let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface with boundary orientation equal to that of $K$, let $g$ satisfy $\\chi(F)=1-2g$, and choose an ordered integral basis $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$. Use the positive normal convention $(n,u,v)>0$ and define $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. Let $A_K=H_1(\\widetilde X_K;\\mathbb Z)$ be the one-variable Alexander module of the knot complement $X_K=S^3\\setminus K$, where the cover is classified by the total-linking homomorphism and $t$ acts by the deck transformation corresponding to the positive meridian. Then there is an isomorphism of $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$-modules\n$$A_K\\cong\\operatorname{coker}\\bigl(V-tV^T:\\Lambda^{2g}\\to\\Lambda^{2g}\\bigr).$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-seifert-matrix-skew-part-is-surface-intersection",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented embedded circle in the oriented standard three-sphere, let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface with boundary $K$, and let $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ be any ordered integral basis of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ with Seifert matrix $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. Let $J_F$ be the matrix of the algebraic intersection form on $F$, with a transverse intersection of oriented curves $u,v$ counted positively exactly when their ordered tangent vectors form a positive basis of $TF$. Then $V-V^T=J_F$. The matrix $J_F$ is skew-symmetric and unimodular; when $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ is a standard handle basis, it is a direct sum of blocks $\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&0\\end{pmatrix}$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-seifert-determinant-is-the-knot-alexander-polynomial",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $K\\subset S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot, and let $F\\subset S^3$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface whose oriented boundary is $K$, with $\\chi(F)=1-2g$. Choose an ordered integral basis $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ and use the positive normal convention $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. Let $A_K$ be the first homology of the infinite cyclic cover of $S^3\\setminus K$ classified by total linking, with $t$ acting by the positive-meridian deck transformation. Let $\\Delta_K(t)$ be the generator of the zeroth elementary ideal $E_0(A_K)$ in $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$, and write $p\\doteq q$ when $p$ and $q$ differ by a unit $\\pm t^k$ of $\\Lambda$. Then for every such $F$ and basis,\n\n$$\\det(V-tV^T)\\doteq\\Delta_K(t).$$\n\nThe determinant is $1$ for the empty $0\\times0$ matrix when $g=0$. This formula concerns the polynomial $\\Delta_K$; the existing knot-normalized fraction $D_K=\\Delta_K/(1-t)$ is a separate invariant.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-square-integer-cokernel-finiteness-and-order",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $n$ be a nonnegative integer and let $A$ be an $n\\times n$ matrix with integer entries. Define $\\operatorname{coker}(A)=\\mathbb Z^n/A\\mathbb Z^n$. Then $\\operatorname{coker}(A)$ is finite if and only if $\\det A\\ne0$, and in that case its order is $|\\det A|$. For the empty $0\\times0$ matrix, take $\\det A=1$ and $\\operatorname{coker}(A)=0$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        }
