          "source": "lem-square-seifert-presentation-and-alexander-normalization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $K\\subset S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot, let $F\\subset S^3$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface with oriented boundary $K$, and let $\\chi(F)=1-2g$ with $g\\ge0$. Choose an ordered integral basis $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$, use the positive normal convention, and set $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. Let $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$, let $A_K$ be the first homology of the infinite cyclic cover classified by total linking with $t$ acting by the positive-meridian deck transformation, and let $\\Delta_K$ be a generator of the zeroth elementary ideal $E_0(A_K)$. Then the square matrix $M(t)=V-tV^T$ generates that ideal:\n\n$$E_0(A_K)=(\\det M(t)).$$\n\nFor $g=0$, the matrix is empty and its determinant is $1$. In every genus, $\\det(V-V^T)=\\pm1$, so every generator $\\Delta_K$ satisfies $\\Delta_K(1)=\\pm1$. The ideal and determinant assertions are compatible with integral basis changes and with orientation-preserving ambient isotopies of knot-surface pairs.",
