        {
          "id": "derive-2.1",
          "claim": "For the unknot, the standard spanning disk has genus zero, so its Seifert matrix is empty and [F1] gives trivial first homology. To identify the whole cover, write $S^3=\\{(z,w)\\in\\mathbb C^2:|z|^2+|w|^2=1\\}$ and define $f(z,w)=\\bigl(z\\sqrt{1+|w|^2},w^2\\bigr)$. The image lies in $S^3$ because $|z|^2(1+|w|^2)+|w|^4=1$. Off $w=0$, each target point has exactly two preimages, corresponding to the two square roots of its second coordinate; on $w=0$ it has one. The involution $(z,w)\\mapsto(z,-w)$ is the deck transformation, and in tubular coordinates about $w=0$ the transverse map is $w\\mapsto w^2$. Hence $f$ is the connected double branched cover of $S^3$ over the unknot, so the cover is $S^3$.",
