    "lem-torus-curves-same-primitive-class-isotopic-kt18-local": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-choice-free-smooth-torus-curves-and-annulus-strips",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "An essential smooth embedded circle in the standard torus $T=\\mathbb R^2/\\mathbb Z^2$ represents a nonzero primitive integral homology class. A finite disjoint family of essential smooth circles can be carried by a jointly smooth ambient isotopy of $T$ to parallel affine circles. Two essential circles with the same primitive unoriented class are smoothly ambient isotopic. The components between disjoint essential circles have smooth annulus parameters, with prescribed product collars on their boundary circles. No choice axiom is assumed.\n\nLikewise two smooth spanning arcs of a parametrized annulus with the same endpoints and relative winding number are smoothly ambient isotopic relative to any collars on which they already agree. When disjoint, they have a smooth disk-strip parameter; disjoint essential circles in a parametrized annulus have smooth annulus-strip parameters. All isotopies may be stationary near their time endpoints.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
