      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Apply a Euclidean similarity of the boundary plane, extended by the same scaling of height, sending the circumcircle of the three finite ideal vertices to the unit circle centered at $0$; this upper half-space isometry fixes $\\infty$. The three vertices become points $p,q,r$ on that circle and remain equilateral. Hence $(0,0)$ lies in the interior of their triangle, so the vertical ray from $(0,0,1)$ to $\\infty$ lies inside the tetrahedron.",
