          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Since $f$ is an isometry, $f^*g_N=g_M$. In any coordinate charts, if $J=Df$ is the coordinate derivative, then the metric matrices satisfy $G_M=J^{\\mathsf T}(G_N\\circ f)J$. Taking determinants gives $\\sqrt{\\det G_M}=|\\det J|\\sqrt{\\det(G_N\\circ f)}$. Thus $f$ pulls the Riemannian volume density of $N$ back to that of $M$, regardless of whether it preserves orientation.",
