          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $h:\\mathbb C\\to\\mathbb C$ be an orientation-preserving homeomorphism. For $x\\in\\mathbb C$ and $r>0$, put $L(x,r)=\\max_{|y-x|=r}|h(y)-h(x)|$ and $l(x,r)=\\min_{|y-x|=r}|h(y)-h(x)|$. Suppose $L(x,r)\\le H l(x,r)$ for every $x,r$, with one fixed $1\\le H<\\infty$. Then $h\\in W^{1,2}_{\\mathrm{loc}}$, its continuous representative is ACL, and it is analytically $H$-quasiconformal:\n$$|h_{\\bar z}|\\le\\frac{H-1}{H+1}|h_z|\\quad\\hbox{almost everywhere}.$$\nFor relatively compact open sets $V\\Subset U\\Subset\\mathbb C$, a coordinate unit vector $e_i$ and $0<|t|<\\operatorname{dist}(V,\\partial U)/2$, one has the explicit estimate\n$$\\int_V\\left|\\frac{h(x+te_i)-h(x)}t\\right|^2\\,dx\\le4H^2\\operatorname{area}(h(U)).$$",
