          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $f:\\Omega\\to\\Omega'$ be an orientation-preserving analytically $K$-quasiconformal homeomorphism, $K\\ge1$, in the sense of [[def-acl-sobolev-quasiconformal-homeomorphism]]. For every Jordan quadrilateral $Q\\Subset\\Omega$ with either pair of opposite marked sides, write $\\Gamma_Q$ for its joining family and $\\Gamma_{f(Q)}$ for the corresponding image family ([[def-geometric-quasiconformal-homeomorphism]]). Then\n$$K^{-1}\\mu(\\Gamma_Q)\\le\\mu(\\Gamma_{f(Q)})\\le K\\mu(\\Gamma_Q),$$\nequivalently\n$$K^{-1}\\lambda(\\Gamma_Q)\\le\\lambda(\\Gamma_{f(Q)})\\le K\\lambda(\\Gamma_Q).$$\nThis result supplies quadrilateral bounds; no inverse regularity, inverse null-set property or arbitrary-ring comparison is assumed.",
