          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Define the locally finite Borel measure $\\omega(E)=\\operatorname{area}(h(E))$. This is a measure because a homeomorphism maps disjoint Borel sets to disjoint Borel sets and respects unions. It is Radon because it is the pushforward of planar area by the homeomorphism $h^{-1}$; compact and open approximation transport through that homeomorphism. The open image $h(B(x,r))$ contains $B(h(x),l(x,r))$: otherwise a segment from $h(x)$ to a point of that smaller disk outside the image would first meet the boundary $h(\\partial B(x,r))$, contradicting the definition of $l$. The maximum distance from $h(x)$ in $h(\\overline{B(x,r)})$ occurs on its boundary, because distance from a fixed point has no maximum in a nonempty open set. Hence $|h(y)-h(x)|\\le L(x,r)\\le H l(x,r)$ for $y\\in\\overline{B(x,r)}$, and $\\pi l(x,r)^2\\le\\omega(B(x,r))$.",
