          "claim": "Continuity makes $h$ square integrable on every relatively compact $U$. The uniform estimate in step 2.1 and [F1], with $p=2$ and complex-valued functions, give $h\\in W^{1,2}(V)$. Exhausting the plane proves local Sobolev regularity. Apply [F2] on a countable collection of rectangles. On almost every coordinate line, its ACL representative agrees with the continuous representative almost everywhere by Fubini, hence everywhere on each compact line interval because both are continuous there. Thus the actual map $h$ is ACL and has finite coordinate partial derivatives almost everywhere, agreeing with the weak derivatives.",
