          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "If $\\gamma$ is an essential simple closed curve on $T$, it is nonseparating; cutting along it gives an annulus. An arc joining the two annulus boundary circles closes to a simple curve $\\delta$ meeting $\\gamma$ once, so the algebraic intersection is $[\\gamma]\\cdot[\\delta]=\\pm1$. Writing $[\\gamma]=p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$ and $[\\delta]=a[\\mu]+b[\\lambda]$ gives $pb-qa=\\pm1$ because the ordered basis has intersection form $\\pm1$. Any common divisor of $p,q$ would divide $pb-qa$, so $\\gcd(p,q)=1$.",
