          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice for the chosen smooth knot-exterior data. Let $K_8$ be the standard figure-eight knot, presented as the boundary of the square plumbing of one positive and one negative Hopf band, with one boundary component. A positive Hopf band is an oriented annulus whose positive normal push-off of its core has linking number $+1$ with the core; a negative Hopf band has linking number $-1$. A square plumbing identifies a square in the boundary collars of the annuli with the four boundary edges alternating between the annuli, then smooths corners. Let $F$ be this plumbed surface, and choose the compact exterior by deleting the interior of the binding neighborhood $N(K_8)\\cong\\partial F\\times D^2$ supplied by the open book; on every page this neighborhood meets the page in an annular collar of $\\partial F$. Let $a,b$ be the core curves, ordered so that $a$ is the positive-band core and $a\\cdot_F b=+1$. The exterior $E_{K_8}$ fibers over $S^1$ with fiber $F$. With the twist convention that the positive twist $R_a$ sends $a\\mapsto a$, $b\\mapsto a+b$, and the negative twist $L_b$ sends $a\\mapsto a+b$, $b\\mapsto b$, the monodromy is $R_a\\circ L_b$. After capping $\\partial F$ by a disk, its action on the ordered homology basis $([a],[b])$ is represented by $\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\1&1\\end{pmatrix}$.",
