        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-complete-curvature-minus-one-manifolds-are-kleinian-quotients",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Every nonempty connected oriented complete Riemannian three-manifold of constant sectional curvature $-1$ is isometric to $\\Gamma\\backslash\\mathbb H^3$ for a discrete torsion-free subgroup $\\Gamma\\le\\mathrm{PSL}_2(\\mathbb C)$. The covering is a universal Riemannian covering and identifies $\\Gamma$ with the fundamental group up to the usual basepoint conjugacies. Its completeness and quotient presentation are conclusions from the stated metric hypotheses. The orientation-preserving isometry group of the model is $\\mathrm{PSL}_2(\\mathbb C)$ with its usual Möbius boundary action.",
