      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $c((e^{i\\theta},w),s)=((1-s/8)e^{i\\theta},w)$ for $(e^{i\\theta},w)\\in\\partial V'$ and $s\\in[0,2]$; this is a collar because its radial coordinate ranges from $1$ to $3/4$. Set $\\rho(s)=1-s$ for $0\\le s\\le1$ and $\\rho(s)=0$ for $1\\le s\\le2$. The map $J(c(x,s))=c(H_{\\rho(s)}(x),s)$ on the collar, extended by the identity outside it, is a homeomorphism: its inverse replaces $H_{\\rho(s)}$ with $H_{\\rho(s)}^{-1}$. It restricts to $H_1$ at the boundary and is isotopic to the identity through the same formula with $H_{u\\rho(s)}$ for $u\\in[0,1]$. Thus $h_0=J|_{\\partial V'}\\circ h$ sends $\\mu$ exactly to $\\mu'$, and extending $h_0$ suffices because postcomposition with $J^{-1}$ recovers an extension of $h$ without changing its orientation sign.",
