          "claim": "Cut $V$ and $V'$ along the product meridian disks $D=D^2\\times\\{1\\}$ and $D'=D^2\\times\\{1\\}$. Each cut-open solid torus is $D^2\\times[0,1]$. After centering the interval at $0$, this convex cylinder is homeomorphic to the unit ball by radial rescaling: in direction $u=(u_1,u_2,u_3)\\in S^2$ its boundary radius is $R(u)=\\min\\{(u_1^2+u_2^2)^{-1/2},(2|u_3|)^{-1}\\}$, with a zero denominator interpreted as $+\\infty$, and $(r,u)\\mapsto rR(u)u$ gives the homeomorphism. The boundary of each cut-open torus consists of the annulus obtained by cutting the boundary torus along the meridian and two disk faces. The restriction of $h_0$ maps the annular portions to one another. Its common restriction to $\\mu$ extends over each disk face by [F1], using the same disk map on both copies. The radial disk maps send the center of each disk face to the center of its target face. These maps assemble to a homeomorphism $\\psi:\\partial B\\to\\partial B'$ between the sphere boundaries of the cut-open balls, carrying the pair of disk-face centers to that pair in the target.",
