          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $M$ be a closed linear subspace of a real or complex Hilbert space $H$. Then every $x\\in H$ has a unique decomposition\n\n$$x=m+n,\\qquad m\\in M,\\quad n\\in M^\\perp ,$$\n\nso that $H=M\\oplus M^\\perp$ as a direct sum of the subspace $M$ and its orthogonal complement.",
          "uses": [
