        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $H$ be a real or complex Hilbert space and let $f$ be a bounded linear functional on $H$ (The dual space X^* of a normed space and its dual norm). Then there is a unique $y\\in H$ with\n\n$$f(x)=\\langle x,y\\rangle\\qquad\\text{for every }x\\in H,$$\n\nand $\\|f\\|=\\|y\\|$, where $\\|f\\|$ is the dual norm (The operator norm as the least bound and as the unit-sphere or unit-ball supremum). Under the first-variable-linear convention the representing vector depends conjugate-linearly and isometrically on $f$: if $f_i$ is represented by $y_i$ and $a,b$ are scalars, then $af_1+bf_2$ is represented by $\\overline a\\,y_1+\\overline b\\,y_2$.",
          "uses": [
            "7.1",
            "8.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Put $G=\\mathrm{PSL}_2(\\mathbb C)$, $K=\\mathrm{PSU}(2)$ and $V=\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)$. Choose $X_1=\\tfrac12\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}i&0\\\\0&-i\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$, $X_2=\\tfrac12\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&0\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$ and $X_3=\\tfrac12\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}0&i\\\\i&0\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$ in $\\mathfrak k$, and put $Y_j=iX_j$. These $Y_j$ are an orthonormal tangent basis for curvature $-1$ hyperbolic space; for example $\\exp(tY_1)$ moves the basepoint distance $|t|$, and the $K$ action rotates this basis. The matrix commutators give $[X_i,X_j]=\\epsilon_{ijk}X_k$ and $[Y_i,Y_j]=i\\epsilon_{ijk}Y_k$. On $V$ let $R_j=\\operatorname{ad}Y_j$. Each $Y_j$ is Hermitian, so $R_j$ is self-adjoint for $\\langle A,B\\rangle=\\operatorname{tr}(AB^*)$, by cyclicity of trace. The $K$ action is unitary for this product.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
