            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Represent $E$-valued forms by horizontal $K$-equivariant $V$-valued forms on $Q=\\Gamma\\backslash G$, expressing their coefficients in the left Maurer–Cartan frame. Indeed a frame $g$ identifies the fiber over $gK$ with $V$ by $\\operatorname{Ad}g$, and replacing $g$ by $gk$ changes these coefficients by $\\operatorname{Ad}k^{-1}$ and rotates the tangent indices. In these coefficients write $\\varepsilon_j$ for exterior multiplication by the dual of $Y_j$ and $\\iota_j$ for contraction by $Y_j$. The ordinary covariant differential of the $K$ connection is $D=\\sum_j\\varepsilon_jY_j$, because the horizontal part of $[Y_i,Y_j]$ is zero. Differentiating the fiber change $\\operatorname{Ad}g$ gives $d_E=D+T$, where $T=\\sum_j\\varepsilon_jR_j$. These are actual coefficient formulas on all degrees, not definitions of a different connection.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "The invariant volume on $Q$ is the product of hyperbolic volume and normalized compact-fiber volume. Integration in a local bundle chart and then a partition of unity shows that integration of a $K$-invariant coefficient norm on $Q$ equals its integration on $M$. The left invariant fields $Y_j$ have zero divergence for this volume: $G$ is unimodular, since $\\operatorname{tr}(\\operatorname{ad}Z)=0$ for the displayed Lie algebra basis, hence for all $Z$, and $\\det\\operatorname{Ad}(\\exp Z)=1$. Right translation therefore preserves its Haar volume. Integration by parts on compact supports now gives $D^*=-\\sum_j\\iota_jY_j$ and $T^*=\\sum_j\\iota_jR_j$. The relations $\\varepsilon_i\\iota_j+\\iota_j\\varepsilon_i=\\delta_{ij}$ show that $DT^*+T^*D+TD^*+D^*T=0$: the two anticommutator sums are respectively $\\sum_jR_jY_j$ and its negative, since coefficient differentiation commutes with the constant matrices $R_j$. Thus $d_E\\delta_E+\\delta_Ed_E=DD^*+D^*D+H$, where $H=TT^*+T^*T$. All statements are $K$-equivariant and descend from $Q$ to $M$.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
