            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "On one-form coefficients $a=(a_1,a_2,a_3)\\in V^3$, the exterior-contraction relations give $(Ha)_i=\\sum_jR_j^2a_i+\\sum_j[R_i,R_j]a_j$. This finite-dimensional self-adjoint operator is positive definite. If $Ha=0$, positivity of $TT^*+T^*T$ gives $Ta=0$, namely $R_ia_j=R_ja_i$ for all $i,j$. Since $[R_i,R_j]=i\\epsilon_{ijk}R_k$, the commutator sum in the displayed formula is a multiple of $R_ka_j-R_ja_k$ and vanishes. Consequently $0=\\langle Ha,a\\rangle=\\sum_{i,j}\\|R_ja_i\\|^2$. Each $a_i$ commutes with all $Y_j$, which span $\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)$ over $\\mathbb C$. A matrix commuting with all traceless matrices is scalar, and a traceless scalar is zero. Thus $a=0$. Compactness of the unit sphere in $V^3$ supplies $c>0$ with $H\\ge cI$.",
