        },
        {
          "id": "step-5-1",
          "claim": "For a compactly supported smooth one-form, integration by parts in step 3.1 and step 4.1 give $\\|d_E\\alpha\\|_2^2+\\|\\delta_E\\alpha\\|_2^2=\\|D\\alpha\\|_2^2+\\|D^*\\alpha\\|_2^2+(H\\alpha,\\alpha)\\ge c\\|\\alpha\\|_2^2$. We next extend this inequality to the joint weak graph domain. On each cusp choose a smooth cutoff equal to one for $t\\le R$, zero for $t\\ge2R$, with derivative bounded by $C/R$, and set it equal to one on the compact core. These cutoffs $\\chi_R$ have compact support and $|d\\chi_R|\\le C/R$. For a weak graph-domain form $v$, the product formulas $d_E(\\chi_Rv)=\\chi_Rd_Ev+d\\chi_R\\wedge v$ and $\\delta_E(\\chi_Rv)=\\chi_R\\delta_Ev-\\iota_{\\nabla\\chi_R}v$ show convergence to $v$ in the joint graph norm. The same conclusion holds separately for each differential and codifferential and for forms of every degree. In the compact case take the cutoff identically one.",
