          "source": "lem-adjoint-hyperbolic-ltwo-one-forms-are-exact",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $M=\\Gamma\\backslash\\mathbb H^3$ be an oriented hyperbolic three-manifold with compact complement to finitely many standard torus cusp ends, each isometric to $(T^2\\times[0,\\infty),dt^2+e^{-2t}g_T)$ for a flat metric $g_T$. The compact case is allowed. Let $E=\\mathbb H^3\\times_\\Gamma\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)$ be the adjoint flat bundle. Give its fiber at a basepoint the Hilbert–Schmidt Hermitian product and transport this product by the homogeneous $\\mathrm{PSL}_2(\\mathbb C)/\\mathrm{PSU}(2)$ construction. Write $d_E$ for its flat differential and $\\delta_E$ for the metric formal adjoint.\n\nThere is $c>0$, depending only on the model normalization, such that every compactly supported smooth $E$-valued one-form satisfies\n$$\\|d_E\\alpha\\|_2^2+\\|\\delta_E\\alpha\\|_2^2\\ge c\\|\\alpha\\|_2^2.$$\nEvery smooth $E$-valued one-form $\\alpha$ with $d_E\\alpha=0$ and $\\|\\alpha\\|_2<\\infty$ has a smooth square-integrable primitive $b$, with $d_Eb=\\alpha$ and $\\|b\\|_2\\le c^{-1/2}\\|\\alpha\\|_2$.",
