          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $M$ be a compact $n$-manifold and let $A=\\partial M$; let $R$ be a commutative unital ring and $\\mathcal L$ an $R$-module local system on $M$. Cap with the canonical relative twisted fundamental class gives isomorphisms, for every integer $k$,\n$$H^k(M;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-k}(M,A;\\mathcal O_M^R\\otimes_R\\mathcal L),\\qquad H^k(M,A;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-k}(M;\\mathcal O_M^R\\otimes_R\\mathcal L).$$\nHere $\\mathcal O_M^R$ is the collar extension of the interior orientation system. The statement is for the actual boundary $A$, not an arbitrary subspace of $M$.",
