          "claim": "We compute the cusp classes and trace derivatives. Normalize the cusp lattice as $z=x+\\tau_i^0 y$, with deck translations $x\\mapsto x+1$ and $y\\mapsto y+1$, and put $F=\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}0&0\\\\1&0\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$, $H=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1)$ and $n(z)=\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}1&z\\\\0&1\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$. The forms $\\eta_i=dx\\otimes E$ and $\\omega_i=dz\\otimes\\operatorname{Ad}_{n(z)}F$ are equivariant and closed: $E$ is translation invariant and the polynomial $\\operatorname{Ad}_{n(z)}F=F+zH-z^2E$ depends only on $z$, so its derivative wedges to zero with $dz$. Their trace-paired cup product is $\\operatorname{tr}(\\eta_i\\wedge\\omega_i)=\\tau_i^0dx\\wedge dy$, while each self-pairing is zero. Thus these two classes are independent and form a basis by step 3.1. The form $\\eta_i$ is square integrable on its cusp: at height $t$, $|dx|$ grows as $e^t$ and the homogeneous norm of $E$ decays as $e^{-t}$, whereas volume decays as $e^{-2t}$.",
