          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For a fixed finite regular diagram $D$ of a nonempty oriented link $L\\subset S^3$, with $n$ crossings and a basepoint $p\\in D$ away from the crossings, choose an admissible pointed Heegaard multi-diagram subordinate to the branched-cover surgeries and the compatible perturbation data and top-generator cycles of the link-surgery construction. Its first page and first differential are isomorphic as a cochain complex over $\\mathbb F_2$ to the reduced Khovanov cochain complex of the mirror diagram $\\overline D$, based at the corresponding point, in the specified normalized grading shifts. The resulting second page is therefore the based reduced Khovanov cohomology of $\\overline D$. The isomorphism is for this fixed diagram and makes no claim about filtered chain complexes for different diagrams.",
