          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-filtered-chain-complex",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **filtered chain complex** $(C,d,F)$ in an abelian category is a chain complex with increasing filtrations $F_pC_n\\subseteq C_n$ for all $n$, whose pieces form subcomplexes. Explicitly $d_n$ factors as $F_pC_n\\to F_pC_{n-1}$ on each piece. These restrictions square to zero since their composites with the monic inclusion into $C_{n-2}$ are $d_{n-1}d_n=0$. The conventions are [[def-increasing-and-decreasing-filtration-of-an-object]] and [[def-subcomplex]]. Thus, in modules, the condition is exactly $d_n(F_pC_n)\\subseteq F_pC_{n-1}$; a factorization implies the inclusion, and the inclusion defines the restricted function. No finite-bound hypothesis is implicit.",
