ntly small integers $s$ and $F_sC=C$ for all sufficiently large integers $s$. If $H(C)\\cong\\mathbb F_2$, define\n$$\\tau(C):=\\min\\{s\\in\\mathbb Z:\\operatorname{im}(H(F_sC)\\longrightarrow H(C))\\ne0\\}.$$\nFor the fixed diagram and surface above, write $\\tau_{\\mathcal H,F}(K)=\\tau(\\widehat{CF}(\\mathcal H),F_*\\widehat{CF}(\\mathcal H))$. Once diagram and surface independence is proved, their common value is the knot invariant $\\tau(K)$. Until that comparison is proved, $\\tau_{\\mathcal H,F}(K)$ denotes only the value for the specified data.",
