          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $C$ be the normalized finite filtered hat complex for a knot and put $t=\\tau(C)$. Choose a cycle $x\\in F_tC_n$ representing the generator of $H(C)\\cong\\mathbb F_2$ in degree $n$. By minimality of $t$, every cycle in $F_{t-1}C_n$ is a boundary. Hence $x\\notin B_n+F_{t-1}C_n$, where $B_n=\\operatorname{im}(\\partial_{n+1})$; otherwise $x-b$ would be a cycle in $F_{t-1}C_n$ representing the same nonzero class. Extend a linear functional $\\lambda:C_n\\to\\mathbb F_2$ that vanishes on $B_n+F_{t-1}C_n$ and satisfies $\\lambda(x)=1$. It is a cocycle and represents the nonzero class in the dual homology, since it evaluates nontrivially on the cycle $x$. By [F3], the reflected knot's normalized Laurent complex is the R-dual with both coordinates negated. In the normalized $i=0$ hat slice, the $U^0$ terms are exactly the hat differential, while positive $U$ powers leave that slice in both original and dual complexes; transposing therefore gives the finite hat dual. Negating the Alexander coordinate gives its annihilator filtration $F_sC^\\vee=\\{\\mu:\\mu(F_{-s-1}C)=0\\}$. Thus $\\lambda\\in F_{-t}C^\\vee$, so $\\tau(C^\\vee)\\le -t$. If $s<-t$, then $-s-1\\ge t$ and every functional in $F_sC^\\vee$ annihilates $F_tC$, hence pairs trivially with $[x]$. The evaluation pairing identifies $H(C^\\vee)$ with $H(C)^\\vee$ and is nondegenerate; therefore no such lower filtration level maps nontrivially to total dual homology. This gives $\\tau(C^\\vee)\\ge -t$, and hence $\\tau(-K)=-\\tau(K)$ in the normalized knot setting.",
