        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-diagonal-five-grid-filtered-staircase-reduction",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Take the grid on $\\mathbb R^2/(5\\mathbb Z)^2$ with marks $O_r=(r+\\frac12,r+\\frac12)$ and $X_r=((r+2)\\bmod5+\\frac12,r+\\frac12)$ for $0\\le r<5$. Let $C$ have the $120$ grid states as its $\\mathbb F_2$-basis, Maslov grading $M_{\\mathbb O}$ and Alexander filtration $A_G$. Its differential counts empty directed torus rectangles avoiding every $O$ but allowing $X$; equivalently, it is the full filtered minus matrix with all five variables set to zero. Then $C$ is a filtered chain complex and is filtered chain homotopy equivalent, preserving Maslov grading, to $S\\otimes V^{\\otimes4}$. Here $S$ has basis $a,b,c$ at respective $(M,A)$ values $(0,-1),(1,0),(2,1)$ with $\\partial c=b$ and other differential zero, and $V$ has zero differential and basis at $(M,A)=(0,0),(-1,-1)$.\n\nIn particular, $H(C)$ has rank $16$. Its homology classes in Maslov degree $-k$, $0\\le k\\le4$, have multiplicity $\\binom4k$ and first appear in Alexander filtration $-1-k$. This is a calculation of the specified grid matrix; no knot type or normalized analytic knot Floer identification is asserted.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
