          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-knot-floer-mirror-complex-duality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot with a supplied regular admissible doubly pointed Heegaard diagram and normalized finite filtered hat complex $C_K$ whose total homology is $\\mathbb F_2$. Let $K^\\dagger$ be its reverse mirror under the fixed orientation-reversing reflection convention, with the reflected Seifert surface and reflected regular diagram. For a finite filtered complex $C$, define its dual complex $C^\\vee=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb F_2}(C,\\mathbb F_2)$ with transposed differential and filtration\n$$F_sC^\\vee=\\{\\lambda\\in C^\\vee:\\lambda(F_{-s-1}C)=0\\}.$$\nThen the reflected diagram's normalized filtered hat complex is filtered chain isomorphic to $C_K^\\vee$. In particular, its total homology is $\\mathbb F_2$ and\n$$\\tau_{\\mathcal H^\\dagger,F^\\dagger}(K^\\dagger)=-\\tau_{\\mathcal H,F}(K).$$",
