          "source": "lem-permissible-surface-niceification-preserves-admissibility",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "A good admissible surface-adapted balanced diagram can be made nice by a finite sequence of permissible fingers and own-family disk slides preserving its surface marking. Weak admissibility is preserved. Every complementary region of the underlying diagram disjoint from its true boundary is a bigon or square.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
