        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-relative-sutured-diagrams-have-signed-move-equivalences",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Two balanced Heegaard diagrams of the same marked sutured manifold are connected by relative attaching-circle isotopies, own-family disk slides, and ordinary stabilizations and destabilizations. An ordinary stabilization can be moved by such slides to the true boundary region. These moves induce integral chain homotopy equivalences for the transported coherent orientation class. The product sutured manifold has integral homology equal to one copy of the integers; on a homology-product branch the periodic-domain character ambiguity vanishes.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-fiber-outer-grading-and-integral-cut-euler-matrix",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the actual marked Seifert surface of genus g, oriented as minus the fiber for the cut, an adapted generator x has Alexander degree g minus the number of its interior polygon coordinates. Thus the top degree-g generators are exactly the outer generators and correspond to the cut diagram generators with their ordered intersection signs. If the integral top homology is one copy of the integers, the actual cut incidence matrix is unimodular, the cut is an integral homology product, and its periodic-domain group vanishes.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-signed-outer-summand-cut-comparison-with-zero-periodic-cut",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For an actual nice admissible good surface diagram whose cut has zero periodic-domain group, the outer differential and the cut differential are identified over the integers after changing generator signs. This identifies the top Alexander homology with the integral homology of the cut diagram when the surface is the marked Seifert surface and the outer degree is its genus. The conclusion applies in particular to a fiber cut and to the rank-one branch of the cut Euler-matrix reduction.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
