          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\ell\\ge3$, $q=e^{\\pi i/\\ell}$, and let $\\mathcal C_\\ell$ be the standard ribbon semisimplification of finite-dimensional integrable type-1 tilting modules for Lusztig's divided-power $U_q(\\mathfrak{sl}_2)$, using the positive-trace quantum ribbon convention. Then $\\mathcal C_\\ell$ is modular, with simples $a=0,\\ldots,\\ell-2$, dimensions $d_a=\\sin((a+1)\\pi/\\ell)/\\sin(\\pi/\\ell)$, twists $\\theta_a=q^{a(a+2)/2}$, and\n\n$$s_{ab}=\\frac{\\sin((a+1)(b+1)\\pi/\\ell)}{\\sin(\\pi/\\ell)},\\qquad S_{ab}=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\ell}\\sin\\frac{(a+1)(b+1)\\pi}{\\ell}.$$",
