          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a complex finite semisimple rigid tensor category with simple unit $\\mathbf 1$ and a finite set $I$ of isomorphism classes of simple objects. Fix a braiding $c$ and a ribbon twist $\\theta$. The induced pivotal map is $j_X=u_X\\theta_X:X\\to X^{\\vee\\vee}$, where $u$ is the Drinfeld morphism of [[thm-a-braided-rigid-category-has-a-drinfeld-morphism]]. Throughout this pair we use the associated spherical pivotal structure: $j$ is part of the data, and sphericality means $\\dim_j(X)=\\dim_j(X^\\vee)$ for every object, as in [[def-spherical-structure]]. Its trace is $\\operatorname{tr}_j(f)=\\operatorname{Tr}_L(j_Xf)$ for $f\\in\\operatorname{End}(X)$.\n\nWrite $0$ for the unit label and $i^*$ for the dual of $i$. Put $N_{ij}^k=\\dim_{\\mathbb C}\\operatorname{Hom}(k,i\\otimes j)$, $d_i=\\operatorname{tr}_j(1_i)$, and $s_{ij}=\\operatorname{tr}_j(c_{j,i}c_{i,j})$. Define $D^2=\\sum_{i\\in I}d_i^2$. The unnormalized Hopf-link matrix is $s=(s_{ij})$. The ribbon fusion category is **modular** when $s$ is invertible. When $D^2\\ne0$, either square root $D$ defines the normalized matrix $S=s/D$; for a modular category, [[lem-modular-hopf-matrix-squared]] proves this nonvanishing. No positivity of the general $d_i$ or of $D$ is assumed.",
