          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice for the link-invariance assertion below, via\n[[thm-the-hecke-trace-construction-is-an-oriented-link-invariant]] and its\nMarkov-equivalence supplier. Let $H(1)\\subset H(2)\\subset\\cdots$ be the Hecke tower over\n$\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[v^{\\pm1},z]$ of\n[[def-markov-trace-on-the-type-a-hecke-tower]], with $H(n)$ generated by\n$T_1,\\dots,T_{n-1}$ ([[def-generic-type-a-hecke-algebra]]). For $1\\le i\\le\nn-2$ let\n$$E^{(i)}_n:=\\sum_{w\\in\\langle s_i,s_{i+1}\\rangle}T_w$$\nbe the sum of the six standard-basis elements over the parabolic subgroup\n$\\langle s_i,s_{i+1}\\rangle\\cong S_3$ inside $H(n)$, and let $J(n)\\subset H(n)$\nbe the two-sided ideal generated by the elements $E^{(i)}_n$ for\n$1\\le i\\le n-2$ ([[def-left-right-and-two-sided-ideal]]). The **Temperley--Lieb\nquotient** of the Hecke tower is the quotient algebra\n$$\\mathrm{TL}(n):=H(n)/J(n)$$\n([[def-quotient-ring]]). Put $D:=\\Lambda[(v+1)^{-1}]$ and form\n$H_D(n):=D\\otimes_\\Lambda H(n)$ and\n$\\mathrm{TL}_D(n):=D\\otimes_\\Lambda\\mathrm{TL}(n)$. The normalized generators\nbelow are defined in these scalar extensions, where $v+1$ is a unit.\n\n**The Temperley--Lieb relations.** In $H_D(n)$ put\n$$e_i:=\\frac{T_i+1}{v+1}\\qquad(1\\le i\\le n-1),\\qquad \\lambda:=\\frac{v}{(v+1)^2}.$$\nThen $e_i^2=e_i$ and $e_ie_j=e_je_i$ for $|i-j|>1$, while in the quotient\n$\\mathrm{TL}_D(n)$ one has\n$$e_ie_{i+1}e_i=\\lambda e_i,\\qquad e_{i+1}e_ie_{i+1}=\\lambda e_{i+1} \\qquad(1\\le i\\le n-2).$$\nThese are Jones' Temperley--Lieb relations\n$e_i^2=e_i$, $e_ie_{i\\pm1}e_i=\\lambda e_i$, $e_ie_j=e_je_i$ for $|i-j|>1$\nwith loop parameter $\\lambda$. After adjoining $s$ with $s^2=v$ to $D$, the\nelements $f_i:=(v+1)s^{-1}e_i=\\lambda^{-1/2}e_i$ satisfy\n$$f_i^2=\\delta f_i,\\qquad f_if_{i+1}f_i=f_i,\\qquad f_{i+1}f_if_{i+1}=f_{i+1},\\qquad f_if_j=f_jf_i\\ (|i-j|>1),$$\nwith $\\delta:=\\lambda^{-1/2}=\\frac{v+1}{v^{1/2}}=s+s^{-1}$ when $s^2=v$.\n\n**The Jones specialization.** Let\n$z_0:=-\\frac{1}{v+1}$ and let\n$$T:=\\mathbb Z[v^{\\pm1},(v+1)^{-1},s]\\Big/\\bigl(s^2-v\\bigr)$$\nbe the ring in which $v+1$ is inverted and a square root $s$ of $v$ is\nadjoined. By the universal property of the coefficient ring\n$R$ of [[def-the-homflypt-coefficient-ring]] there is a unique unital ring\nhomomorphism $\\varphi:R\\to T$ with\n$$v\\mapsto v,\\qquad z\\mapsto z_0,\\qquad s\\mapsto s,\\qquad u\\mapsto s ;$$\nit sends $\\alpha=(uz)^{-1}\\mapsto-\\frac{s^2+1}{s}$. The **Jones\nspecialization** of the invariant $P$ of\n[[def-homflypt-polynomial-from-the-hecke-markov-trace]] is\n$$V(\\widehat\\beta):=\\varphi\\bigl(P(\\widehat\\beta)\\bigr) =s^{e(\\beta)}\\Bigl(-\\frac{s^2+1}{s}\\Bigr)^{n-1} \\operatorname{tr}_n\\bigl(\\pi_n(\\beta)\\bigr)\\Big|_{z=z_0}\\in T$$\nfor $\\beta\\in B_n$ with $n\\ge1$ and closure $\\widehat\\beta$\n([[def-closure-of-a-geometric-braid]]). Then $V$ is an invariant of nonempty oriented links with $V(\\text{unknot})=1$ and\n$$s^{-2}V(L_+)-s^{2}V(L_-)=(s-s^{-1})V(L_0)$$\non every skein triple; in the variable $t:=s^2$ this is the Jones skein\nrelation $t^{-1}V_+-tV_-=(t^{1/2}-t^{-1/2})V_0$, and $V$ is the Jones\npolynomial in the convention of Birman--Brendle §4.3 property 6: positive $\\sigma_1^3$ has value $t+t^3-t^4$. Mirroring a link replaces $t$ by $t^{-1}$; the convention is fixed, rather than chosen separately for each computation. The separate empty-link extension of $P$ specializes to $V(\\varnothing)=-s/(s^2+1)$ in $T$; that formal extension is outside the classical Jones-polynomial identification for nonempty links.\n\n**Caveats.** The quotient $\\mathrm{TL}(n)$ is defined over $\\Lambda$, but the\nnormalized generators and their displayed relations are in the base change\n$\\mathrm{TL}_D(n)$, since $v+1$ need not be a unit in $\\Lambda$. No claim is\nmade here that the Ocneanu trace on $H(n)$ factors through the quotient map\n$H(n)\\to\\mathrm{TL}(n)$; the quotient is recorded for the Temperley--Lieb\nrelations (1), and the Jones invariant is defined as the specialization of the\nlink invariant $P$, not as a trace on the quotient. What\nis proved below is the Markov normalization after scalar extension, namely\n$\\operatorname{tr}_{n+1}^+(xe_n)=\\frac{z+1}{v+1}\\operatorname{tr}_n^+(x)$ for\n$x\\in H_D(n)$, whose value at $z_0$ is $\\lambda$; this is Jones' Markov trace\nnormalization for the Temperley--Lieb parameter $\\tau=\\lambda$. The\nidentification of $V$ with the Jones polynomial uses the explicit Hecke-trace specialization in Birman--Brendle §4.3 property 6, quoted in [F6]. That source also supplies the relation on arbitrary oriented skein triples; the local skein supplier proves the braided triples.",
