 multiplication. The compact SVD expansion gives $\\langle Kx,u_j\\rangle_Y=s_j\\theta_j$, and the positive-noise white-noise coordinate theorem gives the independent standard-normal coordinates $\\xi_j$. Hence the normalized coordinates satisfy $Z_j=\\theta_j+\\epsilon s_j^{-1}\\xi_j,\\qquad j\\in\\mathbb N.$\n\nFor the zero-noise boundary $\\epsilon=0$, define the sequence experiment separately by the point mass at $\\theta$, so $Z_j=\\theta_j$. This boundary is not an instance of the positive-noise functional experiment.",
