          "quote": "Let $V=D^2\\times S^1$ and $V'=D^2\\times S^1$ be solid tori, with meridian curves $\\mu=\\partial D^2\\times\\{1\\}$ and $\\mu'=\\partial D^2\\times\\{1\\}$. Suppose $h:\\partial V\\to\\partial V'$ is a homeomorphism and there is an isotopy $H_t:\\partial V'\\to\\partial V'$ through homeomorphisms, with $H_0=\\mathrm{id}$, such that $H_1(h(\\mu))=\\mu'$. Then $h$ extends to a homeomorphism $\\overline h:V\\to V'$. The extension may be chosen to carry the product core $\\{0\\}\\times S^1$ onto the product core of $V'$, and has the same orientation sign as $h$ with respect to the boundary orientations.",
