        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-linear-map",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $V$ and $W$ be vector spaces over the same field $F$. A function\n$T:V\\to W$ is **linear** when\n\n$$T(au+bv)=aT(u)+bT(v)$$\n\nfor all $a,b\\in F$ and $u,v\\in V$. Such a function is a **linear map**, or\n**linear transformation**.",
          "uses": [
