      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "log-index-concavity",
          "claim": "For $0<t<t_0$, put $L=-\\log t$. Differentiation gives $\\psi'(t)=\\nu/(tL^{\\nu+1})$ and $\\psi''(t)=\\nu((\\nu+1)-L)/(t^2L^{\\nu+2})<0$, since $L\\ge-\\log t_0>\\nu+1$. Thus $\\psi'$ decreases on $(0,t_0)$ and has positive left limit at $t_0$; after $t_0$ the function is constant, so its derivative drops to zero and remains nonincreasing. Also $\\psi(t)\\to0$ as $t\\downarrow0$. Therefore its continuous extension at zero is nondecreasing, concave on $[0,\\infty)$, vanishes at zero and is positive for $t>0$, as required by [F1].",
