        {
          "id": "derive-2-1",
          "claim": "Let $z/s\\in C_1\\otimes_\\Lambda Q$ be a fraction-field cycle, with $z\\in C_1$ and $0\\ne s\\in\\Lambda$. Since $d_1(z)/s=0$ and each coordinate of $C_0$ lies in the domain $\\Lambda$, $d_1(z)=0$. The torsion hypothesis gives $0\\ne f\\in\\Lambda$ and $w\\in C_2$ with $fz=d_2(w)$. Hence $z/s=d_2(w/(fs))$, so every fraction-field $1$-cycle is a boundary and $H_1(C_*\\otimes Q)=0$.",
