          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice convention of the twisted-chain definition. Let $X$ be a certified based deficiency-one exterior spine with one $0$-cell, $n\\ge2$ $1$-cells and $n-1$ $2$-cells, let $\\psi:\\pi_1(X)\\twoheadrightarrow H\\cong\\mathbb Z^m$ have $m\\ge1$, let $\\rho:\\pi_1(X)\\to\\mathrm{GL}_d(\\mathbb F)$, and let $H_1(C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;\\mathbb F[H]^d))$ be torsion over $\\mathbb F[H]$. Form the Fox block matrix $J$ and a chosen Wada column quotient $W_j=\\det(J_{\\widehat j})/D_j$ with $D_j=\\det(\\rho(x_j)\\psi(x_j)-I_d)\\ne0$. Then the fraction-field complex is acyclic, $\\det(J_{\\widehat j})\\ne0$, and $W_j$ equals its based twisted Reidemeister torsion in $Q^\\times/\\mathcal U_{\\rho,\\psi}$. Every admissible deleted column gives the same class. This conclusion applies only to the specified cellular spine; an abstract presentation of the same group is insufficient.",
