vention that torsion is zero on a nonacyclic fraction-field complex, if the twisted complex of $X$ is acyclic then its torsion is represented by $N/D$ modulo the exact determinant and deck-unit subgroup of the coefficient system. If the complex is nonacyclic then $N=0$ and $\\tau(X)=N/D=0$ in $Q$. The acyclic identity follows from the braid-axis filling product.\n\nThe diagram records only the supplied gluing certificate; it is schematic and is not a substitute for the cell or spine data.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth, node distance=2.5cm]\n  \\node (T) {$T$};\n  \\node (Y) [right of=T] {$Y$};\n  \\node (V) [below of=T] {$V=D^2\\times S^1$};\n  \\node (X) [right of=V] {$X=Y\\cup_TV$};\n  \\draw[->] (T) -- node[above] {inclusion} (Y);\n  \\draw[->] (T) -- node[left] {inclusion} (V);\n  \\draw[->] (Y) -- node[right] {glue along $T$} (X);\n  \\draw[->] (V) -- node[below] {glue along $T$} (X);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```",
