          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $L$ be a nonempty oriented smooth $r$-component link with $r\\ge1$, compact exterior $E_L=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(L)$ obtained from pairwise-disjoint closed normal disk tubes, a finite oriented simplicial triangulation $K$ of $E_L$ with ordered vertices and simplices, with least vertex $v_0$ as the basepoint used in the cover definition, and one certified positive-meridian edge loop $\\mu_i$ per component. Orient each normal disk so the positive tangent to its component followed by the positive disk basis agrees with the orientation of $S^3$, and assume the resulting classes form the standard basis of $H_1(E_L;\\mathbb Z)$. If an integer-vector edge labeling is antisymmetric under edge reversal, sums to zero on every oriented 2-simplex, and evaluates to the $i$th standard basis vector on $\\mu_i$, then the chain procedure returns a finite free chain complex over $\\Lambda_r=\\mathbb Z[t_1^{\\pm1},\\ldots,t_r^{\\pm1}]$. The first homology of this complex is the absolute maximal-abelian-cover Alexander module $A_L$. Its Fitting ideals are independent of the triangulation and cell lifts, and its order is defined up to multiplication by a unit $\\pm t_1^{k_1}\\cdots t_r^{k_r}$.",
