          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice convention of the twisted-chain definition. Let a finite colored geometric braid, a field with exact arithmetic, a representation of the closure exterior group, the full positive-meridian abelianization followed by a declared surjective color map, and compatible based spine and axis-filling certificates satisfy all input conditions of the colored twisted Burau procedure. Assume its designated denominator $D=\\det(\\rho(g_n)\\psi(g_n)-I_d)$ is nonzero, so the procedure is applicable, and assume the representation and deck map extend over the filling with the axis meridian acting trivially. Then the procedure returns the class of the twisted Reidemeister torsion of the closure exterior. If the fraction-field complex is acyclic, the returned value is $N/D$, where $N=\\det(\\overline B_\\rho(\\beta)-I_{(n-1)d})$; if it is nonacyclic, the procedure returns $0$ and $N=0$, in agreement with the declared zero-torsion convention. The geometric certificates are essential hypotheses: matching a group presentation alone does not certify an exterior spine or the axis-filling decomposition.",
