        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-temperley-lieb-diagram-category-laws",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every commutative ring $R$, loop value $\\delta\\in R$, and objects $m,n,p,q\\ge0$, the raw diagram data of [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]] form a strict monoidal category $\\mathcal{TL}_R(\\delta)$ with hom-modules $M_R(m,n)$ and the stated $R$-bilinear stacking composition. Composition is associative, the identity diagrams are two-sided identities, and horizontal juxtaposition is a strict monoidal bifunctor with unit object $0$. Consequently $\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathcal{TL}_R(\\delta)}(n)=\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$ is a unital associative $R$-algebra whose underlying $R$-module is free on its noncrossing pairing diagrams.",
          "uses": [
