        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Use source coordinates $(u,v)$ with their standard positive orientation and positive projection coordinates $(t,x)$ on the braid box. For $h>0$, the map $(t,x)=(v,-2hu)$ has determinant $2h>0$. It sends the source over direction $(1,1)$ to $(1,-2h)$ and the source under direction $(-1,1)$ to $(1,2h)$, whose determinant is $4h>0$. The source left/right pairs have constant $u$, hence constant braid position $x$ and give the through pairing $I$; the source top/bottom pairs have constant $v$, hence constant braid time $t$ and give the cup-cap $e_i$. The displayed page coordinates $(x,t)$ reverse the positive projection orientation; their visual quarter-turn is not the orientation comparison. For the opposite crossing, rotating the source chart by a positive quarter-turn exchanges the two endpoint pairings, so its A/B smoothings are respectively $e_i$ and $I$. By [F1] these expansions are $C_i=AI+A^{-1}e_i$ and $C_i^{-}=A^{-1}I+Ae_i$. Using [F2] and [F3], $$C_iC_i^{-}=(AI+A^{-1}e_i)(A^{-1}I+Ae_i)=I+(A^2+A^{-2}+\\delta)e_i=I.$$ The same multiplication in the other order gives $C_i^{-}C_i=I$, since both factors are polynomials in $e_i$. Thus the two opposite crossings in an R2 pair cancel in either order.",
