          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Label the crossing ports northwest $1$, northeast $2$, southeast $3$, and southwest $4$, in the chart of [F1]. The over-strand joins $4$ to $2$ and the under-strand joins $1$ to $3$. For the left exterior cap $(1,4)$ the remaining ports are $2,3$. Orient its through strand from $2$ to $3$: it traverses the over-strand northeast to southwest, then the cap, then the under-strand northwest to southeast. The tangent vectors may be taken as $(-1,-1)$ and $(1,-1)$, whose determinant is $2>0$. This is a positive kink. The A-pairing $(1,4)(2,3)$ closes one additional circle against the cap; the B-pairing $(1,2)(3,4)$ gives just the through arc. Hence its bracket factor is $A\\delta+A^{-1}=-A^3$. Reversing the component negates both tangent vectors and preserves the determinant.",
