          "quote": "Let $X$ be a real Banach space, let $R:X\\to(-\\infty,+\\infty]$ be proper and convex, choose $x^\\dagger\\in\\operatorname{dom}R$, and choose $\\xi^\\dagger\\in\\partial R(x^\\dagger)$. For $x\\in\\operatorname{dom}R$, the **Bregman distance** generated by $\\xi^\\dagger$ from the reference point $x^\\dagger$ to $x$ is\n\n$$D_R^{\\xi^\\dagger}(x,x^\\dagger):=R(x)-R(x^\\dagger)-\\langle\\xi^\\dagger,x-x^\\dagger\\rangle_{X^*,X}.$$\n\nThe subgradient inequality makes this quantity nonnegative, and $D_R^{\\xi^\\dagger}(x^\\dagger,x^\\dagger)=0$. The definition fixes the orientation: the first argument is the comparison point and the second is the reference point carrying the chosen subgradient.",
