          "source": "lem-ip-logarithmic-endpoint-under-effective-noise-control",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix $p,\\nu,a,C_*,C>0$ and let $\\psi$ be a continuous nondecreasing concave source index with $\\psi(0)=0$. Suppose its conjugate $H(q)=\\sup_{t\\ge0}(\\psi(t)-qt)$ satisfies $H(q)\\le C(\\log q)^{-\\nu}$ for all sufficiently large $q$. Let $\\delta\\downarrow0$ be a nominal parameter, and put $L_\\delta=\\log(1/\\delta)$. Suppose nonnegative errors satisfy\n$$S_\\delta+a\\alpha_\\delta e_\\delta\\le d_\\delta+\\alpha_\\delta\\psi(C_*S_\\delta),\\qquad \\alpha_\\delta\\asymp\\delta^p,\\qquad d_\\delta=O(\\delta^pL_\\delta^{-\\nu}).$$\nThen\n$$e_\\delta=O(L_\\delta^{-\\nu}),\\qquad S_\\delta=O(\\delta^pL_\\delta^{-\\nu}).$$\nFor the joint objective estimate with actual data noise $\\varepsilon_\\delta=\\|y^\\delta-y\\|$, the hypothesis on $d_\\delta$ is supplied by $2\\varepsilon_\\delta^p+\\eta_\\delta=O(\\delta^pL_\\delta^{-\\nu})$. This condition explicitly strengthens the usual nominal bound $\\varepsilon_\\delta\\le\\delta$, $\\eta_\\delta=O(\\delta^p)$ at the endpoint. If $e_\\delta=\\frac12\\|u_\\delta-u^\\dagger\\|^2$, the norm rate is $O(L_\\delta^{-\\nu/2})$.\n\nThe universal assertion that $\\alpha\\asymp\\delta^2$ yields a vanishing norm error for every deterministic noise family bounded by $\\delta$ is false, even for an exact quadratic Tikhonov minimizer and a truth satisfying every nonnegative variational source inequality: on real $\\ell^2$, take $Ke_j=j^{-1}e_j$, $x^\\dagger=0$, $y^{\\delta_j}=\\delta_j e_j$, $\\delta_j=1/j$, $\\alpha_j=\\delta_j^2$, and objective $\\|Kx-y^{\\delta_j}\\|^2+\\frac{\\alpha_j}{2}\\|x\\|^2$. Its unique minimizer is $2e_j/3$. This counterexample refutes the universal abstract endpoint assertion; it makes no assertion that these data arise from an EIT conductivity map.",
