          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice and Dependent Choice. Use $\\mathcal H_\\ell$ from [[def-spherical-harmonic-partial-wave-conventions]]. For every $\\ell\\ge0$, $\\dim_\\mathbb C\\mathcal H_\\ell=2\\ell+1$; the spaces $\\mathcal H_\\ell$ are pairwise orthogonal in $L^2(S^2,d\\sigma;\\mathbb C)$ and their algebraic sum is dense there. Thus they give a complete orthogonal spherical-harmonic expansion. For any orthonormal basis $Y_{\\ell 1},\\ldots,Y_{\\ell,2\\ell+1}$ of $\\mathcal H_\\ell$, the basis-independent reproducing kernel\n$$Z_\\ell(\\omega,\\eta):=\\sum_{m=1}^{2\\ell+1}Y_{\\ell m}(\\omega)\\overline{Y_{\\ell m}(\\eta)}$$\nsatisfies $Z_\\ell(\\omega,\\omega)=(2\\ell+1)/(4\\pi)$. In particular,\n$$|g(\\omega)|\\le\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\ell+1}{4\\pi}}\\,\\|g\\|_{L^2(S^2)}\\qquad(g\\in\\mathcal H_\\ell).$$\nFor fixed $\\eta$, rotational invariance makes $Z_\\ell(\\omega,\\eta)$ a degree-$\\ell$ zonal polynomial of $\\omega\\cdot\\eta$; normalizing $P_\\ell(1)=1$ gives the usual addition identity $Z_\\ell(\\omega,\\eta)=\\frac{2\\ell+1}{4\\pi}P_\\ell(\\omega\\cdot\\eta)$.",
