          "source": "lem-ip-logarithmic-index-conjugate-and-parameter-rates",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix $C,\\nu>0$ and $0<t_0<e^{-(\\nu+1)}$. Define $\\psi(0)=0$, $\\psi(t)=C[\\log(1/t)]^{-\\nu}$ for $0<t\\le t_0$, and $\\psi(t)=\\psi(t_0)$ for $t>t_0$. Then $\\psi$ is continuous, nondecreasing and concave, and\n$$H(q):=\\sup_{t\\ge0}(\\psi(t)-qt)\\sim C(\\log q)^{-\\nu}\\qquad(q\\to\\infty).$$\nFor each fixed $c>0$, one consequently has $H(cq)/H(q)\\to1$. For $p>0$, fixed $D,a,C_*>0$ and nonnegative errors satisfying\n$$S_\\delta+a\\alpha e_\\delta\\le D\\delta^p+\\alpha\\psi(C_*S_\\delta),$$\nthe balanced choice $\\alpha\\asymp\\delta^p[\\log(1/\\delta)]^\\nu$ gives\n$$e_\\delta=O([\\log(1/\\delta)]^{-\\nu}),\\qquad S_\\delta=O(\\delta^p).$$\nFor a pure-power choice $\\alpha\\asymp\\delta^k$ with $0<k<p$, the same error rate follows, with residual bound $S_\\delta=O(\\delta^k[\\log(1/\\delta)]^{-\\nu})$. No assertion for $k=p$ is made. If $e_\\delta=\\frac12\\|u_\\delta-u^\\dagger\\|^2$, the corresponding norm rate has exponent $\\nu/2$.",
