      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Addition and multiplication of residue classes are well-defined because congruence modulo $p$ is preserved by sums and products. If $\\bar r\\ne0$ in $\\mathbb Z/p\\mathbb Z$, choose an integer representative $r$ not divisible by $p$. Since $p$ is prime, $\\gcd(r,p)=1$; Bézout's identity gives integers $u,v$ with $ur+vp=1$, so $\\bar u\\bar r=1$. Hence the residue classes form a field. For fixed $b$, the right translation is $R_b(a)=2b-a$ and satisfies $R_b(R_b(a))=2b-(2b-a)=a$. It is therefore a bijection.",
