          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Each crossing contributes one linear equation in the $a$ arc variables, so the algorithm forms a $c\\times a$ matrix over $\\mathbb F_p$. Addition and multiplication of residue classes are well-defined because congruence modulo $p$ is preserved by sums and products. If a residue $r$ is nonzero, then $\\gcd(r,p)=1$, so integers $u,v$ satisfy $ur+vp=1$ and $u$ is the inverse of $r$ modulo $p$. The field hypothesis in [A1] therefore supplies every division used by the pivot instructions in [F1].",
