          "claim": "Each Fourier multiplier commutes with translation because the kth translated Fourier coefficient is multiplied by the scalar $e^{-ik\\alpha}$, which commutes with its channel matrix. Every constant channel matrix, constant bias and coordinatewise scalar activation also commutes with translation. By induction through the lift, all layers and output map, the realized scalar output field is translation-equivariant. The layer fields are in $L^2$: a globally Lipschitz activation has linear growth, the pointwise weights are finite and the finite Fourier multipliers are bounded. For odd $m$, projection onto the first m coefficients commutes with translation by [A1]. Hence the zero-extended output map $F=I_m\\Psi_m$ satisfies $F(U_\\alpha x)=T_\\alpha F(x)$, where $U_\\alpha$ is the orthogonal translation matrix on the retained coefficients. This holds for every individual parameter array, also after data-dependent selection.",
