      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "lem-ip-schwartz-radon-well-defined-1.1",
          "claim": "Fix a derivative multi-index $\\beta$ and an integer $N\\ge1$, and choose an integer $m\\ge N$. Since $(1+|x|)^N\\le(1+|x_1|)^m(1+|x_2|)^m$, expanding the right side and using the finite Schwartz seminorms in [F1] gives a finite $C_{\\beta,N}(f)$ with $|\\partial^\\beta f(x)|\\le C_{\\beta,N}(f)(1+|x|)^{-N}$. For $x=s\\theta+t\\theta^\\perp$, orthogonality gives $|x|=(s^2+t^2)^{1/2}\\ge(|s|+|t|)/\\sqrt2$, so the line integrand is bounded by a constant times $(1+|s|+|t|)^{-N}$. Taking $N>1$ makes this majorant integrable in $t$, proving absolute convergence.",
