          "id": "lem-ip-schwartz-radon-well-defined-2.1",
          "claim": "Let $D_\\theta=\\theta\\cdot\\nabla$. The chain rule [F4] gives $\\partial_s^k f(s\\theta+t\\theta^\\perp)=(D_\\theta^k f)(s\\theta+t\\theta^\\perp)$. Expanding $D_\\theta^k$ gives finitely many partial derivatives with coefficients bounded uniformly for $\\theta\\in S^1$. For the target decay order $N$, apply step 1.1 with spatial decay order $N+2$ to each such derivative. Integrating $(1+|s|+|t|)^{-N-2}$ in $t$ gives $\\left|\\int_{\\mathbb R}(D_\\theta^k f)(s\\theta+t\\theta^\\perp)\\,dt\\right|\\le C'_{k,N}(1+|s|)^{-N-1}\\le C'_{k,N}(1+|s|)^{-N}$, uniformly in $\\theta$ and $s$.",
