        {
          "id": "lem-ip-limited-angle-radon-data-is-l2-on-compact-support-1.1",
          "claim": "Choose $R>0$ with $\\operatorname{supp}f\\subseteq\\overline B_R(0)$. If $|t|>R$, then $|s\\theta+t\\theta^\\perp|\\ge|t|>R$ and the integrand in [F1] is zero. On any compact set of $(\\theta,s)$, uniform continuity of $f$ on the compact image of $(s,\\theta,t)$ for $|t|\\le R$ shows that the line integrals vary continuously: the difference of two such integrals is at most $2R$ times the uniform difference of their integrands. Hence the data function is continuous and measurable.",
