          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every $f\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^2;\\mathbb C)$, every unit normal $\\theta\\in S^1$, and every $\\sigma\\in\\mathbb R$, the compact-support Fourier transform of the line data in the offset variable equals the restriction of the two-dimensional Fourier transform to the line in frequency space with direction $\\theta$:\n$$\\widehat{Rf}(\\theta,\\sigma)=\\widehat f(\\sigma\\theta).$$",
