          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\Theta\\subset S^1$ be a nonempty proper open set of line normals, assume $\\theta\\in\\Theta$ if and only if $-\\theta\\in\\Theta$, and assume $S^1\\setminus\\overline{\\Theta}$ contains a nonempty open arc. The measured line with normal $\\theta$ and signed offset $s$ is $\\ell_{\\theta,s}=\\{y\\in\\mathbb R^2:y\\cdot\\theta=s\\}$. Identify the nonzero cotangent vectors of the Euclidean plane with pairs $(x,\\xi)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\times(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\{0\\})$. Such a covector is visible from $\\Theta$ when $\\xi/|\\xi|\\in\\Theta$, and invisible when $\\xi/|\\xi|\\notin\\Theta$. The associated measured Fourier wedge is\n\n$$W_\\Theta=\\{\\sigma\\theta:\\theta\\in\\Theta,\\ \\sigma\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}\\}.$$",
