          "claim": "Choose a bicollar of $T_K$ in $S^3$ and thicken $E_K$ and $N(K)$ slightly to an open cover. The two sets deformation-retract to $E_K$ and $N(K)$, and their intersection deformation-retracts to $T_K$. By [F1] and [F2], the segment $H_2(S^3;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)\\oplus H_1(N(K);\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(S^3;\\mathbb Z)$ has zero groups at both ends, so the middle map is an isomorphism.",
