          "source": "def-heegaard-splitting-of-closed-oriented-three-manifold",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For $g\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}$, an **orientable handlebody of genus $g$** is a compact connected orientable smooth $3$-manifold obtained from a $3$-ball by attaching $g$ smooth $1$-handles along orientation-compatible pairs of disjoint boundary disks and rounding the corners. A $1$-handle here is a copy of $D^2\\times[-1,1]$ attached by its two end disks to those boundary disks. Its boundary is a connected closed orientable surface of genus $g$. A **Heegaard splitting** of a closed connected oriented smooth $3$-manifold $M$ is a decomposition\n$$\nM=H_-\\cup_{\\varphi}H_+\n$$\nin which $H_-$ and $H_+$ are orientable handlebodies of the same genus, their common boundary is a connected closed surface $\\Sigma=\\partial H_-=\\partial H_+$, and $\\varphi:\\partial H_-\\to\\partial H_+$ is an orientation-reversing diffeomorphism whose gluing gives $M$. The surface $\\Sigma$ is the **Heegaard surface** of the splitting.",
