        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "In the barycentric subdivision, thicken the finite embedded $1$-skeleton by taking disjoint small $3$-balls at its vertices and disjoint narrow tubes around the edge interiors, each tube meeting its endpoint balls in end disks. The vertex balls joined by the tubes along a spanning tree form a $3$-ball: adding a leaf ball and its joining tube joins two balls along a tube and again gives a ball. Each remaining edge tube attaches along two disks to this connected boundary and is one $1$-handle. There are $|E|-|V|+1$ such edges; the cycles formed by each non-tree edge with its spanning-tree path form a basis of the graph's first homology, so this number is $b_1$. The resulting connected orientable manifold is a handlebody of genus $b_1$ by the definition.",
          "step": "2.1",
