        {
          "id": "step-2-2",
          "claim": "In the barycentric dual cell structure, put one vertex in each tetrahedron and join two such vertices through the barycentre of each common triangular face. This dual graph is connected: choose a piecewise-linear path between interior points of any two tetrahedra and perturb its finitely many segments inside simplex stars so it avoids the primal $1$-skeleton and meets triangular faces transversely. Each crossing then passes between tetrahedra sharing that face, producing a finite path in the dual graph.",
