          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "**Framing bookkeeping from bands.** For oriented components $A,B$ with integers $a,b$ and linking number $l$, a slide of $A$ over $sB$, $s=\\pm1$, has framing $a+b+2sl$. Indeed choose small framed parallels and the parallel band. The linking of the new curve with its parallel is the sum of the old self-linkings $a,b$ and the two cross-linkings $sl,sl$; the two bands have disjoint interiors and contribute no further crossing. Its linking with a third component $C$ is $\\operatorname{lk}(A,C)+s\\operatorname{lk}(B,C)$. These are consequences of the actual parallel-and-band construction, not permissions to replace a geometric link by a matrix. We use bands with no added full twist; an existing twist of any component is carried with its strip.",
