opy and framed slides of open graph strands over the specified surgery-framed longitudes. Every original graph label, coupon morphism, attachment order, boundary ribbon and endpoint remains fixed or is transported by the recorded move map.\n\nThus the cumulative move map, with its transported graph, realizes the given marked decorated bordism, including its specified output identification. No hypothesis on any fundamental group is imposed. $O3$ is essential in this general fixed-base scope and is not silently replaced by a split Hopf pair or by $O1/O2$ alone. All supports fix the given external collars; no unproved variable-boundary slicing move list is required. Disconnected bordisms, empty input/output surfaces, closed components, empty graphs and the empty bordism are allowed, with the fixed component partition. Any integer weight and object Lagrangians of the weighted ribbon-bordism definition are retained as part of the external data; this is a presentation and move theorem, independently of the later evaluation and anomaly formulas.",
