          "quote": "Let $T=\\mathbb R^2/\\mathbb Z^2$ be oriented by $dx\\wedge dy$, and identify $H_1(T;\\mathbb Z)$ with $\\mathbb Z^2$ in the standard basis, so the algebraic intersection of classes $v,w$ is $\\det(v,w)$. Let $\\gamma_0,\\gamma_1\\subset T$ be smooth embedded circles that are not null-homotopic. Orient them so that their homology classes agree, and suppose their common class $v\\in H_1(T;\\mathbb Z)$ is primitive, meaning it is not an integer multiple $m u$ with $|m|>1$. Then $\\gamma_0$ and $\\gamma_1$ are isotopic through embedded circles in $T$.",
