          "source": "lem-earring-relative-arc-data-supply-admissible-orbifold-and-determinant-lifts",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Use the actual based earring $K\\cup L\\subset S^3$, its normal radius arc $\\omega$, the compact exterior $X$ and a supplied $SO(3)$ bundle $P\\to X$ with $w_2(P)=PD_{\\mathbb F_2}[\\omega]$ in the singular-data definition. Both boundary-torus restrictions of $P$ have nonzero $w_2$. The bundle admits a compatible extension to an order-two orbifold bundle over $(S^3,K\\cup L)$ whose local isotropy is rotation by $\\pi$, whose axis-orientation cover on each link component is nontrivial, and whose ordinary local singular residue is $\\frac14\\operatorname{diag}(i,-i)d\\theta$ up to conjugation. It therefore supplies the compatible finite local data required by the order-two gauge-completion lemma.\n\nFor this completed data every connection has determinant-one stabilizer exactly $\\{\\pm1\\}$. The bundle on the exterior also has an actual $U(2)$ lift with a chosen determinant line and determinant connection, as needed for cylinder holonomy functions. These statements concern the topology and analytic input data, not independence of the resulting choices or construction of Floer homology. The supplied-bundle existence clause of the original definition is retained; this result does not classify all singular extensions up to canonical isomorphism.",
