          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Supply a compact oriented three-dimensional order-two singular pair $(Y,K)$, compatible orbifold bundle data and determinant-one gauges as in the preceding completion lemma, and a fixed $U(2)$ lift on $Y\\setminus K$ with fixed determinant connection. Suppose every connection in this singular configuration space has stabilizer $\\{\\pm1\\}$. Use $H^k/H^{k+1}$, $k\\ge3$.\n\nThere is a separable Banach space $\\mathcal P$ of countable weighted sums of smooth cylinder functions supported away from $K$. For $\\pi\\in\\mathcal P$ its function $f_\\pi$ is bounded, smooth and gauge invariant, and its $L^2$ gradient $V_\\pi$ is a smooth gauge-equivariant $H^k$ vector field. It is uniformly pointwise bounded by $C\\|\\pi\\|_{\\mathcal P}$, independently of the connection; its derivative is bounded on $L^2$ with the same type of uniform bound. Its spatial covariant derivatives have polynomial bounds in lower spatial covariant derivatives of curvature, with constants uniform on bounded perturbation sets.\n\nThe critical-point projection for $*F_B+V_\\pi(B)=0$ is proper over compact subsets of $\\mathcal P$ in the actual $H^k$ quotient. An open dense subset of $\\mathcal P$ has only nondegenerate critical points; their set is finite. All critical connections are smooth in orbifold gauges. This result proves the critical set and not transversality, compactness or gluing for nonconstant trajectories. The existence of the stipulated global singular data and $U(2)$ lift is not asserted here.",
