          "source": "thm-based-link-earring-complexes-and-resolution-unlink-groups-are-well-defined",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. For any smooth based link $L\\subset S^3$ with a chosen nonzero normal vector at its marked point, add the small meridional earring on that marked component and its joining arc. With the corresponding determinant-one singular bundle data, finite nondegenerate critical points and all-index regular holonomy perturbations give a finite free integral cochain complex. Its differential counts all index-one classes and has square zero; its homology, denoted $I^\\natural(L;\\mathbb Z)$, is independent of regular metric and perturbation and invariant under isotopy of the based link data, with the same orientation sign convention as for knots. For a knot it agrees with the singular knot complex already constructed.\n\nFor the standard $n$-component unlink with a marked component, $n\\ge1$, this group is free of rank $2^{n-1}$. It has a chosen representative complex with zero differential and sphere-pole generators, in the even relative degrees of the unlink model. This theorem does not supply a canonical tensor-product identification under arbitrary cobordisms, saddle maps, an exact triangle or a KHI identification.",
