ted blocks. Use their existing product metrics on every boundary chart and extend over the remaining compact interior by a finite partition in the convex cone of positive metrics. Here the background compatibility can be made literal. Put the planar resolution curves and the saddle surfaces in projection-plane times time; a local saddle has graph $t=x^2-y^2$ and normal coordinate $z=0$. The constant viewing-normal vector $\\partial_z$ is a nonzero normal section on every such panel and every unchanged planar strand strip. Fix the product normal model on the separate earring annulus. Thus the normal splitting in [F2] uses the SAME section on every cube face, rather than separately chosen graph-spine sections. The sheet cover is cut along the SAME vertical marking arcs, outside all crossing balls. Construct the exterior determinant line by the degree-one angular Thom clutch around the fixed marking rectangle; it is the fixed product line outside the crossing balls and the fixed trivial line inside each ball, since the rectangle misses them. On the normal tube use the explicit common sheet gluing $\\rho(v)w=v\\bar w$ of [F2], with these normal coordinates. Restriction at an intermediate resolution, and commuting two disjoint saddles, now preserve these very transition functions and their determinant trivializations. Hence all backgrounds and all corner identifications agree as actual gluing data. Relative perturbations from [F2], by induction on $k$, therefore agree on all corners.",
