          "source": "lem-instanton-knot-complex-asd-analytic-foundations",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC and fix a smooth based knot $K\\subset S^3$ with the earring and admissible singular bundle data of the preceding definitions. For regular perturbation data, the perturbed Chern–Simons critical points and finite-energy singular anti-self-dual trajectories define a finite free cochain complex $C^\\natural(K;\\mathbb Z)$ with differential $d$ satisfying $d^2=0$. Its homology is independent of the chosen regular metric and perturbation up to the declared overall sign and is invariant under isotopy of the based knot data.",
