          "quote": "Let $X$ be a separable real Banach space with norm $\\|\\cdot\\|_X$, let $D\\subseteq X$ be Borel, and let $\\mu_0$ be a Borel probability on $X$ with $\\mu_0(D)=1$. Here $\\mathcal B(X)$ is generated by the norm-open sets. Give $D$ the relative topology and Borel sigma-algebra $\\mathcal B(D)=\\{D\\cap B:B\\in\\mathcal B(X)\\}$, and let $\\mu_{0,D}$ be the restriction of $\\mu_0$ to $D$, so $\\mu_{0,D}(A)=\\mu_0(A)$ for $A\\in\\mathcal B(D)$. Let $(\\mathsf Y,\\mathcal Y)$ be a measurable data space. Assume $\\Phi:D\\times\\mathsf Y\\to(-\\infty,+\\infty]$ is measurable from $\\bigl(D\\times\\mathsf Y,\\mathcal B(D)\\otimes\\mathcal Y\\bigr)$ to $\\bigl((-\\infty,+\\infty],\\mathcal B((-\\infty,+\\infty])\\bigr)$, where $\\mathcal B(\\overline{\\mathbb R})$ is generated by the order topology on the extended real line and $\\mathcal B((-\\infty,+\\infty])$ is its trace on $(-\\infty,+\\infty]$; thus $+\\infty$ is allowed and $-\\infty$ is excluded. Let $\\mathsf Y_0\\subseteq\\mathsf Y$. Suppose that for every $y\\in\\mathsf Y_0$, the section $u\\mapsto\\Phi(u;y)$ is finite and continuous as a real-valued function on $D$ with its relative topology inherited from the norm topology. Suppose there is one Borel function $M_1:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, independent of $y\\in\\mathsf Y_0$, such that\n$$\\Phi(u;y)\\ge -M_1(\\|u\\|_X)\\quad(u\\in D,\\ y\\in\\mathsf Y_0),\\qquad \\int_D e^{M_1(\\|u\\|_X)}\\,\\mu_{0,D}(du)<\\infty.$$\nDefine $\\operatorname{supp}\\mu_0:=\\{x\\in X:\\mu_0(U)>0\\text{ for every open neighborhood }U\\text{ of }x\\}$. Then for every $y\\in\\mathsf Y_0$, the evidence $Z_\\Phi(y)$ is finite and strictly positive, and the normalized fiberwise update $\\Pi^y$ is a probability measure on $D$.",
