          "claim": "For fixed $b\\in\\mathbb F_p$, define $R_b(a)=a*b=2b-a$. Then $R_b(R_b(a))=2b-(2b-a)=a$, so $R_b^{-1}=R_b$. Also $a*a=2a-a=a$. Thus both the forward and reverse crossing rules use the same involution, and an arc's color is uniquely recoverable across one underpass.",
