          "claim": "Let $e_G:=R^G_\\alpha z-y^\\dagger$. On each $y_j$, $I_Y-R^G_\\alpha G$ has multiplier $p^G_\\alpha(\\mu_j^2)$, whose absolute value is at most $S_G$ because $I_Z-GR^G_\\alpha$ has that same multiplier on $z_j$. Thus $e_G=-|G|^\\nu p^G_\\alpha(G^*G)v=|G|^\\nu v'$ with $\\|v'\\|\\le S_G\\|v\\|\\le S_G\\rho$. Also $Ge_G=GR^G_\\alpha z-z$. The difference between the exact and noisy first residuals is $(GR^G_\\alpha-I_Z)(z-z^\\delta)$, of norm at most $S_G\\delta$; the stopping inequality therefore gives $\\|Ge_G\\|\\le(\\tau_G+S_G)\\delta$. Applying [F8] to $e_G=|G|^\\nu v'$ proves $\\|R^G_\\alpha z-y^\\dagger\\|\\le((\\tau_G+S_G)\\delta)^{\\nu/(\\nu+1)}(S_G\\rho)^{1/(\\nu+1)}$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
