        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For each matching basis tangle $T_m$ and each generator $g_i^{\\pm1}$, the product tangle $g_i^{\\pm1}T_m$ has finitely many crossings. In its fixed standard traversal, let $N$ be the crossing count and $b$ the number of crossings whose first branch is under. At a selected bad crossing, set $\\eta=1$ for the fixed $D_+$ chart and $\\eta=-1$ for $D_-$, carrying the smoothing labels along with any rotation of that chart, and apply $$R(D)=R(D^{\\mathrm{sw}})+\\eta z_D\\bigl(R(D_0)-R(D_\\infty)\\bigr).$$ The switched branch has the same $N$ and one fewer bad crossing; each smoothing has crossing count $N-1$. Thus every recursive call decreases $(N,b)$ lexicographically. A descending leaf reduces by the curl and free-circle rules to a standard matching tangle, so the reduction tree is finite and [F5] gives its unique coordinate column. The finite number of basis tangles and generator indices makes every left-multiplication matrix finite. The same crossing-count induction evaluates each closed scalar $P(\\widehat{T_m})$.",
