          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Define $f:R\\to T$ by $q\\mapsto q$, $r\\mapsto a$, $\\Delta\\mapsto d$. Its defining relation maps to zero by [F3], and its unit generators map to units. Conversely define $h:T\\to R$ by $a\\mapsto r$, $d\\mapsto\\Delta$, $q\\mapsto q$, and $z\\mapsto q-q^{-1}$. The relation of $S$ maps to the relation of $R$, and $q-q^{-1}-z$ maps to zero. On each displayed ring generator, both composites are the identity. Thus $f,h$ are inverse ring isomorphisms, without inverting $z$ or requiring a flatness argument.",
