          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $K:X\\to Y$ be compact between real or complex Hilbert spaces over the same scalar field and $\\nu,\\rho>0$. For every $\\delta\\ge0$, $\\varepsilon_K(X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K),\\delta)\\le\\delta^{\\nu/(\\nu+1)}\\rho^{1/(\\nu+1)}$. For every positive singular value $s_j$ with right singular vector $v_j$, equality holds at $\\delta_j=\\rho s_j^{\\nu+1}$, witnessed by $x_j=\\rho s_j^\\nu v_j$. If $K$ has infinite rank, these $\\delta_j$ form a null sequence; if $K$ has finite positive rank, equality is asserted only at its finitely many positive singular values; if $K=0$, the source ball and modulus are $\\{0\\}$ and $0$.",
